xt": "in addition, in winter, the controller 700 controls the operation to operate the heating wire 350 according to the value measured by the temperature sensor 340 to prevent freezing, and the flow rate sensor 600 checks the flow rate of water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102263501-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "water meter freeze protection cover freezing protection cover for water meter the present disclosure relates to a water meter freeze protection cover, and more particularly, to a water meter freeze protection cover for preventing the water meter from freezing due to a decrease in external temperature in winter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102263501-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "embodiments disclosed herein are installed to surround the outer surface of the water meter, to provide a water meter freeze protection cover that can prevent the water meter from freezing even at a low temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102300746-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "this traditional method has a disadvantage in that it is not effective in preventing freezing of the water meter and water pipe due to the problem of thermal insulation when the external temperature is very low below -5"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102300746-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in order to prevent the water stagnant in the water pipe (3) from freezing, when the temperature detected by the temperature sensor (5)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102300746-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "on the other hand, it is possible to prevent the water meter and water pipe from freezing in advance by adjusting the freezing point (freezing point) of water according to the external temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102300746-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as such, in the water pipe freezing prevention system according to the embodiment of the present invention, the opening timing and opening amount of the electromagnetic valve 3 installed in the water pipe 2 are automatically controlled through the controller 10 of the boiler 1 according to the external temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102332096-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "in this way, when the hot air blower is driven (by driving the heater 20 and the fan 30) to generate and blow hot air, the indoor temperature is measured through the temperature sensor 10, and the measured indoor temperature is above the freezing prevention safety temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102344740-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "maintaining the temperature of the purified water flowing into and stored in the purified water tank unit 1100 by the anti-freezing heater unit 1600 at any one temperature selected from the range of 27 to 75 degrees celsius is to promote the activation of the advanced oxidation process (aop)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102346405-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "such a temporary measure has difficulty in preventing freezing of the water meter and water pipe due to the thermal insulation problem when the external temperature is very low below -5 c"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102346405-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as described above, in the system for preventing freezing and freezing of pipes for liquid transport according to another embodiment of the present invention, any one of the antifreeze mixture or water stored in the antifreeze tank 18 or the water tank 21 is selected according to the external ambient temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102440380-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, in the case of a freeze prevention module equipped with such a temperature-type automatic valve, the temperature is measured to prevent freezing through heat transfer, but if the module is exposed to sub-zero weather for a long time, abnormal operation may be executed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102440380-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "this is because when the temperature drops to sub-zero range in winter, rupture due to freezing in valves or pipes may occur"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102466363-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "since the outside air temperature drops below freezing in winter, proper insulation must be accompanied to prevent freezing and bursting of the water meter and the water pipe connected to the water meter, and an open configuration must be taken to allow meter reading of usage even in winter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102466363-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in general, when the outside temperature drops below freezing, such as in winter, the water flowing inside the main body of the water meter freezes and expands, and the expansion force may cause a freeze phenomenon that damages the glass cover of the meter or damages the meter itself"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102467167-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the present invention relates to a water valve for preventing freezing of a water pipe to prevent freezing of a water pipe by discharging water little by little as the stem holder operates and a waterway is partially opened when the temperature is lowered"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102467167-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "however, in the case of a water valve located outdoors, it is difficult to use the water pipe or the tap water inside the water valve due to the freezing temperature in winter, and the volume expansion of the frozen tap water causes the water pipe or the connection parts of the water pipe to deteriorate"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102467167-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "in order to prevent freezing of tap water, conventionally, a method of warming the water valve and the water pipe by wrapping the surroundings of the water valve and the water pipe with a heat insulating material has been most widely used, but the effect is insufficient when the temperature drops significantly"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102498793-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the heating element 40, the temperature sensor 64 installed in the water supply pipe detects the temperature of the water supply pipe, transmits the detected information to the controller box 60, and the controller box analyzes the detected information to determine the prediction of freezing and bursting"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102512635-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the automatic dripping device 100 for freezing prevention according to the present embodiment may open and close the on/off valve 140 by a specific angle according to the temperature data obtained from the temperature detector 120"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102512635-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the power supply unit 170 may provide power stored therein to the temperature detection unit 120, the control unit 130, and the opening/closing valve driving unit when the power supplied from the outside to the automatic dripping device 100 for preventing freezing is cut off"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102563943-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "and further comprising a freeze protection unit installed in the aeration tank connection pipe of the suction unit, the treated water supply pipe of the suction unit, and the washing water supply pipe of the washing unit to prevent the pipes from freezing and bursting, the freeze protection unit, a temperature sensor installed in the aeration tank connection pipe, the treatment water supply pipe of the suction part, and the washing water supply pipe of the washing part to sense the temperature of the pipe or the external temperature around the pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102572857-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "another method for preventing the water pipe from freezing is to prevent the water pipe from freezing by artificially opening a water valve to continuously drain the water when it is expected that the water contained in the water pipe will freeze due to low temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102587945-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "additionally, it is possible to prevent freezing of the air valve 90 in a convenient and effective manner by configuring the heating element 44, solar cell 55, temperature sensor, signal transmitter, and control unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102600404-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "therefore, when the temperature drops, such as in the winter