mperature around the water meter by filling the insulating material in the water meter protection box with the water meter installed or by installing a heat insulating material in the lid installed on the upper surface of the water meter protection box to prevent the freezing point below"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200301700-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the present invention was devised to solve the above problems, and the purpose of the present invention is to prevent the water meter from freezing by heating the bottom of the water meter when the outside temperature decreases"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200302626-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "an anti-freezing-burst type water meter the present invention relates to a water meter, and more particularly, to a freeze-proof water meter to accommodate the air into the water meter to prevent freezing caused by a sudden drop in temperature in winter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200302627-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "an anti-freezing-burst type water meter the present invention relates to a water meter, and more particularly to a freeze-proof water meter having a drain portion for discharging water in accordance with the temperature drop in the lower portion of the water meter to prevent freezing caused by the temperature drop in the winter season"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200302627-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as described above, the present invention includes a drain portion for discharging water at the lower part of the water meter according to the temperature drop, so as to prevent freezing caused by the temperature drop in winter, the freeze is easily prevented according to the change in temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200302638-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, the conventional water-meter protection tube is manufactured by installing a heat insulating material to prevent freezing of water taps and water meters in winter, but in the cold districts where the outside temperature is below 20 c, the protection tube structure applied with such a heat insulating material structure does not show any effect"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200307663-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "to solve the problem of excessive input of metering manpower and metering time due to the use of meter box and freezing of water meter which is easy to occur due to external temperature drop, the function was improved"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200309420-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in order to solve the above problems, a heating freeze protection device has been proposed, which installs a separate heater around the valve and the pipe to prevent freezing by heating the pipe when the ambient temperature drops"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200310432-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "above all, freezing occurs due to a decrease in the external temperature of the water meter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200310444-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the present invention, by simply installing the device around the water pipe and connecting only the power supply, the sensor detects that the temperature drops to sub-zero temperatures and heats the heating sheet to prevent freezing phenomenon that the water pipe freezes or freezes in winter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200312057-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in particular, when the temperature is very low, simply insulating the water meter cannot prevent the freezing of the water meter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200315853-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in this embodiment, the band heaters 80 and 81 are attached to the drain holes 43 and 83 so that the water is automatically heated to prevent freezing when the water is cold below a predetermined temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200321853-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the temperature falls below the freezing point, the built-in electronic temperature control device (2-15) of the pcb board (2-1) detects it and the hot water tank (2- by operating the heater 2-3 and the warm water circulation device 2-21 of 2), the temperature inside the system is increased due to electric heat dissipation, thereby preventing the freezing of the system at the source"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200335080-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, the conventional water meter protection tube is manufactured by installing a heat insulating material to prevent freezing of water taps and water meters in winter, but in the cold districts where the outside air temperature is below 20 c, there is a problem that the protection tube structure using such a heat insulating material does not show any effect"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200362784-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, when the second set temperature is set to the control unit 50 at 8 c and the third set temperature to 12 c, the room 50 is detected from the temperature sensor 40 in the state in which the operation is stopped the operation of the heater 20 and the fan 30 is controlled such that the temperature is between 8 c and 12 c to prevent freezing of water pipes"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200365284-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the heater 16 then raises the temperature in the water tank 10 under the control of the controller 64 to prevent freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200372345-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "if you install the water meter outside the building as described above, there is an advantage that the meter reading staff can easily read, and the privacy is not infringed during the metering process, but it is installed outdoors in the winter season where the freezing is low due to the low outside temperature this will provide a cause for freezing of the water meter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200373667-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, if the water meter is exposed to freezing temperatures below zero in winter, the water inside the water meter expands due to the water freezing inside, and thus freezing occurs in the water meter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200375794-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "conventionally, in order to prevent freezing of the water meter, a case covering the outer shell of the water meter is formed, and a heating line is built in the case, or on one side of the number counter in the water meter for heating while sensing the temperature of water in the water meter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200387639-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "on the other hand, warm geothermal heat is introduced in the winter season, so that the temperature inside the water meter protector can maintain a temperature similar to that of the geothermal temperature, thereby preventing freezing of water meters and the like"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200407276-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the controller 124 determines the water temperature of the cold water tank 101 received from the temperature sensor 128, and controls the operation of the freezing unit to control the operation of the freezing unit 101 water temperature of a level suitable for the user to drink cold water of the cold water tank 101 to fit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200415940-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "such a freeze protection method by the circulation pump 90 is electric compared to the freeze protection method that prevents freezing of the water supply line by applying heat when the water supply line falls below a predetermined temperature by winding the entire water supply line applied to a conventional water supply fountain with a heating wire"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200415940-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, since the temperature sensor 80 and the circulation pump 90 are installed in the water supply line 20 of the present invention, the water supply line 20 can be freely prevented from freezing in winter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200415979-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "fitting projection line the present invention relates to a water meter freeze protection device, and more particularly to a water meter freeze protection device that can maintain a constant temperature at room temperature to prevent freezing of the water meter pipe in winter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200415979-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in particular, since water meters installed in buildings such as apartment complexes are installed in corridors that are not heated, they are easily influenced by temperature and are easily frozen when the temperature drops sharply, thus exposing more of them to the risk of freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200426270-Y1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "the method of claim 1, by measuring the temperature of the water by the temperature sensor 5 in the water pipe (p2), when the temperature is less than the set temperature, the inlet valve 7 and the outlet valve 19 for a predetermined time to prevent freezing by circulation of water secondary water purification equipment"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200426270-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "another object of the present invention is to provide a secondary water purification apparatus designed to prevent freezing by using a temperature sensor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200426270-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and, the flow sensor to prevent the freezing of the filter and the device by opening the inlet valve 7 and outlet valve 19 for a predetermined time when the temperature sensor (5) located in the water pipe (p2) below a set temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200430457-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "meter lid 5.heating wire the conventional technique is to install a heating wire in the shape of caps on the outside of the water meter and to arrange a sensor to heat it when the temperature is below a certain temperature to prevent freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200430463-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "conventional water meter is to be installed in the thermal insulation case to prevent freezing in winter, but there is a limit to the thermal insulation capacity of the thermal insulation case and if water is left inside the meter, it is frozen when the temperature drops, so it cannot be completely prevented"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200430524-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the object of the present invention is to provide a self-heating function to maintain the water meter main body at a certain temperature even in winter to prevent frost condensation or condensation on the outside surface of the water meter main body in winter, in particular, it is to provide a water-coil built-in water meter to prevent winter freezing accidents"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200430528-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "conventional water meter protection box is installed in the water meter inside of the water meter in the water meter to prevent the water meter from freezing in winter, but the water meter is stuck in the water meter when the temperature drops rapidly"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200433469-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "control setting part the present invention relates to a simple abnormality of water, and more specifically, when the ambient temperature drops below 0 c and there is a possibility of freezing of water pipes, a water intake pump that drives water from underground pipes and the like is driven for a predetermined time interval"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200433469-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and a freeze blocker configured to control an operation state of the intake pump according to a preset operating condition for freezing prevention of the water pipe when the outside air temperature is detected below the set temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200468890-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the user can adjust the temperature controller 32 so that the water (w) heating temperature in the steam tank 10 can be arbitrarily set to be heated, whereby the water (w) appropriately according to the freezing state of the freezing pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200487219-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in this water meter 10, tap water is allowed to pass through the water meter, so that when the air temperature falls below freezing in winter, tap water passing through the water meter is frozen, and thus the water meter 10 is frequently frozen"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200498205-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, in the winter, if the permeated water that seeps into the pavement layer of the bridge deck is not drained quickly and remains, it freezes due to the low temperature, causing freezing and rupture of the pavement layer"}, {"pat_id": "US-10246349-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "however, the salinity of salt water/industrial brine 202 that enters freezing desalination cell/unit enclosure 271 via salt water/industrial brine inlet 275 also has influence on the freezing process (the higher the salt concentration, the lower the necessary freezing temperature to be accomplished)"}, {"pat_id": "US-10526548-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in one example, a low temperature fault may be determined and set in response to a low temperature signal from the temperature sensor 176, which may impact the ability to evacuate water due to freezing water"}, {"pat_id": "US-10634284-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "using the latent heat signatures associated with phase changes of a process fluid (in this case sulphur) to identify solidification or melting of the process fluid at locations along a pipeline is not dependent on a particular melting or freezing temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-10634284-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "for example, curves in the pipeline may tend to accumulate more solidified process fluid compared to straight sections of the pipeline, and anchor points along the pipeline may accumulate more solidified process fluid as a result of heat transfer to the anchors supporting the pipeline, which may drop the temperature of the anchor points below the freezing point of the process fluid"}, {"pat_id": "US-10898826-B2", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "if the air temperature sensor 140 is activated, the system 100 will stop operations due to an inability of the air heater with fan 143 to raise the wastewater temperature in the sump (bottom) of the container 139, 339 above the freezing point"}, {"pat_id": "US-10981818-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the higher wattage and overcapacity of the heating element is preferred to ensure that the chamber temperature is maintained because the air pump would bring in cold air in very cold or freezing weather"}, {"pat_id": "US-11047115-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it should be appreciated that if water temperatures are detected as being close to or below freezing, a pressure sensor may look for an increase in pipe pressure that may indicate freezing water in the pipe"}, {"pat_id": "US-11054295-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "elevated temperatures can be an indication of bacteria growth in water networks and temperatures that are too low can lead to freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-11066813-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in some example embodiments, the temperature sensor (115) may be used to prevent pipes from freezing, and the pressure sensor (115) may be used to prevent pipes from bursting"}, {"pat_id": "US-11066813-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in some example embodiments, the system may receive weather data, and if there is prediction of sub-zero temperatures in the forecast, the system may automatically turn on the main valve to allow water to flow through the pipes, thereby preventing the pipe from freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-11066813-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the temperature drops, the system opens the main valve and allows the water to flow, thus preventing the pipe from freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-11095960-B2", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "furthermore, be communicating with a home router, the water meter and leak detection system 10, 126, 200 can communicate with intelligent thermostats sending a signal to turn on the residential or corporation heat to a temperature that will inhibit freezing water in the residential and corporation interior water pipes"}, {"pat_id": "US-11549837-B2", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "furthermore, be communicating with a home router, the water meter and leak detection system 10, 126, 200 can communicate with intelligent thermostats sending a signal to turn on the residential or corporation heat to a temperature that will inhibit freezing water in the residential and corporation interior water pipes"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the primary temperature sensor package 702 and the secondary temperature sensor package 706 may be utilized to raise the temperature of the fluid to prevent the fluid within the fluid conduit system 720 from freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, a temperature or temperature range may be chosen at which the microprocessor 712 will add heat energy to the fluid in the fluid conduit system 720 before the water reaches 32 degrees fahrenheit to prevent it from freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the primary temperature sensor package 806 and the secondary temperature sensor package 840 may be utilized to raise the temperature of the fluid to prevent the fluid within the fluid conduit system 810 from freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the system 1100 is configured for use on a fluid conduit system 1102 located within a structure 1101 to prevent the fluid conduit system 1102 from damage due to freezing fluid upon detection of freezing conditions, such as the temperature of the fluid in the fluid conduit system 1102 and the temperature of the environment surrounding the fluid conduit system 1102"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "by placing the primary heating element 1120 and secondary heating element 1122 at the areas of the fluid conduit system 1102 with the coldest temperatures, the heating element may be turned on to prevent the fluid within the conduit from freezing or defrost already frozen fluid within the fluid conduit"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "based on the temperature and flow of the fluid, the control system 1140 determines whether the fluid in the fluid conduit system 1102 is close to freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the control system 1140 may also turn on the heating elements to heat up the pipes when the external environment temperature or the local environment temperature reaches a predetermined value to prevent the fluid within the conduit from freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, a temperature or temperature range may be chosen for the fluid temperature and the environment temperature at which the control system 1140 will add heat energy to the fluid in the fluid conduit system 1102 before the water reaches 32 degrees fahrenheit to prevent it from freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the control system 1140 may turn on the heating elements 1120 and 1122 to prevent fluid within the fluid conduit system 1102 from freezing when the temperature of the fluid reaches a certain value and if the temperature is at or below a certain value for a predetermined period of time"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the control system 1140 may turn on the heating elements 1120 and 1122 to prevent fluid within the fluid conduit system 1102 from freezing when the temperature reaches a certain value, the temperature is at or below a certain value for a predetermined period of time, and the temperature is at or below a certain value and the wind speed is at a certain value"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "based on the temperature and flow of the fluid, the control system 1230 determines whether the fluid in the fluid conduit system 1102 is close to freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the control system 1230 may also turn on the heating element to heat up the fluid and pipes when the external environment temperature or the local environment temperature reaches a predetermined value to prevent the fluid within the conduit from freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the control system 1230 may turn on the heated recirculation circuit 1220 to prevent fluid within the fluid conduit system 1102 from freezing when the temperature of the fluid reaches a certain value and if the environment temperature is at or below a certain value for a predetermined period of time"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the control system 1230 may turn on the heated recirculation circuit 1220 to prevent fluid within the fluid conduit system 1102 from freezing when the temperature reaches a certain value, the temperature is at or below a certain value for a predetermined period of time, and the temperature is at or below a certain value and the wind speed is at a certain value"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the second threshold temperature tps2 and max time at second threshold temperature tpsmax provides a factor of safety to prevent possible freezing of fluid due to unexpected wind, dips in temperature, or other unaccounted factors that may affect the temperature of the fluid within the fluid conduit system 1102"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the second threshold temperature tss2 and max time at second threshold temperature tssmax provides a factor of safety to prevent possible freezing of fluid due to unexpected wind, dips in temperature, or other unaccounted factors that may affect the temperature of the fluid within the fluid conduit system 1102"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the second threshold temperature tle12 and max time at second threshold temperature tle1max provides a factor of safety to prevent possible freezing of fluid due to unexpected wind, dips in temperature, or other unaccounted factors that may affect the temperature of the fluid within the fluid conduit system 1102"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the second threshold temperature tle22 and max time at second threshold temperature tle2max provides a factor of safety to prevent possible freezing of fluid due to unexpected wind, dips in temperature, or other unaccounted factors that may affect the temperature of the fluid within the fluid conduit system 1102"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the second threshold temperature tet2 and max time at second threshold temperature tetmax provides a factor of safety to prevent possible freezing of fluid due to unexpected wind, dips in temperature, or other unaccounted factors that may affect the temperature of the fluid within the fluid conduit system 1102"}, {"pat_id": "US-11976446-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in climates where freezing temperatures occur, the problem of frozen spigots is well known, which may result in interrupted water supply from frozen spigots, rupturing of spigots and connected supply pipes, and a substantial potential for flooding and flood damage"}, {"pat_id": "US-11976446-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "empirical testing has determined that modest power, on the order of five watts, will produce a temperature differential of thirty degrees fahrenheit, or more, in the spigot body, which is sufficient to prevent freezing at temperatures of zero degrees fahrenheit, or less"}, {"pat_id": "US-11998860-B2", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "if the air temperature sensor 140 is activated, the system 100 will stop operations due to an inability of the air heater with fan 143 to raise the produced water or wastewater temperature in the sump (bottom) of the container 139, 339 above the freezing point"}, {"pat_id": "US-12231085-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the moisture collection layer 40 may additionally and/or alternatively prevent the energy dissipating receiver 20 from cracking and/or freezing, such as during circumstances when there are large temperature changes"}, {"pat_id": "US-12337259-B2", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "if the air temperature sensor 140 is activated, the system 100 will stop operations due to an inability of the air heater with fan 143 to raise the wastewater temperature in the sump (bottom) of the container 139, 339 above the freezing point"}, {"pat_id": "US-4018682-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in a practical sense, sludge from a retention pond is treated by the method of the present invention during the winter months of the year when the ambient temperature is below freezing at least part of the time, thereby foregoing the need to artificially freeze the water"}, {"pat_id": "US-4236382-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in any of the vacuum freezing processes described, an aqueous solution is introduced into a chamber which is maintained at a pressure that is somewhat lower than the vapor pressure of the solution at the freezing temperature of the solution to thereby simultaneously flash vaporize water and form ice crystals"}, {"pat_id": "US-4243522-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and 6 p.m., it is possible to use the waste water as a source of heat for a heat pump, the temperature of the waste water being sufficiently high that it can be reduced, such as by 5 c., without a risk of freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-4313452-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the lower end of the exterior thaw tube 32 thus thaws quickly and also freezes quickly, which provides a fast refreezing of the apparatus and reopening of the drain opening 30 should the ambient temperature, after only a short period of thaw, again go below freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-4456024-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "ambient temperatures below freezing but of insufficient duration to reduce the water temperature to the freezing point, will not activate the valve resulting in an unnecessary discharge of water"}, {"pat_id": "US-4657038-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "furthermore, each of those devices are actuated in response to ambient air temperature and thus will serve to trickle water when the air temperature is near the freezing temperature of water, even though the temperature of the water in the conduit may be at a higher temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-4657038-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "since the actuation of the unit depends upon the water temperature within the conduit, the unit will only operate to trickle water when there exists a real danger that freezing may occur, thus minimizing water waste"}, {"pat_id": "US-4672990-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "despite colder above-ground ambient temperatures, radiant heat from main water supply line 2 should prevent freezing of main branch line 3 and main valve 4"}, {"pat_id": "US-4763682-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the valve closing element of this patent is caused to open said valve and allow the drainage of fluid from a connected pipe in response to temperatures approaching the freezing point"}, {"pat_id": "US-4763682-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is thus seen that it would be desirable to have a simple, inexpensive system for draining water lines at the approach of freezing temperatures, and in which the activating mechanism is maintained out of contact with the fluid both during and after its activation"}, {"pat_id": "US-4763682-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is therefore seen that the present invention provides a simple device for activating a fluid valve in response to a thermal, and specifically, to a freezing, change in temperature, without the requirement for external power or human intervention"}, {"pat_id": "US-4784173-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "after the valve has been opened to bleed water from the water line, it thereafter closes because of such heat transfer and is again in position to operate responsively to freezing ambient temperatures"}, {"pat_id": "US-4784173-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when freezing temperatures are sensed by the bulb, there is an outflow of water from the valve device and an inflow of water from the inlet conduit, thereby preventing freezing of water within the tank"}, {"pat_id": "US-4784173-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, there is a need for a completely failure-safe freeze prevention valve that is useful under industrial conditions, automatically responsive to freezing temperatures and to thawing temperatures, completely reliable as a standby device, entirely independent of outside power sources, incapable of leaking, and operable without periodic maintenance"}, {"pat_id": "US-4798239-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the two anti-freezing valves 15 and 16 effectively protect the meter against freezing by virtue of the transfer of heat from soil zones where the collectors 10 are buried, to the valves 15 and 16 flanking the meter, thereby preventing the freezing of the water circulating from the valve 15 to the valve 16, even in the case of a substantially negative temperature of the adjacent atmosphere"}, {"pat_id": "US-4838039-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "direct contact heat transfer requires less temperature difference between the vaporizing refrigerant and freezing solution than does indirect heat transfer systems to achieve the same energy transfer due to the elimination of the heat exchanger surface"}, {"pat_id": "US-4936114-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "sufficient aqueous ice slurry is fed to mixing tank 22 by conduit 54 to keep the temperature of the liquid therein close to, but above, the freezing point so that there is no increase in ice particle formation"}, {"pat_id": "US-5059228-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "referring to the processing of an aqueous solution by any vacuum freezing process, the aqueous solution is introduced into a chamber which is maintained at a pressure that is somewhat lower than the vapor pressure of the solution at the freezing temperature of the solution to thereby simultaneously flash vaporize water and form ice crystals"}, {"pat_id": "US-5075010-A", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "lower temperatures may produce freezing and clogging of the vessels, while higher temperatures may cause vaporization of the water, both unwanted for efficient operation"}, {"pat_id": "US-5080704-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "referring to the processing of an aqueous solution by any vacuum freezing process, the aqueous solution is introduced into a chamber which is maintained at a pressure that is somewhat lower than the vapor pressure of the solution at the freezing temperature of the solution to thereby simultaneously flash vaporize water and form ice crystals"}, {"pat_id": "US-5126048-A", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "lower temperatures may produce freezing and clogging of the vessels, while higher temperatures may cause vaporization of the water, both unwanted for efficient operation"}, {"pat_id": "US-5448892-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "vacuum freezing processes referring to the processing of an aqueous solution by any vacuum freezing process, the aqueous solution is introduced into a chamber which is maintained at a pressure that is somewhat lower than the vapor pressure of the solution at the freezing temperature of the solution to thereby simultaneously flash vaporize water and form ice crystals"}, {"pat_id": "US-5553637-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the second chamber 31 has a primary inlet 34 connected at 35 to the outlet 11 via the supply line section 13a subjected to freezing temperature, i.e., aboveground"}, {"pat_id": "US-5715855-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "field of the invention the present invention relates to anti-freezing devices, and in particular to temperature-activated assemblies that prevent freezing and rupture of outdoor water-supply conduits"}, {"pat_id": "US-5715855-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the temperature of household water, continuously flowing through to the outdoor valves, is usually sufficient to prevent freezing of the valve and associated plumbing"}, {"pat_id": "US-5715855-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "description of the invention brief summary of the invention the present invention provides a simple design for a mechanically actuated, temperature-responsive valve that efficiently utilizes the volumetric expansion of freezing water to cause water from an outdoor tap to flow through discharge ports"}, {"pat_id": "US-5816288-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "temperature variations, especially low temperatures below freezing, can cause the screens to frost over and become damaged thus allowing an entrance to the storage tank for insects and other undesired elements"}, {"pat_id": "US-5876596-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "after valve 44 has been open for a sufficiently long interval to permit the essentially deuterium free water from separator 28 to flow into tank 50, timer 62 or microprocessor 18 activates cooling element 56 to reduce the temperature of the water sample to the freezing point (32 f.)"}, {"pat_id": "US-6003780-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "water residing within the standpipe is exposed to freezing temperatures and thus may freeze therein to obstruct water flow and fountain usage, while additionally posing a significant risk of pipe breakage"}, {"pat_id": "US-6003780-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "interruption of water supply pressure, when the main fountain valve 20 is in the off condition, does not result in exposing any portion of the collected water to freezing temperatures"}, {"pat_id": "US-6021798-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a number of devices have been proposed over the years for preventing water pipes of buildings from freezing in cold weather by automatically causing water to drain or trickle therefrom in response to a drop in temperature below the freezing point"}, {"pat_id": "US-6021798-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the temperature rises above freezing, the sensor is de-actuated to interrupt the flow of electricity from the power source to the solenoid-actuated valve, and thereby close the valve and stop the flow of water therethrough"}, {"pat_id": "US-6152707-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "likewise, a heater 34 may be included inside storage tank 12, to prevent the water stored in tank 12 from freezing in low temperatures"}, {"pat_id": "US-6152707-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a heater may be activated at low water temperatures to prevent the water inside tank 112 from freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-6182453-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "including the peltier probe itself can be activated in reverse, to provide a sufficient amount of heating to prevent freezing of the lines, valves, and reservoir when the ambient or housing panel temperature falls into the range 5 to 5 c"}, {"pat_id": "US-6237620-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "which may require removal of a structural component of the mobile home, boat/yacht, cottage, or lodge, in order to provide access to the freeze damaged length of pipe or the particular fitting adversely affected by the freezing temperature in the winter months"}, {"pat_id": "US-6436299-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the ambient temperature sensor circuit measures the ambient temperature of the atmosphere, so that the water treatment system can maintain a temperature level above freezing or some other predetermined temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-6436299-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the ambient temperature sensor circuit 114 measures the ambient temperature of the atmosphere so that the water treatment system 10 can maintain a temperature level above freezing or some other predetermined temperature setting"}, {"pat_id": "US-6763845-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus a subject water utilizing device (e.g., an evaporative cooler and its associated piping system) and certain freezing temperature exposed-portions of applicant s device are drained and thus winterized"}, {"pat_id": "US-6763845-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "indeed, in some particularly preferred embodiments of this invention, the third valve may be attached to a water utilization device that is located out of doors and therefore exposed to freezing temperatures"}, {"pat_id": "US-7089955-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "when the outside temperature drops below freezing, the water system must be drained to prevent damage to the pipes, tanks, water fixture(s) and other plumbing components"}, {"pat_id": "US-7497228-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "because the temperature control valve measured a higher temperature, it would remain closed and not allow warmer water from below ground to replace the freezing water"}, {"pat_id": "US-7510656-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "submerged combustion heaters, or other heat sources, may be used to raise water temperature as desired, such as in the winter to prevent water freezing if the aerator 106 is an outdoor pond"}, {"pat_id": "US-7527736-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "submerged combustion heaters, or other heat sources, may be used to raise water temperature as desired, such as in the winter to prevent water freezing if the aerator 106 is an outdoor pond"}, {"pat_id": "US-8105488-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "submerged combustion heaters, or other heat sources, may be used to raise water temperature as desired, such as in the winter to prevent water freezing if the aerator 106 is an outdoor pond"}, {"pat_id": "US-8117998-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is possible to prevent pipelines from freezing and bursting at temperatures below zero during the winter, using the configuration of the hot water supplying system 20"}, {"pat_id": "US-8141584-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in colder environments, existing exterior collection and storage tanks may crack or break when the temperature drops below freezing, and the water in the tank turns to ice"}, {"pat_id": "US-8141584-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the temperature of the water in the storage tank falls below a specified temperature for a specified period of time, thereby indicating that the possibility of freezing exists, the microprocessor activates the pump to dump water from the storage tank through the alternate outlet to the alternate destination"}, {"pat_id": "US-9238904-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the temperature sensing device detects the temperature of the fluid within the flushing device 100, measuring for freezing conditions, and triggers the freeze control valve 710 to open under predetermined temperatures, such as freezing condition temperatures, to prevent freezing of the fluid within the flushing device 100"}, {"pat_id": "US-9482357-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in doing so, pressure relief in the system at a temperature above the freezing point of water, generates fluid flow from the well and/or pressure tank or other source, thereby preventing freeze-up"}, {"pat_id": "US-9482357-B2", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "above the freezing point of water, will open and allow relatively warmer water from the tank 304 to enter the trough to prevent ice buildup when the air temperature is cool"}, {"pat_id": "US-9567250-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the preheating coils may contain antifreeze which can be circulated to prevent freezing of the preheat tank when not in use or to maintain the temperature of the preheat tank"}, {"pat_id": "US-9567250-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the antifreeze filled coils may continue to flow to prevent freezing of the preheat tank when not in use or to maintain the temperature of the preheat tank"}]</data>
