ons greatly reduces the likelihood of precipitation of inorganic materials, and maintains the supercritical temperature from the inlet of the reactor to increase organic decomposition effects"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100806134-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is composed of a double wall having a minimum temperature difference between the ground and the valve chamber structure 10 to prevent condensation inside the valve chamber structure 10 to prevent corrosion of the valve facility 110 disposed in the valve chamber structure 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101247110-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "pressure and temperature generated when the micro bubbles are destroyed can cause a corrosion state in the reaction chamber 41, so the reaction chamber 41 is connected to both ends by a flange 44, so that the structure can be replaced immediately in case of serious damage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101541469-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "further, the sandwich panel used in the buried flow meter chamber according to the present invention can prevent the condensation phenomenon caused by the temperature difference from the outside, thereby preventing the corrosion of the mechanical structure installed in the buried flowmeter chamber have"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101762614-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "these ducts are subject to cracking due to contraction and expansion due to external environment such as corrosion, external shock, temperature, etc., resulting in problems such as leakage of the fluid flowing in the pipeline to the outside or severance of pipeline do"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101804811-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in addition, since the sandwich panel 90 used in the temporary end water service valve chamber 1 according to the present invention can prevent condensation caused by a difference in temperature from the outside, corrosion of the mechanical structure can be prevented"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101804812-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in addition, since the sandwich panel 90 used in the temporary end water service valve chamber 1 according to the present invention can prevent condensation caused by a difference in temperature from the outside, corrosion of the mechanical structure can be prevented"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101910492-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "these ducts are subject to cracking due to contraction and expansion due to external environment such as corrosion, external shock, temperature, etc., resulting in problems such as leakage of the fluid flowing in the pipeline to the outside or severance of pipeline do"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102036529-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "that is, such a water tank is contaminated with water quality because the temperature of the stored water is increased due to the high external temperature of the summer, and the water quality is contaminated, and the contaminated water is not suitable for extinguishing, corrosion (mic"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102085280-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "a temperature control device installed in the liquid corrosion tank to reduce an elevated liquid temperature of the liquid corrosion solution in the aerobic liquid corrosion tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102085280-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "on the contrary, in the case where the mlss concentration is increased, the wastewater temperature in the tank is maintained at about 30 to 40 c during the biological treatment in the liquid corrosion tank, which is caused by the difference between the external temperature and the air supplied into the tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102085280-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "figure 3 is a schematic diagram showing a scattering prevention device in the temperature control device applied to the liquid corrosion tank of the high concentration organic sewage treatment system according to an embodiment of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102196538-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "meanwhile, when the chamber 10 is buried in the ground, condensation is generated in the wall plate 12 due to a temperature difference between the pipe and the underground, and such condensation occurs along the wall plate 12 of the chamber 10 and the bottom plate 13 it becomes a factor of failure due to corrosion of various valves and measuring instruments"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200358103-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the flexible conduit tube is wavy, so it is very easy to draw wires and is not subject to temperature changes, so there is no need for relaxation measures, and it is easy to prevent acid and corrosion resistance and has almost no condensation"}, {"pat_id": "US-10005001-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a corrosion resistant material is preferred because the sump is exposed to high temperatures, moisture, and corrosive source water"}, {"pat_id": "US-10722824-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in second (sensor) compartment 23 to determine the temperature at the ph and corrosion sensors and permit correction of their readings"}, {"pat_id": "US-10722824-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in the second compartment, a corrosion monitor, ph meter, and temperature sensor were installed for continuous monitoring"}, {"pat_id": "US-10759676-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a corrosion resistant material is preferred because the sump is exposed to high temperatures, moisture, and corrosive source water"}, {"pat_id": "US-11002699-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a corrosion resistant material is preferred because the sump is exposed to high temperatures, moisture, and corrosive source water"}, {"pat_id": "US-11826681-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a corrosion resistant material is preferred because the sump is exposed to high temperatures, moisture, and corrosive source water"}, {"pat_id": "US-11884555-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a corrosion resistant material is preferred because the sump is exposed to high temperatures, moisture, and corrosive source water"}, {"pat_id": "US-12163944-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "temperature sensors t