  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "EP-1218293-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "also, the air-cooler 25 will ensure that incoming raw water cannot be heated within the heat exchanger 18 to a temperature which would induce premature precipitation of dissolved solids in the incoming raw water, and thus lead to ultimate blockage inside the heat exchanger"}, {"pat_id": "EP-1228003-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "also, the air-cooler 25 will ensure that incoming raw water cannot be heated within the heat exchanger 18 to a temperature which would induce premature precipitation of dissolved solids in the incoming raw water, and thus lead to ultimate blockage inside the heat exchanger"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100339649-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "to block the cold air and temperature of the outside to maintain the heat retention it is to prevent the malfunction or breakage of the instrument of the water meter 7 installed in (1)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100432779-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "by blocking the external cold air double triple to maintain the underground temperature inside the protective casing (1) to prevent the rapid descent to below zero to prevent freezing of the water meter (2)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100432780-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it relates to a water meter protection tank to increase the temperature blocking force to prevent freezing of water meters and water pipes"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100439863-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, in the conventional washing machine generating apparatus 200 of the washing machine, the washing rate is lowered in the winter when low-temperature tap water is supplied, while a part of the electrolyte that is not dissolved is collected around the drain hole 101 to block drainage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100479757-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "the method of claim 1, the heat transfer unit 150 checks the temperature of the washing water at all times and the washing water temperature monitoring sensor 152 to block the operation of the heater when the temperature of the washing water is above a predetermined predetermined temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100479757-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "the heat transfer unit 150 checks the temperature of the washing water at all times and the washing water temperature monitoring sensor 152 to block the operation of the heater when the temperature of the washing water is above a predetermined predetermined temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100768274-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is to provide a water tank using unit hollow plate material that blocks air flow to prevent condensation caused by temperature difference between indoor and outdoor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100886893-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "such a water metering box protective casing cap is installed in a protective casing because it cannot block the ground temperature during the cold winter season"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100901209-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "on the other hand, the water supply control device 250 by checking the pressure in the water supply pipe 230 through the pressure sensor unit 260, it is possible to prevent the water from flowing into the water supply pipe 230 is frozen or blocked due to low temperature, the pipe is broken"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100970425-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at this time, the operation of the boiler 341 is stopped and the high temperature steam obtained by the operation of the heat pump 340 is blocked by blocking the inflow of water vapor through the boiler 341 to prevent the backflow of the boiler 341"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101050727-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the outer mixing part 2 formed as described above slides in contact with the inner diameter or one side and blocks and opens the cold water inlet 5, the hot water inlet 7, and the normal temperature inlet 6 while passing through the water purifier"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101255667-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, during the summer when the air temperature is high, the light blocking pad 51 is closed to prevent the internal temperature of the reaction tank 10 and the temperature of the sewage or waste water from being excessively high to block sunlight from penetrating into the internal space of the housing 30"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101289929-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as another example, the controller 14 may receive the temperature of the water in the water pipe detected by the temperature detection sensor unit 11, and block the valve 13 when the temperature of the water in the water pipe rises above a predetermined temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101368425-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at this time, the first cover 20 and the second cover 30 is provided to cover the opening of the water tank 10 to prevent the inflow of foreign matter and infiltration of bacteria in the air, the first cover 20 the space between the second cover 30 serves as a thermal insulation space to block the influence of the external temperature of the water tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101368425-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as such, the first cover 200 covers the opening of the water tank 100 to prevent the inflow of foreign substances and the penetration of bacteria in the air, and the space between the first cover 200 and the second cover 300 is it functions as an insulated space to block the influence of the outside temperature of the water tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101373842-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, by measuring the temperature change of the hot water inside the hot water tank through the temperature sensor, if the temperature change of the hot water over time is greater than the reference value by stopping the operation of the heating unit, heating in the absence of hot water in the hot water tank the negative operation can be blocked to prevent defective or malfunction of the heating unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101583008-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "1, the bimetal 23 or 23 the heater power is directly applied to the steam generating part 20 and the power is not applied to the bimetal 23 or 23 so that the bimetal 23 or 23 can not function as a temperature sensor, accordingly, the bimetal 23 or 23 can not block the input of the heater power when the steam generating part 20 overheats, and thus the steam thawing device can not be operated safely"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102106221-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the heat insulating material 20 is seated and inserted on the upper side of the inner water meter 1 of the protective tube 10 to block the cold outside and maintain the temperature to prevent freezing of the water meter 1"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200325952-Y1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "the method of claim 1, the heat transfer unit 150 checks the temperature of the washing water at all times and the washing water temperature monitoring sensor 152 to block the operation of the heater when the temperature of the washing water is above a predetermined predetermined temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200325952-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the heat transfer unit 150 checks the temperature of the washing water at all times and the washing water temperature monitoring sensor 152 to block the operation of the heater when the temperature of the washing water is above a predetermined predetermined temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200383900-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and a cpu that controls a current controller to block a current flowing through the electrode plate when the temperature of the inflow water detected by the temperature sensor is equal to or greater than a predetermined reference temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-10046988-B2", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "a blocking valve is advantageously inserted at the filtrate outlet of the filter which stops the permeate flow to the place of use in the event of deviation from predetermined trend data or in the event of defective process data, such as defective conductivity and/or temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-10948131-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "moreover, in some embodiments, the control sub-system 50 may determine fluid temperature within the tubing annulus 25 of the pipe segment 20 based on sensor data determined by a fluid temperature annulus sensor 54 (process block 118)"}, {"pat_id": "US-10989621-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in other words, in such embodiments, fluidly connecting an upstream sensor 58a to a vent port 42 on a pipe fitting 18 may include fluidly connecting a fluid temperature sensor 58 between the vent port 42 and a fluid valve 60 in the testing apparatus 40, for example, via one or more external fluid conduits 62, such as a hose (process block 98)"}, {"pat_id": "US-10989621-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "additionally or alternatively, determining the one or more fluid parameters associated with the fluid in the tubing annulus 25 of the pipe segment 20 may include determining fluid temperature present within the tubing annulus 25, for example, via an upstream fluid temperature sensor 58a (process block 120)"}, {"pat_id": "US-11112190-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "(or a different temperature for a different application), the expansion of the pcm bag 428 and the right and left pet blocks 414a, 414b is not sufficient to cause the graphene sheet 408 to become in contact with the pipeline 402"}, {"pat_id": "US-11112190-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "at block 1806, the method includes affecting the temperature of the transported fluid in the pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "US-11112190-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the inhibiting of heat transfer (block 1802) from the pipeline to the environment (e.g., when the external temperature is below a threshold) may maintain the temperature of the fluid in the pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "US-11112190-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the promoting of heat transfer (block 1804) from the environment to the pipeline (e.g., when the external temperature is above a threshold) may increase the temperature of the fluid in the pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "US-11193847-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, in such embodiments, based on the sensor data determined by the temperature sensors 52, the control sub-system 54 may determine fluid temperature at multiple different locations along the bore in the pipeline system 10 (process block 106)"}, {"pat_id": "US-11199502-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is very easy to produce the natural gas hydrate in the oil and gas exploitation and transportation process especially in low-temperature and high-pressure deep water environments, and the natural gas hydrate will block a conveying pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "otherwise the controller 6034 may receive a sump temperature value and a low pressure vapor temperature value in block 7274"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "if, in block 7348, the difference for each is greater than a threshold set for each respective parameter, the controller 6034 calculates a derivative based on data received from at least one temperature sensor in the system 6000 in block 7351"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "for example, the controller 6034 may calculate a derivative based on data received from a low pressure steam temperature sensor 6066 in block 7351"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "otherwise, the controller 6034 may, in block 7392, receive temperature data signals from one or more product temperature sensor (e.g"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "if, at block 7069, the system 6000 is currently in a normal water production mode, the target temperature 7068 along with a product or condensate output temperature 7070 determined from data provided by a product output sensor (e.g"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "a current low pressure steam temperature may be received by the controller 6034 in block 6884 from, for example, a low pressure steam temperature sensor 6066 (see, e.g., fig"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "as shown, in block 6592 a controller may determine a difference between a desired temperature and the source inlet temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "in block 7528, the controller 6034 may receive data from each of the product temperature sensors (e.g"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "in block 7832, the controller 6034 may find a derivate of the product level based on data received from the product temperature sensor(s) 6082a-d"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "in some embodiments, the individual derivatives determined from each product temperature sensor 6082a-d may all be required to be less than the threshold in order for the controller 6034 to proceed to block 7840"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "in some embodiments, if any of the individual derivatives determined from each product temperature sensor 6082a-d are less than the threshold, the controller 6034 may proceed to block 7844"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "a blowdown temperature control loop may be initialized and an extra source valve command cap may be determined in block 8018 as well"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "if, in block 8016, the system 6000 is not in a production start-up state, in block 8020 the target temperature for the blowdown process stream exiting the blowdown heat exchanger 6008b may be set to the desired temperature determined in block 8014"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "otherwise the controller 6034 may receive a sump temperature value and a low pressure vapor temperature value in block 7274"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "if, in block 7348, the difference for each is greater than a threshold set for each respective parameter, the controller 6034 calculates a derivative based on data received from at least one temperature sensor in the system 6000 in block 7351"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "for example, the controller 6034 may calculate a derivative based on data received from a low pressure steam temperature sensor 6066 in block 7351"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "otherwise, the controller 6034 may, in block 7392, receive temperature data signals from one or more product temperature sensor (e.g"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "if, at block 7069, the system 6000 is currently in a normal water production mode, the target temperature 7068 along with a product or condensate output temperature 7070 determined from data provided by a product output sensor (e.g"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "a current low pressure steam temperature may be received by the controller 6034 in block 6884 from, for example, a low pressure steam temperature sensor 6066 (see, e.g., fig"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "as shown, in block 6592 a controller may determine a difference between a desired temperature and the source inlet temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "in block 7528, the controller 6034 may receive data from each of the product temperature sensors (e.g"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "in block 7832, the controller 6034 may find a derivate of the product level based on data received from the product temperature sensor(s) 6082a-d"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "in some embodiments, the individual derivatives determined from each product temperature sensor 6082a-d may all be required to be less than the threshold in order for the controller 6034 to proceed to block 7840"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "in some embodiments, if any of the individual derivatives determined from each product temperature sensor 6082a-d are less than the threshold, the controller 6034 may proceed to block 7844"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "a blowdown temperature control loop may be initialized and an extra source valve command cap may be determined in block 8018 as well"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "if, in block 8016, the system 6000 is not in a production start-up state, in block 8020 the target temperature for the blowdown process stream exiting the blowdown heat exchanger 6008b may be set to the desired temperature determined in block 8014"}, {"pat_id": "US-11559765-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "at block 720, the controller 180 may determine a dew point of the chamber 28 and an optimal post-evaporator air temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-11623178-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "at block 720, the controller 180 may determine a dew point of the chamber 28 and an optimal post-evaporator air temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-11738314-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at block 1310, the high-temperature, high-pressure liquid is received into a vessel having one or more walls that define a hollow interior cavity partially filled with water, with an air pocket within the cavity"}, {"pat_id": "US-3978709-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "description of the invention this invention relates to a method and a system for detecting a leakage from a liquid-transporting pipeline, and more particularly to a method and a system for minimizing a pressure change due to a temperature change of a liquid within a blocked pipeline containing the liquid to be transported, and detecting a leakage of the liquid from the blocked pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "US-3978709-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, it is necessary to make the block distance shorter than a specified length, e.g., said 10 km, or to wait for the leakage detection until the temperature of the pipeline has reached the ambient one, for reducing the effect of the temperature change"}, {"pat_id": "US-4808290-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "if pool water stops flowing through metal conduit 46 while electrical power continues to be supplied to field wiring block 366, then after approximately five minutes, the temperature of metal bar 384 and thermostatic switch 386 rises above the aforementioned predetermined temperature, and themostatic switch 386 opens"}, {"pat_id": "US-5776333-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "also, the air-cooler 25 will ensure that incoming raw water cannot be heated within the heat exchanger 18 to a temperature which would induce premature precipitation of dissolved solids in the incoming raw water, and thus lead to ultimate blockage inside the heat exchanger 18"}, {"pat_id": "US-5858248-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "also, the air-cooler 25 will ensure that incoming raw water cannot be heated within the heat exchanger 18 to a temperature which would induce premature precipitation of dissolved solids in the incoming raw water, and thus lead to ultimate blockage inside the heat exchanger"}, {"pat_id": "US-7723700-B2", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "via the ion source block, the surfaces of conduit 150 are thus preferably maintained at temperature greater than the set-point of pid 3"}, {"pat_id": "US-9370746-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, when a pressure pump that delivers supply water to the ro membrane module is operated at a constant operating pressure, a water volume of produced permeate water (pure water) becomes mailer than a required production volume of water, when a temperature of supply water is low or when a membrane is blocked"}, {"pat_id": "US-9810377-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "it is noted that changes of the temperature of a compressible gas in the modified inlet block 444 may cause the gas to expand or contract, and thereby result in unwanted variances in the flow rate"}, {"pat_id": "US-9810377-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "to avoid such unwanted fluctuations in temperature, the increased surface area, or contact area of the chambers 447 provides a heat exchanger interface between the fluid and the material that forms the modified inlet block 444 and thereby minimize changes in fluid temperature as the fluid moves along the surface of the modified inlet block 444"}, {"pat_id": "US-9810377-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "this heat exchanger interface will help in keeping the temperature of the fluid in the modified inlet block 444 constant during the pressure decay, thereby improving the accuracy of the rate-of-decay measurement by avoiding fluctuations in the rate that may have otherwise been cause by fluctuations in the temperature of the modified inlet block 444"}]</data>
</edge>
