  <data key="d5">["earthquake", "seawater", "steel", "outlet", "stress", "embodiment", "room", "decrease", "volume", "separation", "discharge", "gap", "end", "variation", "meter", "expansion", "position", "component", "body", "air", "valve", "rise", "excess", "leakage", "channel", "wedge", "cylinder", "length", "joint", "temperature", "distance", "gravity", "vessel", "pipe", "deterioration", "conductivity", "skeleton", "coupling", "water", "chamber", "location", "sensor", "reactor", "drainage", "grating", "gate", "problem", "recirculation", "transfer", "waterproofness", "interval", "point", "stretch", "part", "cover", "flow", "loop", "fermentation", "device", "base", "addition", "change", "connection", "pressure", "unit", "tank", "need", "heat", "panel", "leak", "difference", "crack", "bragg", "coolant", "area", "example", "surface", "waste", "core", "deformation", "invention", "degree", "advantage", "oxidation", "cracking", "strain", "composition", "piping", "structure", "word"]</data>
  <data key="d6">["rise", "instal", "mention", "bear", "absorb", "deform", "achieve", "make", "be", "result", "protect", "cover", "integrate", "loop", "exhibit", "perform", "damage", "create", "provide", "affect", "say", "measure", "becomes", "bend", "weave", "secure", "locate", "solve", "cause", "use", "operate", "occur", "claim", "peel", "embed", "constitute", "introduce", "dry", "adopt", "space", "connect", "assemble", "confirm", "fix", "support", "comprise", "minimize", "reach", "accord", "cool", "supply", "compute", "fit"]</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "EP-3706066-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "in another embodiment, not covered by the claimed invention, moreover the pressure sensor comprises another bragg grating, installed on a part of said sensor not deforming after pressure, such for example a cylindrical body, so that it is subject only to deformation due to temperature"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3706066-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "preferably, in addition the pressure sensor comprises another bragg grating, installed on a part of said sensor not deforming after liquid flow, so that it is subject only to deformation due to temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100315762-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the present invention, the composite panel 10 can be firmly assembled by fitting the composite panel 10 to the skeleton constituting each component panel of the large tank, so that the connection part of the composite panel 10 is caused by internal deformation pressure due to bending deformation or temperature change"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100988365-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the concrete tank exhibits deformation due to temperature deterioration, the cracks may occur in the panel adhesive composition of the concrete tank, resulting in a decrease in waterproofness and separation of the panel and the adhesive composition"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101044701-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, there is an urgent need to introduce a structure that can effectively absorb such heat deformation to protect the gravity wet oxidation reactor.the present invention created to solve the above problems is to protect the gravity wet oxidation reactor by effectively absorbing the heat deformation according to the temperature inside the gravity pressure vessel"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101044701-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in other words, if the heat deformation occurs due to the temperature rise of the coolant chamber 100, the lower surface of the coolant chamber 100 is fixed to the bottom surface of the core (99) so that the upper end of the coolant chamber 100 rises due to thermal deformation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101044701-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, when the upper end of the external pipe 200 rises due to heat deformation due to the temperature rise of the cooling water chamber 100 or the external pipe 200, the internal pipe 300 also rises together, and the internal pipe 300 of the the distance between the lower surface and the lower surface of the outer pipe 200 is farther away, thereby further securing an area (length) capable of absorbing heat deformation of the inner pipe 300"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101967405-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "therefore, if a point sensor is used to measure the temperature and strain in the water pipe, it is not possible to confirm the position of the sensor even if leakage or deformation occurs in the interval between the sensors"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102031231-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "15, 2002)the present invention provides a drainage outlet with an inner cylinder and an outer cylinder to minimize heat transfer of the hot temperature of the waste, and the inner cylinder is spaced from the outer cylinder so that the heat transfer of the outer cylinder is not performed, so that the gap due to thermal deformation of the outer cylinder is achieved"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102093874-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "however, the coupling by bearing is possible in a fermentation device operated at room temperature and normal pressure, but there is room for problems such as leakage and deformation due to thermal expansion in a drying device supplied with high-temperature and high-pressure dry air"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102101131-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "due to this stress, the inner circumferential surface of the water pipe becomes seriously damaged such as peeling, peeling or cracking, and the expansion joint, which is a stretch joint, is damaged due to elastic deformation due to a temperature difference, and leaks are caused by this"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "this structure adopts the advantages of a wedge gate valve (413) and a parallel gate valve (416), and is relatively less affected by deformation due to temperature and pressure"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200330013-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "concrete channel for seawater discharge is made by embedding and connecting precast concrete channel, and expansion joint device is provided at the connection part so that it can support some degree of external deformation such as heat deformation or earthquake due to temperature difference"}, {"pat_id": "US-11035484-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as mentioned above the respective flow meters are integrated in the base unit and thus still relatively close to the handheld unit so as to minimize variations of computed water volume if the flow meter were located at a more distant location in the recirculation loop due to piping deformation because of water temperature changes and/or loop internal pressure variations"}, {"pat_id": "US-11318396-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "due to the thermal conductivity of the exterior cover, both the interior woven or non-woven panel and the interior surfaces of the pressure vessel are theoretically capable of reaching temperatures in excess of the deformation temperature of 304 stainless steel"}]</data>
</edge>
