rganism collection and dormancy process (s90), the filtered microorganisms are collected and stored in a low-temperature container (preferably below 15 c.) to prevent contamination, and then put into a dormant tank at a predetermined speed, for example, 2m/sec, for dormant treatment"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102707115-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the present invention provides an automatic chlorine injection device for preventing contamination of tap water in a public building water tank, which stores a large amount of chlorine in an automatic chlorine injection device and enables timely injection and replenishment, and also prevents deterioration of chlorine solution due to changes in ambient temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200430484-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is introduced by itself while maintaining the same water quality and the same water temperature at the time of intake, and at the same time prevents the contamination of the groundwater system, and simultaneously withdraws and pumps the water automatically"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200430484-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is introduced by itself while maintaining the same water quality and the same water temperature at the time of intake, and at the same time prevents the contamination of the groundwater system, and at the same time automatically takes in and pumps the water"}, {"pat_id": "US-8388833-B2", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "for the top of the tank, a non-illustrated insulated lid (e.g., having an r-12 rating) can cover the entire open top and help keep the temperature regulated and prevent both evaporative cooling and contamination from outside sources"}]</data>
