tom of the reservoir"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100819522-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "an index member 33 made of a general rubber material or a synthetic resin material is installed to prevent leakage of rainwater stored from the water storage tank 1 having a horizontally sealed structure"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100819522-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the upper end of the lower connection block (50a), similar to the above-described connection block 50, the general rubber material so as to prevent the leakage of rainwater stored in the reservoir (1a) of a vertical closed structure through the weight of each member alternatively, an index member 53 made of a synthetic resin material is installed, and the sealing member 53 is formed between the connection block 50 and the lowermost connection block 50a by the index member 53 installed as described above"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100842368-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, in the drainage process of rainwater, unexpected rainwater and leakage of rainwater can be prevented through the connection pipe to further enjoy the effect of improving the safety of using the combined rainwater drainage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101012226-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, since the conventional separating wall is formed by forming a protrusion and a groove in a plurality of main bodies and are coupled in a fitting manner, when the amount of rainwater increases, the combined part is distorted, and water leakage occurs frequently"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101167604-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "since the connection pipe p1 can be inclined, the drain port 115 provided in the rainwater receiver can be conveniently connected to the connection fume pipe (drain pipe), thereby preventing leakage at the connection portion"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101197024-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the rainwater penetration system of the present invention stores rainwater underground and partially penetrates underground to effectively inhibit rainwater leakage during heavy rains, and includes a sedimentation tank for depositing sand and foreign substances in water, and rainwater discharged from the sedimentation tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101246202-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the water collecting groove 402 provides a volume for collecting water introduced into the concrete structure 400 due to leakage of water supply pipes or inflow of rainwater, and a worker is provided with a water pump (hereinafter, not shown) separately provided through the inspection opening 401"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101248434-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in addition, the present invention is another object to provide a block structure of the wall block, the index plate and the prefabricated rainwater storage tank to effectively prevent the leakage of stored rain while combining the wall block"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101326602-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "by opening a large amount of rainwater into the reservoir quickly and allowing it to be discharged into the drain, it is possible to respond quickly to the rainy weather conditions of the road, and also to prevent leakage of odors from the underground drainage to the outside and the introduction of foreign substances into the drain can be controlled"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101632920-B1", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "a malodor leakage prevention device installed in a rainwater receiver, a blocking plate for blocking the odor leaking from the lower side to the upper side"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101632920-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is another object of the present invention to provide a malodor leakage prevention device capable of smoothly performing an excellent discharge operation and an odor shielding function by ensuring stability of operation and a rainwater receiver equipped with the same"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101632920-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in order to attain the above object, the malodor leakage prevention device according to the present invention is a malodor leakage prevention device installed in a rainwater receiver, comprising"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101632920-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in order to attain the above object, the malodor leakage prevention device according to the present invention is a malodor leakage prevention device installed in a rainwater receiver, comprising"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101632920-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in order to attain the above object, the malodor leakage prevention device according to the present invention is a malodor leakage prevention device installed in a rainwater receiver, comprising"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101632920-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and a malodor leakage prevention device installed inside the rainwater receiver housing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101632920-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "meanwhile, the malodor leakage prevention device (v) according to the present invention can be constructed by directly installing the shield plate (2) having the above-described structure on the rainwater receiver housing, and a sub housing (1)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101632920-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "5a and 5b, the rainwater collector having the malodor leakage prevention device includes a rainwater receiver enclosure 6 having a drainage passage formed therein, and a plurality of fine inflow holes formed on the rainwater receiver enclosure 6 a rainwater catching cover 7, and a malodor leakage preventing device v installed in the rainwater catching enclosure 6"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101632920-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "hereinafter, the malodor leakage prevention device according to the first embodiment of the present invention and the operation of the rainwater receiver having the same will be briefly described"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101632920-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thereafter, the odor leakage preventing device (v) is joined to the lower housing part (62) of the rainwater receiver by welding or the like to complete the rainwater receiver, and then the windwater is installed at the edge of the road or the sidewalk, the cover 7 is installed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101715262-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, there has recently been a problem in that leaks occur in the rainwater harbor connection port to weaken the ground where the rainwater receiver is installed, and furthermore, there is a problem that the sinkhole is formed due to the leakage of the earthworm"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101715262-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thirdly, there is an advantage that the sinking of the ground caused by the rainwater receiver can be prevented by leakage of the rainwater due to the mortar operation finishing of the joint between the rainwater collector and the connecting pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101834261-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "it is another object of the present invention to provide an excellent watertightness and a satisfactory workability in order to prevent leakage of sewage or rainwater through a drain pipe connection hole of a public pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101834261-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "in addition, the watertightness is excellent in order to prevent leakage of sewage or rainwater through a drain pipe connection hole of the public pipeline, thereby providing an excellent effect of satisfactory construction"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102041291-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in order to solve this problem, a number of techniques have been disclosed for preventing leakage of odor flowing back from the sewage pipe back to the rainwater pipe or rainwater collection tank, for example, to cover oil and access holes of the rainwater collection tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102041291-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "however, only the mechanical devices installed in rainwater pipes or storm water collection tanks do not completely prevent leakage of odors flowing back from the sewage pipes, and as a result, odor leaks around sewage pipes or storm water collection tanks, causing discomfort to passers-by"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102380491-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the above-mentioned joint method, the joint method using the color ring is not used for sewage pipes including rainwater pipes because it is difficult to fill the mortar and there is a concern about groundwater contamination and subsidence due to leakage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102571397-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "a water leakage prevention unit disposed on a circumferential surface of the water collecting body and preventing rainwater from penetrating downward between the water collecting body and the drain hole"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200300524-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it can be inserted and inserted into the body to provide a pipe connection structure with a simple structure, and furthermore, it is possible to prevent soil contamination due to leakage of rainwater through securing watertightness, as well as to reduce the time and cost required for the reconstruction of the manhole"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200306646-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the present invention can prevent leakage of sewage or rainwater introduced into the manhole by the fixing ring to the outside"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200318223-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in particular, the seating plate 51 forms a certain curved shape and facilitates the seating of the sewage pipe 10 for sewerage, and also facilitates leakage and collection of rainwater, thereby effectively achieving leakage and rainwater discharge through the drain pipe 53"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200333351-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "through the present invention telescopic expansion means tube as described above, when connecting polyethylene manhole and concrete manhole, which are widely used for sewage and rainwater, it prevents leakage due to shrinkage and expansion of polyethylene pipe to prevent leakage and can reduce environmental pollution"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200368643-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is an object of the present invention to provide a resin reinforced