wing back to the rainwater inflow space through the lifting floating means provided in the manhole"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100774588-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "of the front wall of the rainwater chamber (3) to be rotatable through the operation from the outside and a tap hole for guiding the lifting and lowering of the horizontal bar 71 of the drop preventing jaw 7 in front of the vertical spiral shaft 81 through which the drop preventing jaw 7 is capable of lifting and lowering"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101128069-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "on the other hand, the rainwater stored in the elevator 55 is drained through the drainage holes 55a and 54a, and the weight of the elevator 55 becomes light when there is little or no inflow of rainwater, and thus, the elastic member 56 the lifting cylinder 55 rises by the elastic force of the"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101154026-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "after the manager removes the grating 23 to open the rain gutter 22 and connects the collecting rod to the lifting hook 27a on the ground, the container 27 is lifted to the outside of the rainwater storage tank 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101314575-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at this time, the discharge pipe is integrally coupled to the membrane module to be lifted together, so that the c type opening side of the discharge inlet is disposed on a vertical line with the rainwater inlet to prevent mutual interference during vertical lifting of the discharge inlet"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101326602-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "rainwater drainage for roads apparatus for draining of rain water for road the present invention relates to a rainwater drainage system for roads, and more particularly, between a plurality of stationary grates provided with rainwater inlet holes in the grating and each of the fixed grates, while being lifted up and down according to the lifting of the buoyant body"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101326602-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when a certain load (when a certain amount of rain is filled into the reservoir) is applied to the lifting plate 41a, the weight 41b opposite to the opening and closing plate 41a is lifted upward while the opening and closing plate 41a is axially rotated downward while the the bottom drain 11 is opened to drain the rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101326602-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as described above, the rainwater drainage device for a road according to an embodiment of the present invention is disposed between a plurality of fixed grate provided with rainwater inlet for grating and each of the fixed grate, while being lifted up and down according to the lifting of the buoyant body"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101386144-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the lifting flange 23 protrudes from the main body, foreign matter contained in rainwater or sewage is caught, thereby preventing the flow of water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101989601-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the opening and closing member 55 coupled with the lifting rod 51 is coupled to the upper storage chamber 35 when the lifting rod 51 moves upward to block the discharge port 39 to prevent the discharge of the rainwater to the outside"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102118557-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "therefore, in the filtration device of the second embodiment including the ball top valve 35 of the above embodiment, when the level of rainwater filled in the upper portion of the horizontal blocking plate 31 is low or there is no rainwater, the buoyant elevation part 353 descends, the lifting valve plate 352 is lowered to block the lower portion of the vertical pipe 34"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102882673-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "and the lifting grating (50) described above is formed below the upper surface of the grid plate (60a), thereby minimizing the accumulation of various sediments such as cigarette butts and fallen leaves around the rainwater drain on the grating"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102882673-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "due to this, the fixed grating (60) and the lifting grating (50) cover the opening of the rainwater drain, thereby maintaining the original function of the rainwater drain grating, which is to prevent the wheels of a vehicle or the legs of a pedestrian from falling into the drain"}]</data>
