  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100842368-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "here, the bottom of the dust collecting container 40 is preferably located below the height of the rainwater drainage pipe 12, the height of the deposit accumulated on the bottom of the dust collecting container 40 is the maximum to prevent the discharge of the deposit it is good not to exceed the height of the storm drain pipe (12)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100842368-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "this, if the bottom height of the dust collector (40) is located at the same or extremely similar height to the rainwater drainage pipe 12, the rainwater pipe through the rainwater rainwater drainage pipe 12 through the rainwater drainage pipe 12a this is because a vortex phenomenon is generated in the process of draining to (1), and sediment is deposited in the rain pipe 1, thereby preventing the drainage of rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101056650-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "here, the drain valve 158 is frequently opened to remove foreign substances when the rainwater reservoir tank 150 is cleaned or when foreign substances are deposited at the bottom"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101408976-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a branch pipe 121 for opening and closing the branch pipe 180 with the fixed flange 125 and the opening and closing door 182, the outlet 194 is pierced to the rear side of the branch pipe 121, and the end of the branch pipe 121 is rotated downward to remove the deposited soil 122 together with the rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101743540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "whether or not the backwash operation is performed is determined by the control panel 90 in accordance with the differential pressure alarm measured by the differential pressure sensor 690 a backwash operation is performed to remove foreign matters deposited inside the rainwater treatment apparatus 60"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200187320-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when it rains and rains a lot, rainwater and sewage are mixed, and a lot of water flows into the sewer inlet (1), and the flow rate increases, and sand flowing by sand and rainwater deposited on the floor flows downstream with the sewage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200328168-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "accordingly, sludge such as fine earth and sand is introduced into the rainwater and is deposited on the bottom surface of the water collecting part, thereby preventing the drainage part and the inflow part"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "including pollutants deposited on road surface during initial rainfall, even if the amount of drainage flows into the inlet of rainwater drainage is large can be stored to prevent the drainage of water back to the road"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200399238-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, sludge deposits, such as fallen leaves, cigarette butts, and earth and sand, which are introduced together with the rainwater and sewage, are separated while passing through the first, second, third filtering means 21, 22, and 23 that vary the areas of the drain holes 212, 222, 232"}, {"pat_id": "US-5239794-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the structure further comprises a catchment supported to receive rainwater running from the roofing and at least one water-carrying conduit extending from the catchment to the enclosure interior so as to deposit rainwater running from the roof into the enclosure beneath the flooring"}, {"pat_id": "US-5239794-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at least one water carrying conduit 62 is provided extending from the catchment 60 to the interior of the enclosure formed by foundation 20 and floor 30, in particular the enclosure 25a, so as to deposit rainwater running from the roofing into the enclosure beneath the flooring 40"}]</data>
</edge>
