, "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and a backflow prevention part provided to block backflow of sewage and rainwater introduced into and drained from the manhole body"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200467574-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a backflow prevention buoy coupled to the hollow tube to prevent departure, provided to block the hollow tube by water pressure when the sewage and rainwater flowing into the manhole body are drained"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200467574-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the reverse flow prevention unit 130 blocks the reverse flow of sewage and rainwater that flows into the manhole body 110 and is drained, thereby inducing sewage and rainwater flowing into the inflow pipe 110a and the manhole cover 120"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200467574-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is provided to guide the upward movement of the induction part 131 provided to drain, the backflow prevention buoy 134 and the backflow prevention buoy 134 provided to block the backflow of sewage and rainwater by raising the induction unit 131 to the upward movement"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200467574-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the hollow tube 132 of the induction part 131 is blocked by the backflow prevention buoy 134, the sewage and rainwater generated from the drain pipe 110b are inflowed through the hollow pipe 132 and the manhole cover 120"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200467574-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the reverse flow prevention unit 230 blocks the reverse flow of sewage and rainwater that flows into the manhole body 210 and then drains"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200467574-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the drainage passage 237c, the hollow tube 322 and the guide portion 239 is sequentially passed through the drainage pipe 210b, the blocking portion 235 of the backflow prevention buoy 234 is lowered by its own weight it is caught through the locking portion 236 to the support portion 237 to open the rear hollow tube 232 (see fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200467574-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the hollow pipe 232 of the induction part 231 is blocked by the backflow prevention buoy 234, the sewage and rainwater generated from the drain pipe 210b are passed through the hollow pipe 232 to the inlet pipe 210a and the manhole cover 220"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200478285-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the water supply and drainage line 250 is made of stainless steel so as not to cause corrosion, and comprises a water supply line for supplying water and a drain line for draining the used water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200485881-Y1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "however, the conventional odor prevention type sewer lid can achieve a purpose of smooth drainage and odor shielding, but the structure of the door for naturally sealing or opening the hole formed in the sewer lid is complicated, which increases the manufacturing cost"}, {"pat_id": "US-10184221-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "for example, low temperature conditions may indicate ice formation which could prevent water control by blockage of water through the drains of the water control devices"}, {"pat_id": "US-11060313-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "should flood waters exceed the dfe 3, water will enter the building 1 through the drain holes 19 preventing the collapse of exterior wall 5a and damage to the building foundation 4 from buoyancy effects"}, {"pat_id": "US-11118824-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "another non-trivial challenge is that to prevent freezing, the water piping must drain completely when not in use"}, {"pat_id": "US-11298635-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "alternative structures, for example, chambers filled with porous media and underdrains, can be cost prohibitive and may fail resulting in flooding the rain garden with debris, which requires extensive clean-up"}, {"pat_id": "US-11560697-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the drainage line becomes clogged or blocked with debris, ice, or as a result of build-up inside the pipe, a flooding event can occur in the building if adequate precautions are not taken"}, {"pat_id": "US-11560697-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "such scenarios can occur when the sewer conduit has been blocked by detritus, and/or accumulation or buildup around the interior of the drainage pipes which can occur without regular maintenance and monitoring of the sewer drainage lines"}, {"pat_id": "US-11560697-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "this causes a flood condition, where blockage of the drainage from the building causes pressure buildup between the municipal sewer and the building, putting the building at risk of a backwater flood"}, {"pat_id": "US-11959688-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "another non-trivial challenge is that to prevent freezing, the water piping must drain completely when not in use"}, {"pat_id": "US-11987945-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "slots must be cut into the collection pipe, the free end of the drain belt must be sealed (to prevent fine soil particles from entering into and blocking channels within the drain belt), and the sealing mechanism must be installed around the interface"}, {"pat_id": "US-12202741-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as a result, the particulates and other contaminants that can be dislodged and removed by backwashing the resin are caused to flow out the top of the tank, through the valve and are discharged to a suitable waste drain through the drain port c"}, {"pat_id": "US-12209051-B2", "para_id": "para_84", "text": "it is therefore not necessary to wrap the water drainage device in a geo-textile to prevent contamination"}, {"pat_id": "US-12252874-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "method 300 begins at block 302, where drain sensor data is received from the drainage sensors (e.g., the set of drainage sensors 146a-d of figs"}, {"pat_id": "US-12252874-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at block 312, a start time of a tidal backflow (e.g., backflow of tidal water into the drainage system s set of outputs) is determined"}, {"pat_id": "US-12252874-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at block 322, tidal backflow and no tidal backflow zones of the drainage sensor depth data may be determined"}, {"pat_id": "US-4180094-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the drain cover assembly is compact, portable, and easily intalled over a drain to prevent water from backing up into a building in which the drain is located"}, {"pat_id": "US-4180094-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the drain cover 12 is placed over a drain 14 in the floor 16 to prevent water backing up in the sewage system from flooding into the building in which the drain 14 is located"}, {"pat_id": "US-4180094-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the drain cover assembly 10 is compact, portable, and easily intalled over a drain 14 to prevent water from backing up into a building in which the drain is located"}, {"pat_id": "US-5322629-A", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "this is due to the continual accretion of pollutants on the drained surfaces over time"}, {"pat_id": "US-5322629-A", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "to further prevent compost particles from filtering into the rock underdrain and minimize potential blockage problems, various woven and non-woven filter fabrics were tested, positioned between the compost bed and the rock underdrain layer"}, {"pat_id": "US-5662801-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it may further have the capability of monitoring the flow of the feed stream throughout the system via the flow meter, controlling the main pump and prompting the operator to drain organic contaminants from the separating unit"}, {"pat_id": "US-5736059-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the tank must therefore drain away into the lower heat exchanger and thence to the sewer when there is no wastewater flow, leaving the upper heat exchanger high and dry protecting the fresh water supply from contamination"}, {"pat_id": "US-5788409-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in colder climates, the drain field lateral 2 may be buried deeper to prevent the liquid in the pipe 4 from freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-6932540-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the reservoir covers of the invention further provide adequate liquid transport properties to drain rainwater from the surface of the cover into the reservoir, thereby avoiding inundation"}, {"pat_id": "US-8277646-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "such solutions, however, often can be ineffective at protecting and preventing dirt and debris from entering the storm water drainage system"}, {"pat_id": "US-8632273-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "12, water flows into a drain well 22 through a draining pipe 3 of a draining structure of vertical roads, wherein impurities enters a deposit layer and water is drained via a drain tube 23"}, {"pat_id": "US-8661819-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the contaminants may be removed from the heat exchanger in a generally non-invasive manner by periodically discharging water with the highly concentrated contaminants from a bottom drain of the heat exchanger (e.g., blow-down, blow-by, etc.) and directing the water to a containment location (e.g., evaporation pond or heat exchanger, storage tank etc.)"}, {"pat_id": "US-8661819-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the separator 486 also advantageously helps to capture contaminants that carry-over with the steam, and may be collected from the drain portion of the separator 486"}, {"pat_id": "US-8703065-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, a leakage detection pipe may extend from the surface into the drainage material so that an operator may visually inspect the drainage material to determine whether the primary liner is leaking"}, {"pat_id": "US-8776522-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the contaminants may be removed from the heat exchanger in a generally non-invasive manner by periodically discharging water with the highly concentrated contaminants from a bottom drain of the heat exchanger (e.g., blow-down, blow-by, etc.) and directing the water to a containment location (e.g., evaporation pond or heat exchanger, storage tank etc.)"}, {"pat_id": "US-8776522-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the separator 486 also advantageously helps to capture contaminants that carry-over with the steam, and may be collected from the drain portion of the separator 486"}, {"pat_id": "US-9005310-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, a leakage detection pipe may extend from the surface into the drainage material so that an operator may visually inspect the drainage material to determine whether the primary liner is leaking"}, {"pat_id": "US-9550686-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "5, it can be seen that failure to properly clean the ducting and exhaust fan assembly 2, blockage of the drainage spout 22 or over flowing of the grease collection tray 24 will result in significant spillage, environmental liability and damage to the roof"}, {"pat_id": "US-9624658-B2", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "7 shows a side view of a storm water drain filter secured to a wall of a pit via a cantilever bracket"}, {"pat_id": "US-9963865-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "leaves, plastic bags, disposable cups, soda cans, and twigs, are all common litter that could flow into a drain, collect in the drain or further down the sewer, and cause a blockage"}]</data>
