 and when rainwater flows in, the cover rotates to block the drainage hole, thereby achieving the purpose"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102805058-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "wherein the rotating part of an opening/closing cover that blocks a drain hole of a trap body is formed higher than the opening/closing part, thereby preventing the rotating part from being submerged in rainwater during the rainwater draining process"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102805058-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as a result, when rainwater does not flow in, the opening/closing cover (50) cannot close the drain hole (31), failing to block the bad smell"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102811690-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in this case, the accumulated small sediments block the connection to the sewer pipe through which the rainwater is discharged, reducing the efficiency of the rainwater drainage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102814353-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "meanwhile, if waste such as leaves flows into the drain, the drain with the above function loses its flood prevention function by blocking the flow and discharge of rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102822205-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "an experiment conducted by the national disaster and safety research institute found that when a rainwater drain is blocked by trash or covered with rubber sheets, the flooded area increases three times and the flood depth increases by more than 2.3 times"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102827175-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and a plurality of permeable blocks that are fitted closely into the square spaces of the square frame with their lower surfaces caught on the wire mesh and block the inflow of sewage while draining rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102882673-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "and the lifting grating (50) described above is formed below the upper surface of the grid plate (60a), thereby minimizing the accumulation of various sediments such as cigarette butts and fallen leaves around the rainwater drain on the grating"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102882673-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "due to this, the fixed grating (60) and the lifting grating (50) cover the opening of the rainwater drain, thereby maintaining the original function of the rainwater drain grating, which is to prevent the wheels of a vehicle or the legs of a pedestrian from falling into the drain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200151725-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the upper part of the drainage channel was reveted to prevent vehicle accidents and blockage of the channel by foreign substances and soil, and instead, water collectors were installed at regular intervals so that rainwater flowed into the drainage channel"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200208312-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the sediment is separated by stages through the fine holes of the primary filtration network and the bottom plate to provide a rainwater catchment for the road equipped with a filtration tank to prevent the drainage blockage in advance"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200303595-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "drainpipe anti-closed device of manhole the present invention relates to a manhole drainage blockage preventing device to collect the rainwater or sewage, and to prevent foreign substances from entering the clogged drainage pipe of the manhole discharged to the sewer pipe connected to the sewage treatment plant"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200318223-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in particular, the seating plate 51 forms a certain curved shape and facilitates the seating of the sewage pipe 10 for sewerage, and also facilitates leakage and collection of rainwater, thereby effectively achieving leakage and rainwater discharge through the drain pipe 53"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200328168-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "accordingly, sludge such as fine earth and sand is introduced into the rainwater and is deposited on the bottom surface of the water collecting part, thereby preventing the drainage part and the inflow part"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200328168-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the present invention was devised to solve the general problems of the aforementioned conventional warfare, the object of the present invention is to provide a rainwater drainage drainage that is provided with a blockage preventing means and a water removal means of the sediment, which prevents the rainwater from being clogged by the sediment at the source and also easily removes the sediment"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200338818-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "here, the main body 10 is formed with a recess 14 so as to protrude downwards at the adjacent portion of the lower side bottom drain 12 and to pour sand, thereby preventing the scour of the ground due to drainage of rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200338818-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "here, the main body portion 10 is formed with a groove portion 14 to protrude downward at the side adjacent to the lower side bottom drain 12 thereof and to circulate sand, thereby preventing the scour of the ground due to drainage of rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200338818-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "here, the main body 10 is formed with a recess 14 so as to project downwards at the adjacent portion of the lower side bottom drain 12 and to pour sand, to prevent scour of the ground due to the drainage drain of rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "including pollutants deposited on road surface during initial rainfall, even if the amount of drainage flows into the inlet of rainwater drainage is large can be stored to prevent the drainage of water back to the road"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200357071-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "road drainage with first flush treatment ability the present invention is to insert a filter filling tank having a filtration treatment function in the conventional rainwater receiver to the road surface drainage treatment device having an initial excellent treatment function that can reliably remove and treat contaminants contained in the road surface drainage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200391152-Y1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "it is possible to secure the strength, and because the drain pipe is normally blocked by the odor backflow installed in the drain pipe, it is possible to block the odor backflow from the sewage main pipe to the rainwater receiving side"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200398817-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the vinyl bag may be covered on the grating of the drain to prevent the backflow of the odor, but in case of sudden rain, the vinyl bag may block the drain of the rainwater, which may prevent the rainwater from draining and cause a safety accident due to the rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200399238-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, sludge deposits, such as fallen leaves, cigarette butts, and earth and sand, which are introduced together with the rainwater and sewage, are separated while passing through the first, second, third filtering means 21, 22, and 23 that vary the areas of the drain holes 212, 222, 232"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200403834-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, the sewage and rainwater flowing along the road surface 1 in the state in which the floating block 20 is seated on the lid 11 flows to the drainage block 10 via the drainage hole 21 and the lid 11"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200403834-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and, according to the amount of sewage and rainwater can move the pot can prevent the blockage of the drain block"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200416889-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "to block the upper portion of the trench cover 31, the drainage is not made smoothly, at this time through the inlet / outlet 12 of the body 11 installed on one side is introduced into the manhole 20 ), so that the inflow of water is prevented from rainwater and sewage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200446316-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "sewage should be supplied with household sewage from homes or commercial buildings near sewer pipes, and rainwater quickly drains rainwater generated during rainfall or snowfall to prevent road flooding and to prevent contamination from rainwater splashing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200448229-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, the above-described invention is effective for blocking odor and drainage, but it is necessary to discharge the water in the sewage pipe to the outside in order to prevent breakage of the sewage pipe when the rainwater is filled with rainwater and the pressure is applied to the sewage pipe due to heavy rain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200449313-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, in winter, a small amount of water (rainwater or tears) accumulated on the bottom of the barrel can be quickly drained to the outside to prevent freezing of the barrel.in the agricultural season, water is leaked along the barrel by blocking the drain pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200467574-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and a backflow prevention part provided to block backflow of sewage and rainwater introduced into and drained from the manhole body"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200467574-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a backflow prevention buoy provided to block the hollow tube by an upward movement by water pressure when the sewage and rainwater flowing into the manhole body are drained"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200467574-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and a backflow prevention part provided to block backflow of sewage and rainwater introduced into and drained from the manhole body"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200467574-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a backflow prevention buoy coupled to the hollow tube to prevent departure, provided to block the hollow tube by water pressure when the sewage and rainwater flowing into the manhole body are drained"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200467574-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the reverse flow prevention unit 130 blocks the reverse flow of sewage and rainwater that flows into the manhole body 110 and is drained, thereby inducing sewage and rainwater flowing into the inflow pipe 110a and the manhole cover 120"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200467574-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is provided to guide the upward movement of the induction part 131 provided to drain, the backflow prevention buoy 134 and the backflow prevention buoy 134 provided to block the backflow of sewage and rainwater by raising the induction unit 131 to the upward movement"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200467574-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the hollow tube 132 of the induction part 131 is blocked by the backflow prevention buoy 134, the sewage and rainwater generated from the drain pipe 110b are inflowed through the hollow pipe 132 and the manhole cover 120"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200467574-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the reverse flow prevention unit 230 blocks the reverse flow of sewage and rainwater that flows into the manhole body 210 and then drains"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200467574-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the hollow pipe 232 of the induction part 231 is blocked by the backflow prevention buoy 234, the sewage and rainwater generated from the drain pipe 210b are passed through the hollow pipe 232 to the inlet pipe 210a and the manhole cover 220"}, {"pat_id": "US-6932540-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the reservoir covers of the invention further provide adequate liquid transport properties to drain rainwater from the surface of the cover into the reservoir, thereby avoiding inundation"}]</data>
