ter may leak into the rainwater chamber 110 through such a method"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200300524-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it can be inserted and inserted into the body to provide a pipe connection structure with a simple structure, and furthermore, it is possible to prevent soil contamination due to leakage of rainwater through securing watertightness, as well as to reduce the time and cost required for the reconstruction of the manhole"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200322595-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "there is considerable difficulty in construction because the inlet pipe connection part or outlet pipe connection part of the receiver does not match, and if the inlet pipe or outlet pipe which is already constructed is forcibly bent and connected to the rainwater receiver, the connection part is weak and easily leaks"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200455130-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as shown in figure 10 and 11, the bollard-type hot water leak detection panel guard according to another embodiment of the present invention, it is possible to prevent rainwater from entering the interior of the housing 110 through the inlet 130"}, {"pat_id": "US-11629721-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the algorithms can be trained to determine whether sensor data from a system is indicative of, for example, a normal activity (a normal flush), an abnormal activity (a minor, medium or major leak), a condition, and/or an activity in the fluid system"}, {"pat_id": "US-11629721-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "for example, the system can detect whether data is indicative of normal use conditions or a leak using machine learning algorithms that can be trained over time with data fed into the system(s) such that the system can accurately identify whether sensor data is indicative of normal and/or abnormal conditions"}, {"pat_id": "US-8337121-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "while the 705 patent does teach the utilization of a rubber gasket for preventing leakage of snow, rain, or the like, this apparatus is unsuitable for utilization in conjunction with the system of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "US-9709431-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in this example, if the rain sensor indicates that there is no local precipitation, but that there are water levels above a threshold, the control system 100 may track property operations to determine if there is a problematic operation that may be causing water leakage within the property"}, {"pat_id": "US-9709431-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in this example, if the rain sensor indicates that there is excessive local precipitation, the calculated susceptibility of water damage may be increased based on determining that the likelihood of water leaking into the property is much higher"}, {"pat_id": "US-9828757-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "vacuum sewer systems operate inefficiently when water infiltration and inflow are present due to leaks and improper connections to storm water drains"}]</data>
