  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "JP-2589989-Y2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the water accumulated in the rainwater infiltration basin penetrates from the bottom of the rainwater infiltration basin into the gap between the gravel or crushed stones in the foundation block, and is drained from a drain hole formed in the side circumference of the rainwater infiltration basin"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2589989-Y2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "[0016] the water retention block for a rainwater infiltration basin according to the invention is much lighter and easier to handle than a conventional water retention block, so that its volume can be increased"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3459918-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "further, the drainage tool according to the invention of claim 2is provided at the upper end of the side wall of the gutter block to prevent rainwater, etc.a drainage tool for guiding theit has a water body"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3459918-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "further, the drainage tool according to the invention described in claim 3is provided at the upper end of the side wall of the gutter block to prevent rainwater, etc.a drainage tool for guiding theit has a water body"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3459918-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "further, the drainage tool according to the invention of claim 4is provided at the upper end of the side wall of the gutter block to prevent rainwater, etc.a drainage tool for guiding theit has a water body"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3459918-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "next, the gutter block 1 having the above structure the function and effect of the drainage tool 2 will be described"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3459918-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the first conduit e1 or the second conduit e it is possible to guide rainwater and the like that have entered into the gutter block 1 through the drainage grooves 1d and 1d into the gutter block 1 without being blocked by the covering material w placed on the lid-hanging stepped portion 1b"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3459918-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "wherein:it produces the effect of item 1.also, as described in claim 12.according to the gutter block provided with the drainage tool, the effect of claim 5 is obtained.play the fruit"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3459918-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "further, according to the gutter block provided with the drainage device described in claim 13 , in addition to the effect of claim 11 or 12 , rainwater and the like that have entered the first water conduit can be along the lower surface that is the inclined surface"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100435535-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, the conventional sidewalk block has a problem that the flooding area occurs frequently in the case where the drainage is vulnerable because the phenomenon that the rain water is not submerged through the ground of the block and concentrated in the sewer pipe occurs"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100593258-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "in the boundary block system capable of drainage, installed between the sidewalks and the driveway, the wheels of the vehicle are removed to serve as a boundary between the sidewalks and the roadway, to drain the rainwater on the roadway, and to prevent the vehicle from rushing to the sidewalk due to the collision with the car"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100593258-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "another object of the present invention to provide a boundary block system that can prevent backflow and block the odor generated in the drainage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100593258-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "still another object of the present invention is to provide a boundary block system that is easy to clean the drainage path and that can substantially increase the running area of the vehicle"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100605037-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in case of rain, as the inflow of sewage increases, the sewer inlet is blocked while the frame plate is kept horizontal"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100605041-B1", "para_id": "pa