er leakage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101632920-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is another object of the present invention to provide a malodor leakage prevention device capable of smoothly performing an excellent discharge operation and an odor shielding function by ensuring stability of operation and a rainwater receiver equipped with the same"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101632920-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in order to attain the above object, the malodor leakage prevention device according to the present invention is a malodor leakage prevention device installed in a rainwater receiver, comprising"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101632920-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in order to attain the above object, the malodor leakage prevention device according to the present invention is a malodor leakage prevention device installed in a rainwater receiver, comprising"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101632920-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in order to attain the above object, the malodor leakage prevention device according to the present invention is a malodor leakage prevention device installed in a rainwater receiver, comprising"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101632920-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and a malodor leakage prevention device installed inside the rainwater receiver housing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101632920-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "meanwhile, the malodor leakage prevention device (v) according to the present invention can be constructed by directly installing the shield plate (2) having the above-described structure on the rainwater receiver housing, and a sub housing (1)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101632920-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "5a and 5b, the rainwater collector having the malodor leakage prevention device includes a rainwater receiver enclosure 6 having a drainage passage formed therein, and a plurality of fine inflow holes formed on the rainwater receiver enclosure 6 a rainwater catching cover 7, and a malodor leakage preventing device v installed in the rainwater catching enclosure 6"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101632920-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "hereinafter, the malodor leakage prevention device according to the first embodiment of the present invention and the operation of the rainwater receiver having the same will be briefly described"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101632920-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thereafter, the odor leakage preventing device (v) is joined to the lower housing part (62) of the rainwater receiver by welding or the like to complete the rainwater receiver, and then the windwater is installed at the edge of the road or the sidewalk, the cover 7 is installed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101715262-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, there has recently been a problem in that leaks occur in the rainwater harbor connection port to weaken the ground where the rainwater receiver is installed, and furthermore, there is a problem that the sinkhole is formed due to the leakage of the earthworm"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101715262-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thirdly, there is an advantage that the sinking of the ground caused by the rainwater receiver can be prevented by leakage of the rainwater due to the mortar operation finishing of the joint between the rainwater collector and the connecting pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101730962-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "this leakage path causes the drain and raw water to leave the fitting rather than entering the generated steam through the drain 320 shown in figures 3g-3i"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102009028-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "leakage drainage system for underground parking lot in apartment house waterproofing system for underground parking lot in apartment building the present invention relates to an underground parking lot leakage system drainage device for a multi-unit house, and more specifically, to provide a space for smoothly draining water in the underground parking lot, it is possible to keep the parking lot of the building clean through rapid drainage, it relates to a drainage system of the underground parking lot of the multi-unit house which can easily remove foreign substances filtered from the drainage system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102041291-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in order to solve this problem, a number of techniques have been disclosed for preventing leakage of odor flowing back from the sewage pipe back to the rainwater pipe or rainwater collection tank, for example, to cover oil and access holes of the rainwater collection tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102041291-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "however, only the mechanical devices installed in rainwater pipes or storm water collection tanks do not completely prevent leakage of odors flowing back from the sewage pipes, and as a result, odor leaks around sewage pipes or storm water collection tanks, causing discomfort to passers-by"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102081866-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "this leakage path causes the effluent and raw water to leave the fit rather than enter the product vapor through the drain 320 shown in figs"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102571397-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "a water leakage prevention unit disposed on a circumferential surface of the water collecting body and preventing rainwater from penetrating downward between the water collecting body and the drain hole"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200300524-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it can be inserted and inserted into the body to provide a pipe connection structure with a simple structure, and furthermore, it is possible to prevent soil contamination due to leakage of rainwater through securing watertightness, as well as to reduce the time and cost required for the reconstruction of the manhole"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200403422-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "more specifically, by artificially opening and closing the drain hole formed in the manhole cover by opening the drain hole in the rainy season when you want to discharge the sewage or rain, and smoothly discharged sewage or rain water, and closed in the dry season by preventing the leakage of flies, mosquitoes and other harmful insects, and to prevent odors to achieve a more pleasant environment free of odors and pests"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200449230-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "more specifically, the present invention relates to a safety manhole cover for preventing rainwater trapping with a catch preventing part and a slope to prevent safety accidents due to rainwater swelling and rainwater leakage during rainy weather and to prevent accidents caused by footing when a pedestrian is walking"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200449230-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "there was a problem that causes an electric shock accident.in order to solve these problems, the present invention prevents safety accidents due to rainwater swelling and rainwater leakage in rainy weather, and safety manholes for preventing rainwater swelling with a catch preventing part and an inclined part to prevent accidents caused by footfalls when pedestrians walk"}, {"pat_id": "KR-960008516-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, since the temperature sensor is weak to moisture, if the inside gets wet due to snow or rain when exposed to the outside, the temperature sensor often malfunctions, and there is a tendency for the risk of electric leakage and breakdown"}, {"pat_id": "KR-960008516-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as a result, the present invention does not have any risk of moisture penetrating into the temperature sensing sensor effectively embedded in the cover even if it is hit by snow or rain as in the prior art, so there is no risk of leakage or risk of failure, especially the temperature sensing sensor is damp"}, {"pat_id": "US-8337121-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "while the 705 patent does teach the utilization of a rubber gasket for preventing leakage of snow, rain, or the like, this apparatus is unsuitable for utilization in conjunction with the system of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "US-8703065-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, a leakage detection pipe may extend from the surface into the drainage material so that an operator may visually inspect the drainage material to determine whether the primary liner is leaking"}, {"pat_id": "US-9005310-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, a leakage detection pipe may extend from the surface into the drainage material so that an operator may visually inspect the drainage material to determine whether the primary liner is leaking"}, {"pat_id": "US-9709431-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in this example, if the rain sensor indicates that there is no local precipitation, but that there are water levels above a threshold, the control system 100 may track property operations to determine if there is a problematic operation that may be causing water leakage within the property"}]</data>
