  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100499612-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "first, it is a method of capturing various contaminants, solids, and earth and sand contained in sewage or rainwater in the manhole, requiring maintenance for the removal of these captures, and high maintenance costs"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100516951-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "therefore, in the present invention, the removal of contaminants is actively performed for the building drainage during the initial rainfall stage with a high content of contaminants, and some of the contaminants are considered in consideration of the low content of contaminants for the subsequent building drainage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100546061-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "also, in sewage or polluted small streams, contaminants are deposited on the bottom in sinking areas, lowlands, and bore areas, and when the flow rate increases during rainfall, the sewage power increases, causing the sediment to float and outflow"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100584236-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "however, even with this method, it is difficult to completely remove the harmful contaminants that are strongly attached to the catchment surface by hydrophobic interaction, and the accumulated contaminants are gradually introduced into the storage tank over a long period of time during rainfall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100584236-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in addition, the continuous disinfection of rainwater in the storage tank requires expenditure of chemical costs, power costs, etc., and because the process is difficult to control and cumbersome, a more fundamental solution for removing the contaminants is required"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100584236-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "thus, when rainwater is concentrated on the catchment surface 2 in which contamination by contaminants is prevented early by the titanium dioxide photocatalyst layer, the rainwater is transferred to the storage tank 1 through the catchment port 3 and stored"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100614766-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in addition, the present invention satisfactorily removes contaminants such as insecticides and herbicides contained in the drainage in the field, and suspended matters contained in the water falling out after the harrowing prior to planting, so that these suspended matters are flowed into the river or the like"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100614766-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "a discharge box (91) having an outlet partition wall (61) for storing contaminants after the contaminants are filtered and for draining the road surface drainage through the discharge opening (90) and excess water exceeding the processing capacity and draining it to the drainage path (100)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100614766-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the treated water through which the contaminant is removed by passing through the filter medium filling tank 71 is accommodated in the discharge box 91 by overflowing through the discharge unit 90, and then introduced into the drain pipe or artificial wetland through the drainage path 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100614766-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "therefore, in the present invention, the removal of contaminants is actively performed on the road drainage during the initial rainfall stage in which the content of the pollutants is high, and the filter filling tank 71 considering the low amount of pollutants in the subsequent road drainage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100614766-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "(3) since the filter filling tank which removes contaminants contained in the drainage by filtration or adsorption is detachably installed in the treatment tank, while the drainage flowed from the inlet of the storm receiver flows through the treatment tank, contaminants contained in the waste water are removed by the filter medium"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100681933-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "on the other hand, in the reservoir where rainwater is introduced, large and small floating garbage, contaminants are introduced to float on the water surface, thereby damaging the waterfront landscape"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100750645-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "these storm receivers store the road drainage during rainfall and transfer it to the filtration apparatus to adsorb and remove contaminants contained in the road drainage, and then discharge only the treated water to the sewer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100750645-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is provided in the storage space of the treatment tank 6 includes a filtration device (9) for filtering and adsorption to remove contaminants contained in the road surface drainage rising from the lower portion of the treatment tank (6)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100750645-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the amount of contaminants in the road surface drainage due to the subsequent rainfall is small, and it can be said that there is little problem even if the excess water is discharged immediately without passing through the filtration tank 54"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100784496-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the filtration tank 30 is provided with a filter 31 for filtering contaminants such as organic substances, oil components, and suspended solids in the rainfall that do not settle in the precipitation tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100784496-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the contaminants having their own weight among the contaminants included in the initial rainfall introduced into the first settling tank 10 are primarily precipitated at the bottom of the first settling tank 10 and do not settle in the first settling tank 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100784496-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "meanwhile, contaminants having their own weight among the pollutants included in the rainfall flowing into the second settling tank 20 are second precipitated to the bottom of the second settling tank 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100786511-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "this phenomenon causes a vortex phenomenon while the rainwater including the pollutant moving in the contaminant treatment tank 13 passes through the rainwater port 16 eccentrically to one side, and despite this vortex phenomenon, 17) and the reverse flow prevention plate 18 once settles down as it is"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100786511-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "fine suspended matter having little specific gravity remaining after being precipitated in the contaminant treatment tank 13 is moved through the filter 20 installed in the upper part to the storm conduit 12 due to the continuous inflow of rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100823236-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the bottom of the cylindrical screen, the bottom is formed with a drain hole is formed by the coarse sediment freely dropped through the contaminant discharge pipe and the vortex discharged to the sewage pipe intermediate intermediate sediment removed from the cylindrical screen"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100823236-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "1 to 3, the screw screen 10 excludes coarse contaminants included in the initial rainwater during rainy weather and sediment contaminants deposited in the combined sewer pipe 2, and removes the coarse contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100823236-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the initial rainwater accumulated at the tip of the screen body 11 together with the coarse contaminants and sediment contaminants may be discharged through the contaminant discharge pipe 17, which may cause a variety of problems such as a burden on the sewage pipe 4 or the sewage treatment plant"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100823240-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, when the initial rainwater and sediment contaminants are completely excluded from the initial rainwater treatment facility 1 and the pressure or water level becomes zero, the drain pump 21 receiving the water is driven to operate the water tank 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100841267-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as described above, in the conventional rainwater discharge chamber, the floating contaminants 5 flowing in do not flow into the collecting pipe 3 in rainy weather, but are discharged into the public water through the discharge pipe 4 so that water pollution of the public water is ) is the cause"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100927631-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at this time, when rainwater flows into the sedimentation tank 200, heavy foreign matter such as sand sinks to the bottom and light foreign matter such as leaves or vinyl fragments rises on the surface of the water to easily remove contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100927631-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "1 to 3, when rainwater is first moved through a manhole or the like and is introduced into the rainwater storage tank 100 through the inlet 120, the relatively heavy contaminants in the sedimentation tank 200 sink and relatively light contaminants accumulate on the surface of the water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100958442-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, the conventional non-point contaminant purification device of the initial excellent excellent outflow water is the final outflow pipe line 21 only after the rainwater received in the median filling tank 13 and the settling tank 14 of the initial excellent purification tank 10 becomes the full water level"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100962546-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the end region of the drain pipe, it is preferable that a backflow prevention plate is provided to prevent backflow of contaminants in the sediment holding tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100962546-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, the contaminants accumulated on the bottom surface of the sediment holding tank 410 may be prevented from rising to the filter plate accommodating part 160 by riding the drain pipe 420"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100962546-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, particulate contaminants contained in rainwater fall into the sediment holding tank 410 and is confined"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100990483-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the screen 12 is installed in multiple stages on the sewage pipe 10 to prevent the inflow of contaminants into the stormwater chamber 11 by separating various contaminants in advance before the initial rainwater reaches the first opening and closing plate 111"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101024670-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "this is called cso (combined sewer overflow), and due to the initial rainfall, the pollutants on the surface and the contaminants settled in the combined sewage pipe are simultaneously leaked, resulting in a high concentration and load of the pollutants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101067633-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "this is called cso (combined sewer overflow), and due to the initial rainfall, the pollutants on the surface and the contaminants settled in the consolidation sewers flow out at the same time, resulting in a very high concentration and load of the pollutants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101089297-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the inner cylinder 142 is installed inside the inlet 122 to increase the flow rate of rainwater flowing into the contaminant collecting network 130, so that the contaminants mixed with rainwater (including the flocculents)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101095323-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "this is called cso (combined sewer overflow), and due to the initial rainfall, the pollutants on the surface and the contaminants settled in the consolidation sewers flow out at the same time, resulting in a very high concentration and load of the pollutants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101113989-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, since the tip of the connecting pipe 50 is bent downward so as to be submerged in the rainwater in the sedimentation tank 10, contaminants having a small specific gravity such as oil floating on the water surface may not pass through the connecting pipe 50"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101113989-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the contaminant is finally filtered while passing through the side surface of the ball-type water pipe 43 and discharged into the drain hole 24 at the bottom of the filtration tank 23 connected with the water pipe 43"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101124771-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, if a contaminant is introduced along with the inflow water, even if the water is drained, it is trapped by the opening and closing plate to accumulate and cause poor drainage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101133277-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "the height of the purification device 1 of the present invention is lower than the height of the inclined drain conduit 2, so that the contaminants are smoothly conveyed to the contaminant collecting part 40, and also due to the heavy rain, the flow rate of rainwater may be high"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101154026-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "to prevent or prevent flooding and flooding of roads and houses, and to treat sewage by storm control facilities after rain, and to utilize the sidewalls of the stormwater to collect contaminants contained in rainwater and to vent rainwater reservoirs"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101154026-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in this way, by collecting the contaminants collected in the container 27 periodically, the inside of the rainwater storage tank 20 can be kept clean, and clogging of the drainage system by the contaminants can be prevented"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101181324-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, after treating the roadbed sediment and sediment contaminants contained in the sewage of rainy weather has been developed and used to flow into natural rivers or nearby sea, there is a storage tank type treatment device"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101192911-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, as the rainwater is further collected through the bottom of the rainwater container, the drainage speed is lowered, and contaminants introduced with the rainwater are accumulated on the floor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101192911-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, the rainwater that passes through the rainwater container to the main d