  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "EP-0211164-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "if both yes signals are present at the and gate 41 at the same time, then there is a blockage in the drain pipe 13, because otherwise the flow through the drain pipe 13 would be significantly greater at such high water levels and there will therefore be a fault message indicating this blockage reports, and / or triggered a security process"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2780720-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, when the water level of the pair of water level sensors installed in the snow channel changes, the blockage of the two water level sensors is determined by judging which of the three types of the fluctuations is the above-described pattern"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2780720-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, since fluctuations in the water level are also observed in other water level monitoring panels in the system, the overall system determines the blockage position in units of sections where water level sensors are installed by comprehensively judging the detection results of each water level monitoring panel"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2780720-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "also, in consideration of the degree of water level difference between the two points, the absolute water level of each water level sensor, etc., the urgency of the water level rise due to blockage is divided into, for example, three stages, and only the alarm lamp is turned on in the first stage"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5213295-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a decrease in pump discharge due to an air lock or suction blockage is determined based on the actual water level at the expected arrival time"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7774358-B1", "para_id": "para_54", "text": "when the water level becomes abnormal (rising), factors such as blockage of the discharge pipe, backflow from the discharge pipe (rainwater, etc.), failure of the discharge pump, or blockage of the return pipe 25 cause the water level to rise from the normal water level, causing the floating body 1 to tilt more"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100348160-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the additional installation of the conveying pipe and the pump complicates the overall device structure, makes it difficult to quantify the sewage transfer, can cause the blockage of the pipe during long-term operation, and can not maintain the high water level due to the upper conveying pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100499785-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the controller 64 is difficult to supply water to the water tank 10 due to a failure of the pump 3a or a blockage of the reverse osmosis filter 7 when the lower limit water level detection signal is input for a predetermined time or more among the water level detection signals sh"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100540762-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the controller 64 is difficult to supply water to the water tank 10 due to a failure of the pump 3a or a blockage of the reverse osmosis filter 7 when the lower limit water level detection signal is input for a predetermined time or more among the water level detection signals sh"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100841664-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the fifth water level sensor 45 detects an overflow phenomenon that occurs when the water level in the electrolytic cell 30 is increased due to a blockage of the outlet 27a or the like, which is not drained or an increase in inflow from the storage tank 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101054375-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the fifth water level sensor 45 detects an overflow phenomenon that occurs when the water level in the electrolytic cell 30 is increased due to a blockage of the outlet port 27a or the like, which is not drained or an increase in inflow from the storage tank 20 increases"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101171869-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, when the pumping of the stream water 2 collected in the sump 120 continues while the collection efficiency of the screen 110 is lowered due to the blockage of the lower bed 4, the water level in the sump 120 is increased"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101220540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, when the water level in the pressure tank 314 is increased because the pressurized water does not flow smoothly into the flotation tank 200 due to the blockage of the microbubble injection unit 320, the water level sensor 334 detects the pump 312"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101272800-B1", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "the method of claim 1, the compressed air supply means provides a compressed air shock wave to the filtration filter according to the state of the reservoir tank level of the water level detector to eliminate the blockage of the filtration filter, or to provide a compressed air shock wave periodically or occasionally to prevent the blockage of the filtration filter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101272800-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the compressed air supply means provides a compressed air shock wave to the filtration filter according to the state of the reservoir tank level of the water level detector to eliminate the blockage of the filtration filter, or to provide a compressed air shock wave periodically or occasionally to prevent the blockage of the filtration filter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102490690-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "pipe blockage prediction system pipe blockage prediction system the present invention relates to a system for predicting pipe clogging, and more specifically, when a plurality of water level sensors are installed in a pipe through which sewage, sewage, rainwater, etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102490690-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it relates to a pipe blockage prediction system, a central control system that can predict the possibility of blockage in each section of the pipe by measuring the water level in each section of the pipe by utilizing the fact that the water level in the vicinity of the pipeline where sediment is accumulated and the water level rises"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102599308-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "in cases where the drainage function is lost due to blockage by various foreign substances, rainwater whose water level rises due to poor drainage treatment can be safely bypassed and treated to prevent flooding damage due to rainfall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200365284-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the controller 64 is difficult to supply water to the water tank 10 due to a failure of the pump 3a or a blockage of the reverse osmosis filter 7 when the lower limit water level detection signal is input for a predetermined time or more among the water level detection signals sh"}, {"pat_id": "US-7294257-B2", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "in this case, blockage of the mesh 13 will lead to reduction in the water level in the downstream container thus activating the float switch and pump 17"}]</data>
