r water level abnormal fall monitoring"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4297310-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "[0022] reservoir water level abnormal drop monitoring is intended to detect a sudden drop in the water level of a reservoir due to water leakage due to a distribution pipe accident or a large amount of water discharge due to a fire"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100932027-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in particular, the temporary storage tank of chemicals is formed by double walls of the outer wall and the inner wall so that even if the chemical exceeds the inner wall due to the malfunction of the water level control valve, it is protected by the outer wall as well as between the inner wall and the outer wall, that is, the leak detection sensor installed in the safety space"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100932027-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in particular, the temporary storage tank of chemicals is formed by double walls of the outer wall and the inner wall, so that even if the chemical exceeds the inner wall due to the malfunction of the automatic water level control valve, it is protected by the outer wall, and between the inner wall and the outer wall, that is, a leak detection sensor installed in the safety space"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100985209-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "for example, when a leak occurs in the water supply pipe 120, even if the water level of the water tank 130 continues to increase, the pressure sensor 140 may sense a low pressure"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100985209-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "by estimating the wide water level range, it is possible to increase the reliability of controlling the water level in the water tank, and also, if an error occurs in either the pressure sensor or the angle sensor, such as leakage into the water pipe, the control device does not malfunction by the other"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101000865-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, when the pressurized water tank reaches the minimum water level, the disk interlocked with the buckle automatically descends to close the flow path of the water cylinder connected to the water supply and drain pipe, thereby blocking the air pressure from leaking to the outside through the water supply and drain pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101114764-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, there are advantages in that various accidents such as fire and water leakage, which may be caused by malfunction of the water level sensor, may be prevented in advance"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101296571-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "the method of claim 3, the stopper is a water level sensor comprising a leak prevention packing to prevent leakage by contacting the water purification tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101408121-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the plurality of detection sensors may be different depending on the structure or form of the cold / hot water supply device 100, and may include, for example, a water level sensor 612, cold water (hot water) temperature sensors 624 and 634, (wire or the like) sensor signal receiver 740 receives signals from the plurality of sensor sensors 640, 660, a water leakage sensor 670, one or more overflow sensors 690, can do"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102554668-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "will leak control unit 112 is configured to cause ro pump 450 to stop pumping if empty level switch 350a in tank 350 detects air or a critically low water level"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200428182-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "5 does not form a conduit in the main body because the motor is installed outside, and in addition to the water level measurement tube 220, a separate tube is not formed in order to prevent leakage of pressure from the outside"}, {"pat_id": "US-10184221-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the event of a leak of the impoundment area, if the water level observed is falling relatively quickly and unrelated to the operation of the water control device for gate/weir movement, this could alert a user that the area needs to be checked for an impoundment leak such as the breach of a impoundment wall"}, {"pat_id": "US-10480824-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "further, water (either from a leak condition or a non-leak condition (condensation)) may accumulate in the bottom pan 200 and trigger the leak sensor 1200 when the water level in the bottom pan 200 rises approximately by the distance d (e.g., the elevation of the sensor channel 602) from the base 202 of the bottom pan 200"}, {"pat_id": "US-10480824-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "accordingly, water that accumulates in the bottom pan may contact the leak sensor 1200 via the opening at the bottom portion 1195 of the sensor housing 1000 when the water level rises to the elevation at which the leak sensor 1200 is disposed in the sensor channel 1102"}, {"pat_id": "US-5467640-A", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "(k) determine that the pipeline segment thus tested is leak free if stability of the water level is positive or leaking if the water level recedes into the pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "US-6627073-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "if the water level in the area on the uppermost stream side in the electrolytic tank is controlled in a predetermined range, as in the claim 16, therefore, it is possible to more reliably prevent the water from leaking from the electrolytic tank"}, {"pat_id": "US-9709431-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "for example, the application server 170 may receive information from neighboring properties that indicate that both sump pumps are turned on but the water level is high, which may indicate that major water leak may be impacting both properties"}, {"pat_id": "US-9709431-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in this example, if the rain sensor indicates that there is no local precipitation, but that there are water levels above a threshold, the control system 100 may track property operations to determine if there is a problematic operation that may be causing water leakage within the property"}, {"pat_id": "US-9950935-B2",