  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "JP-2780720-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, when the water level of the pair of water level sensors installed in the snow channel changes, the blockage of the two water level sensors is determined by judging which of the three types of the fluctuations is the above-described pattern"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2780720-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, since fluctuations in the water level are also observed in other water level monitoring panels in the system, the overall system determines the blockage position in units of sections where water level sensors are installed by comprehensively judging the detection results of each water level monitoring panel"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2780720-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "also, in consideration of the degree of water level difference between the two points, the absolute water level of each water level sensor, etc., the urgency of the water level rise due to blockage is divided into, for example, three stages, and only the alarm lamp is turned on in the first stage"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7183463-B1", "para_id": "para_40", "text": "for example, the monitoring device 200 uses the measurement data of the sensor devices 210 distributed in the a block to calculate the dynamic water level at each location in the a block"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0137696-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "moreover, the method of checking the low water level in the water tank by using the air tank is very conventional, and it only functions to block the flow of water only when the water is almost full in the water tank, thereby making it difficult to identify the low water amount in the water tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100540762-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the controller 64 is difficult to supply water to the water tank 10 due to a failure of the pump 3a or a blockage of the reverse osmosis filter 7 when the lower limit water level detection signal is input for a predetermined time or more among the water level detection signals sh"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100546851-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the control unit 90, when the second filter material 22a of the second filter tank 20 is blocked and the water level is increased, the water flows back through the overflow pipe 45, and this is applied to the detection signal of the second water level sensor 22b"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100546851-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the control unit 90 is blocked by the second filter material 22a of the second filter tank 20 when the water level is increased, the water flows back through the overflow pipe 45, by the detection signal of the second water level sensor 22b the operation of the inflow pump 70 is stopped"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100556994-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "automatic backwashing device is to prevent the waste of chemicals by shutting off the operation of chemical feeder by blocking the inflow of raw water when the basin maintains the water level"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100654756-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the amount of sewage flowing into the collecting manhole, that is, when the water level changes, the elevating member blocks all of the drainage holes of the fixing plate, thereby preventing the sewage from flowing back to the road through the collecting manhole"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100706118-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "due to this replenishment, when the water level in the brine reservoir 5 reaches the upper limit, the electric valve 11 is automatically closed to block the supply of water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100727599-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the overflow prevention process by the water level adjusting apparatus of the present invention is largely, the first blocking step of first blocking the inflow of raw water into the purified water tank 500 by a mechanical opening and closing structure when the water level of the purified water tank 500 is full"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100992828-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the water level of the wastewater introduced into the water treatment tank 110 rises above the water level detection sensor 200, the water level detection sensor 200 blocks the wastewater inlet 112a to prevent the inflow of wastewater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101000865-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, when the pressurized water tank reaches the minimum water level, the disk interlocked with the buckle automatically descends to close the flow path of the water cylinder connected to the water supply and drain pipe, thereby blocking the air pressure from leaking to the outside through the water supply and drain pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101014995-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the amount of water increases, the water level sensor detects and opens the initial rainwater blocking door to remove the foreign matter from the primary strainer after collecting the rainwater from the primary strainer, filter it once more from the strainer, and then remove the foreign substance in the sedimentation chamber for final precipitation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101039196-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "this structure is to block the inflow of the initial excellent water when the internal water level of the first excellent soil chamber 21 and the second excellent soil chamber 31 is increased due to the continuous inflow of the initial excellent rain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101044802-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the water level in the brine reservoir 5 reaches the upper limit due to the water supply and replenishment, the electric valve 11 is automatically closed to block the supply of direct water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101051656-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, water is supplied from the water storage container to the spray generator through the water supply valve, and when an appropriate amount of water is supplied to the spray generator, the water level control means rises by buoyancy and blocks the water supply valve so that water is no longer sprayed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101118626-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "2 is a block diagram of a wireless receiver in a wireless automatic water level controller having a communication distance extension function according to the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101202895-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "such a structure is intended to block the inflow of the initial excellent water when the water level of the septic tank 30 reaches the full water level due to the continuous inflow of the initial excellent water level"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101215187-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the high water level alarm sensor 46 is a water level of the sewage and rainwater in the chamber 12 of the collecting facility 10 above the limit point because the sewage pipe 16 is not blocked in the rain due to a malfunction of the first water level detection sensor 42"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101220540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, when the water level in the pressure tank 314 is increased because the pressurized water does not flow smoothly into the flotation tank 200 due to the blockage of the microbubble injection unit 320, the water level sensor 334 detects the pump 312"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101254083-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the water level of the groundwater well is changed according to the operation of the water pump (m), the sewage blocking air valve 40 is kept open so that air flows in and out of the groundwater, and the groundwater pollution prevention device is flooded by flooding or the like"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101258565-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the rainwater introduced into the rainwater chamber 10 is increased in quantity and gradually increased in water level to reach the moving induction plate 300 installed in the sewage inlet 22 and the blocking plate 260"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101323649-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "first, if rainwater is supplied through the inlet 1 of the single finishing block 20, it is stored while maintaining the same water level in the entire pipeline while flowing along the curved pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101388033-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the water level of the sewage stored in the tank 30 rises and the height of the buckle member 54 increases, the wire 56b is pulled up by the load of the sensing block 56c and the sensing block 56c is lowered"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101388033-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "if the water level of the sewage is continuously increased, the bure member 54 is raised and the sensing block 56c is lowered, so that the sensing block 56c is the fourth contact sensor 58d, the third contact sensor 58c, and the second"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101439225-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in this case, as the water level l measured by the water level sensor 31 increases or decreases, the amount of the contaminants blocked by the screen member also increases or decreases proportionally to the internal water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101588396-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "on the other hand, when the float valve 16 is closed by the buoy 17, the water level of the dirt increases due to the dirt that flows into the dirt collection vehicle, thereby blocking the movement of the air and further preventing the dirt from being introduced into the collection vehicle"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101996050-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the above-mentioned prior art patents, the open / close plate is provided as a buoyant body, and when the internal water level is raised by the inflow of sewage, the open / close plate is rotated to block the manhole entrance to prevent the backwashing of sewage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101996050-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a backflow preventing plate (70) for blocking an upper and lower space instantaneously as the end portion is brought into close contact with the stopper (51) of the tubular body (50) while rotating at a predetermined angle according to the water level flowing into the manhole body (10)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102008815-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the above-mentioned patent of the prior art, the opening and closing plate is provided as a buoyancy body to increase the internal water level by the inflow of sewage so that the opening and closing plate rotates to block the manhole inlet to prevent backflow of sewage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102008815-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a backflow prevention plate 70 which allows the upper and lower spaces to be blocked at the moment when the end is in close contact with the stopper 51 of the tubular body 50 while rotating at a predetermined angle according to the water level flowing into the manhole body 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102053107-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "on the other hand, while the rain odor blocking member 320 maintains the closed state, when the rainwater rises in the pipeline due to excessive rain, such as rainy season, the rainwater flows back from the pipeline, the water level in the pipeline rises"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102087796-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "according to one disclosure, in block 102, the sewage water level adjusting apparatus 100 may calculate the rate of increase of the amount of sewage introduced into the first intermediate reservoir and the amount of introduced sewage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102087796-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "according to one disclosure, in block 103, the sewage water level adjusting apparatus 100 may determine, based on an increase rate of the amount of sewage, whether or not the introduced sewage amount exceeds the sewage storage threshold of the first intermediate reservoir as three levels"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102149596-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "the emergency monitoring terminal has an effect of blocking the rise of the water level when the electronic equipment malfunctions by including a buoyancy type inlet water level meter 150 having a mechanical configuration while sharing a water level meter by electronic sensing together with a constant monitoring terminal"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102399564-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the gate 20 not only collects an appropriate amount of sewage or rainwater by opening and closing the inlet, but also blocks the pressure from being transmitted into the collecting pipe due to the rise of the water level in the conduit during flooding to prevent damage to the collecting pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102400040-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the water level of the treated water tank is measured in real time, and when the water level is out of a certain range, the gate valve is selectively opened and closed to block the flow path of the overflow pipe, thereby increasing the overflow height of the treatment tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102595204-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the evaporator tray 1125 further comprises an evaporator tray water level sensor 1171 arranged to detect when the water level in the evaporator tray 1125 is above a predefined maximum water level, thereby causing the drain 1125b to be at least partially it will display that you are blocked"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102595218-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the evaporator tray 1125 further comprises an evaporator tray water level sensor 1171 arranged to detect when the water level in the evaporator tray 1125 is above a predefined maximum water level, thereby causing the drain 1125b to be at least partially it will display that you are blocked"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102595234-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the evaporator tray 1125 further comprises an evaporator tray water level sensor 1171 arranged to detect when the water level in the evaporator tray 1125 is above a predefined maximum water level, thereby causing the drain 1125b to be at least partially it will display that you are blocked"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102683587-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, it is characterized by controlling and managing the operation of the pump by deriving the most stable and efficient optimal drainage reservoir, water level of the manhole, operating conditions of the pump, inlet pressure, and discharge pressure for each block, reservoir, customer, and manhole"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102683587-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the operation of the pump is controlled and managed by deriving the most stable and efficient optimal water level in the reservoir for each block and customer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102794732-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "if the electrolytic water generator continues to be used while the second feed water passage or the second outlet is blocked, the second outlet is immediately filled with the gas generated in the second electrode chamber, and the water level in the second outlet is lowered"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102807029-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the control unit can block the inflow of water before the equipment inside the main body housing (10) is affected by the inflow of water through the water level sensor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200145021-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "2 is a block diagram of a water purifier to which the water level deviation preventing device of the purified water tank according to the present invention is applied"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200328661-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "if the treated water is stored in the backwash tank and the water level falls below a certain level during non-operating, it falls down due to the weight of the stopper 9 to block the flow path of the treated water so that the water in the pump head does not empty"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200332116-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at this time, when the water tank level is a high water level, the flow of water is blocked by the float 42 and the pressure valve 43, so that the current of the pump motor increases without being stabilized as shown in fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200351993-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, when the water level of the sewage collected in the manhole is increased due to excessive sewage or heavy rain in the manhole, the level of the sewage is increased and the cover blocking the discharge hole rises due to the sewage level so that the slope is forcibly opened"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200359449-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, when the water level is above a certain level, the ball tower 30 floats due to the buoyancy of the water to block the water intake pipe 32"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200361466-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "bad smell intercepting apparatus of rain and dirty water receiver the present invention relates to a malodor blocking device of a rainwater receiver, and more particularly, to increase the water level and to increase the water level at the discharge end of the openable malodor blocking device such that the water pressure pushes the opening door"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200425676-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the water level in the water tank 40 reaches a predetermined height, the float 56 serves to block the water inlet pipe 50 while rising upward according to the water level"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200427833-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when water level is measured by sensor detection while blocking the inflow of floating garbage, it automatically adjusts the rainwater inflow switch to block the inflow"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200442330-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "more specifically, when the purified water is filled to the water level set in the purified water storage tank (pressure tank), the automatic shut off valve for the water purification system can automatically block the inflow of raw water to the purified water filter due to the pressure"}]</data>
