  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "JP-5042805-B2", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "specifically, when the water level gauge 111 detects that the water level in the contaminant removal tank 110 is higher than the specified water level, control is performed to relatively increase the amount of water transferred by the advection pump 122, and the contamination level is also increased"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5042805-B2", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "for example, in the case of the water level gauge 111 having a configuration in which an on signal is output when the water level of the contaminant removal tank 110 exceeds a prescribed water level defined in advance and an off signal is outputted when the water level falls below the prescribed water level, the amount of effluent water can be derived from the time when the off signal switches"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100510269-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "into the flow rate adjustment tank 30 in a state in which the coarse contaminant is filtered and removed while passing through), and when the water level detection sensor 33 of the flow adjustment tank 30 detects the water level, the raw water pump 31 according to the detected signal"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100673536-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "on the other hand, since the holes 22 of the storm duct 20 are formed to be below the normal water level of the second accommodation chamber 11b, relocation of the contaminants suspended through the holes 22 and their backflow is prevented"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100674176-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "since the second filtration system 40 is relatively small and runs for a long time, it filters out contaminants as much as possible, enters the filtered water into the water level control tank 10 and consequently returns it to the swimming pool"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100823240-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, the pressure gauge detects and measures the pressure caused by the initial excellent or sediment contaminants in the initial excellent treatment facility 1, and performs the detection step, and the level gauge detects the initial excellent water level in the initial excellent treatment facility 1 the measurement is performed to detect"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100823240-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, when the initial rainwater and sediment contaminants are completely excluded from the initial rainwater treatment facility 1 and the pressure or water level becomes zero, the drain pump 21 receiving the water is driven to operate the water tank 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100958442-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, the conventional non-point contaminant purification device of the initial excellent excellent outflow water is the final outflow pipe line 21 only after the rainwater received in the median filling tank 13 and the settling tank 14 of the initial excellent purification tank 10 becomes the full water level"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101130918-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the present invention by installing the filtration device 200 in the position as described above, the contaminants in the water discharged through the drain pipe 120 from the swimming pool to be filtered immediately before passing through the water level control tank (300)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101223419-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "if the water is not inhaled because it is located above the water level, and the water is introduced into the well where the water-soluble contaminant and the water are mixed, the lower end of the nozzle 140 is submerged into the water-soluble contaminant in the well, thereby recovering the light-water pollutant"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101306120-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is characterized in that the anti-pollution cap is configured to be coupled to the upper side of the casing to support the water level sensor to prevent contaminants from entering the ground"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101311288-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the drainage pump is provided with a water level sensor to drain the stagnant water while the position of the sediment detector descends to the settled contaminant surface"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101322190-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "therefore, when the purified treatment water from which the contaminants have been removed through the purification treatment water recovery pipe 140 provided in the internal treatment tank 200 of the present invention is recovered, the amount corresponding to the purification treatment water by the water level detection means and the control unit 600"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101383594-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "according to the variable water level screen filter according to the present invention, since the filtration position is changed according to the water level, the contact between the contaminants accumulated on the bottom of the reservoir can be effectively prevented, and the treatment efficiency of sewage can be increased"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101439225-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in this case, as the water level l measured by the water level sensor 31 increases or decreases, the amount of the contaminants blocked by the screen member also increases or decreases proportionally to the internal water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101741449-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "that is, if the operating time of the filtration tank is increased, the flow rate of the flow of the rainwater or the flow rate of the treated water is lowered due to the increase of the amount of contaminants collected in the lcd artificial floating filter media, or the water level of the tank before the rainwater is increased do"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200314265-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, when the water level of the water channel 10 rises due to rain or the like, the flow rate increases so that the inflow amount of the contaminant 40 increases, so the removal speed of the contaminant 40 should also proceed rapidly in proportion to the inflow of water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200314265-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as such, by automatically controlling the driving speed of the lifting motor 26 in several stages according to the water level of the water channel 10, water flows in the water channel 10 so that the contaminants 40 can be quickly removed when the water level suddenly blows in rainy weather"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200323476-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "into the flow rate adjustment tank 30 in a state in which the coarse contaminant is filtered and removed while passing through), and when the water level detection sensor 33 of the flow adjustment tank 30 detects the water level, the raw water pump 31 according to the detected signal"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200326076-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "since the second filtration system 40 is relatively small and runs for a long time, it filters out contaminants as much as possible, enters the filtered water into the water level control tank 10 and consequently returns it to the swimming pool"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200361427-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "on the other hand, since the holes 22 of the storm duct 20 are formed to be below the normal water level of the second accommodation chamber 11b, relocation of the contaminants suspended through the holes 22 and their backflow is prevented"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200420116-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in other words, the water level detector 12 is to operate the contaminant processing unit 40 only when the waste water reaches a constant level in the inflow chamber 10 to prevent unnecessary waste of power"}]</data>
</edge>
