  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "EP-0448924-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "example 5 1400 l of wastewater with an initial concentration of 0.01% nmmo and 0.02% softening were fed with the pre-pressure pump 4 via the heat exchanger 5, which ensured that a temperature of 30 c"}, {"pat_id": "EP-1565408-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "after the lower layer 23 has thus been heated to the desired temperature, the pump 7 can be activated for pumping water from the pit 4 through the heat exchanger to the evaporator"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5374527-B2", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "if only the operation of the pump 23 is stopped while the operation of the electrolysis unit 25 is continued during intermittent discharge, the electrolysis electrode is not cooled, and the temperature of the electrolysis electrode and the raw material water rises"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6819735-B1", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "the cold water in the pit 44 is supplied to the refrigerator main body 21 via the pump 45 and the pipe 46, and heats are exchanged to raise the temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100634761-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, when it is determined that the communication state is good, the temperature data of the water tank together with the ambient temperature data (which can determine the possibility of freezing of the water pipe, measured by the temperature sensor) and (if the pump abnormality can be determined) preferably, a current sensor is further provided to control the pump using the current data supplied to the pump"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100901209-B1", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "a freeze protection driver for intermittently driving a pump to prevent freezing of the water supply pipe when the outside air temperature sensed by the temperature sensor is equal to or less than a reference value"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100901209-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "according to this aspect of the present invention, the water supply control device checks the outside air temperature sensed by the temperature sensor and intermittently drives the pump to prevent freezing of the water supply pipe supplying water to the water tank of the drain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100901209-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, when the outside air temperature falls below the reference value through the temperature sensor 270, the water supply control device 200 intermittently drives the pump 220 to prevent freezing of the water supply pipe 230"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100901209-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "if the outside air temperature falls below the reference value, the pump control unit 250 controls the operation of the freezing prevention driving unit 254"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100908201-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the sludge preventing and freezing prevention apparatus of the present invention installed as described above, when the temperature of the water is lower than the predetermined temperature, the water supply pipe 20 is opened by the operation of the high pressure pump 30 while the water supply pipe 10 is opened with the automatic opening and closing valve 50"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100970425-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at this time, the operation of the boiler 341 is stopped and the high temperature steam obtained by the operation of the heat pump 340 is blocked by blocking the inflow of water vapor through the boiler 341 to prevent the backflow of the boiler 341"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101707178-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the present invention also provides a method and system for monitoring the supply of groundwater and the groundwater condition by real-time checking of the groundwater level by measuring the groundwater level, temperature, pollution level and pumping flow rate of the groundwater channel,"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102065694-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "if the temperature measured by the temperature sensor 270 provided in the controller 250 is below a specific temperature, the freezing prevention function is performed in a manner of operating the discharge pump 200 for a specific time at a predetermined specific period"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102073704-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "sludge solubilization device for the pre-treatment is additionally provided, the heat exchanger is configured to reduce fouling in a heat exchange method in which a heat exchanger and a heat pump are connected to maintain a constant sludge temperature of the heat exchanger by a heat pump"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102082802-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "next, the control unit 200 calculates the influence value (a4) due to membrane contamination in a predetermined manner by using the calculated pretreatment filter, the water temperature, and the influence values (a1, a2, a3) due to the osmotic pressure and the initial expected pump operation rate"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102578604-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the first, second, and third coolant pump control units (240, 250, and 260) receive electrolysis reactor temperature data measured from the electrolysis reactor temperature sensor 140, and when the electrolysis reactor temperature is higher than the set temperature, the first coolant pump (p1), serves to operate the second coolant pump (p2) and the third coolant pump (p3)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102809593-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "for example, cavitation occurs when the pressure of the water flowing inside the pump becomes lower than the saturated vapor pressure of the water at that temperature and pressure, causing partial vaporization of the water, creating bubbles"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200415940-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "such a freeze protection method by the circulation pump 90 is electric compared to the freeze protection method that prevents freezing of the water supply line by applying heat when the water supply line falls below a predetermined temperature by winding the entire water supply line applied to a conventional water supply fountain with a heating wire"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200415940-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, since the temperature sensor 80 and the circulation pump 90 are installed in the water supply line 20 of the present invention, the water supply line 20 can be freely prevented from freezing in winter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200430484-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is introduced by itself while maintaining the same water quality and the same water temperature at the time of intake, and at the same time prevents the contamination of the groundwater system, and simultaneously withdraws and pumps the water automatically"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200430484-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is introduced by itself while maintaining the same water quality and the same water temperature at the time of intake, and at the same time prevents the contamination of the groundwater system, and at the same time automatically takes in and pumps the water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200433469-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "control setting part the present invention relates to a simple abnormality of water, and more specifically, when the ambient temperature drops below 0 c and there is a possibility of freezing of water pipes, a water intake pump that drives water from underground pipes and the like is driven for a predetermined time interval"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200433469-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and a freeze blocker configured to control an operation state of the intake pump according to a preset operating condition for freezing prevention of the water pipe when the outside air temperature is detected below the set temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-10914393-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "conventional hot water balancing systems and shutoff valves have centered on the timely delivery of hot water without wasting water while waiting for hot water to arrive to a user, or avoiding excessive energy usage by recirculation pumps, or avoiding scalding a user by limiting the exposure to water above a safe temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-10981818-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the higher wattage and overcapacity of the heating element is preferred to ensure that the chamber temperature is maintained because the air pump would bring in cold air in very cold or freezing weather"}, {"pat_id": "US-11761838-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "when the temperature distribution in equipment such as pumps, rotors, compressors and turbines changes or when the temperature ranges exceed normal values, the nanoparticles based sensors can alert and prevent breakage and down time of the asset"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "after turning on the pump and allowing the hot water to flow through the first set of pipelines in the first loop on the property for the period of time, checking a temperature of all floors of the property to determine if there is a noticeable increase in temperature of a particular floor anywhere on the property"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "claim_8", "text": "after turning on the recirculation pump and allowing the hot water to flow through the first set of pipelines in the first loop on the property for the period of time, checking a temperature of all floors of the property to determine if there is a noticeable increase in temperature of a particular floor anywhere on the property"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "after turning on the pump and allowing the hot water to flow through the first set of pipelines in the first loop on the property for the period of time, the method may include checking a temperature of all floors of the property to determine if there is a noticeable increase in temperature of a particular floor anywhere on the property"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "after turning on the recirculation pump and allowing the hot water to flow through the first set of pipelines in the first loop on the property for the period of time, checking a temperature of all floors of the property to determine if there is a noticeable increase in temperature of a particular floor anywhere on the property"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at step 1712, after turning on the recirculation pump 180 and allowing the hot water to flow through the first set of pipelines 114 in the first loop on the property 104 for the period of time, checking a temperature of all floors of the property 104 to determine if there is a noticeable increase in temperature of a particular floor anywhere on the property 104"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at step 1812, the method includes checking a temperature of all floors of the property 104 to determine if there is a noticeable increase in temperature of a particular floor anywhere on the property 104 after turning on the pump 180 and allowing the hot water to flow through the first set of pipelines 114 in the first loop on the property 104 for the period of time"}, {"pat_id": "US-4243522-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and 6 p.m., it is possible to use the waste water as a source of heat for a heat pump, the temperature of the waste water being sufficiently high that it can be reduced, such as by 5 c., without a risk of freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-8141584-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the temperature of the water in the storage tank falls below a specified temperature for a specified period of time, thereby indicating that the possibility of freezing exists, the microprocessor activates the pump to dump water from the storage tank through the alternate outlet to the alternate destination"}, {"pat_id": "US-9370746-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, when a pressure pump that delivers supply water to the ro membrane module is operated at a constant operating pressure, a water volume of produced permeate water (pure water) becomes mailer than a required production volume of water, when a temperature of supply water is low or when a membrane is blocked"}]</data>
