40-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, when the initial rainwater and sediment contaminants are completely excluded from the initial rainwater treatment facility 1 and the pressure or water level becomes zero, the drain pump 21 receiving the water is driven to operate the water tank 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101004130-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "water level control system water level controll system the present invention relates to a water level control system, and more particularly, it is possible to prevent the contamination of groundwater by sealing the upper part of the groundwater well as well as to control the operation of the pump by sensing the water pressure formed in the upper part of the groundwater well"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101036584-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the water level of the sludge storage tank 100 increases above a predetermined level, the flow rate controller 110 increases the output of the transfer pump 107 to increase the flow amount of sludge transferred to the cavitation storage tank 120, and the sludge storage tank 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101113083-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in addition, the pump well 46 operates the transfer pump when a certain water level is reached while storing the treated water discharged from the organic material decay reaction tank 40"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101113090-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the pump well 46 is provided with a transfer pump that operates when the predetermined water level is reached while storing the treated water discharged from the organic material decay reaction tank 40"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101113090-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in addition, the pump well 46 operates the transfer pump when a certain water level is reached while storing the treated water discharged from the organic material decay reaction tank 40"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101171869-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, when the pumping of the stream water 2 collected in the sump 120 c