  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100733608-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "third, the internal space of sewage separation pipe is almost completely separated from the internal space of sewage culverts, which prevents the mixing of sewage and rainwater in sewage culverts in rainy weather, thus preventing stream contamination and improving the water quality of the water flowing into the sewage treatment plant"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100763800-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, if the water is confined to a certain place for a long time, the contamination is further increased by the material decomposition and material binding action, so that the water stored in the reservoir is always kept at the full water level and water flowing from the upstream through the lower part of the sluice gate"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100763800-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "actions increase water contamination, but confine water using a bottom drainage reservoir configured to discharge a large amount of water from the upstream of the stream through the bottom of the reservoir, i.e., the bottom of the drainage sluice"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101042852-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "actions increase water contamination, but confine water using a bottom drainage reservoir configured to discharge a large amount of water from the upstream of the stream through the bottom of the reservoir, i.e., the bottom of the drainage sluice"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101067632-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "of the reservoir or river prevents turbid water diffusion that prevents contamination of the reservoir or stream so that it is economically appropriately blocked before it spreads inward, so that only clean water from which the soil and contaminants have been removed from the turbid water flows into the reservoir or stream to prevent contamination"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101802534-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "by maintaining the adsorbent material in the biological reactor 202 or other upstream of the membrane operating system 204, the suspended-media membrane biological reactor system minimizes the possibility of contamination and / or wear of the membrane operating system tank membrane by the adsorbent material, remove"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101895031-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "or deposits that accumulate over time in channels such as canals need to be removed for contamination of the stream or formation of an appropriate flow path"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101946554-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "according to the early stormwater treatment system according to the prior art, the initial stormwater having a high pollution level is discharged to the secondary tank through the gypsum, and when the amount of stormwater is increased, it is possible to prevent contamination of streams by flowing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102224305-B1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "the system 100 of the present invention uses a siphon principle to circulate water while discharging water and sludge from the compensation stream to the downstream, but it is also significant in separating and discharging the water in a specific section with high contamination in the compensation stream before diffusion"}, {"pat_id": "US-10464021-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "accordingly, the systems disclosed herein can include a decontamination apparatus (e.g., outlets and inlets designed to remove and replace draw stream or diluted draw stream"}, {"pat_id": "US-5958240-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "waste streams can be treated with a de-chelation chamber that effectively removes high levels of organics and bacterial contamination"}, {"pat_id": "US-8961793-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "further, storm drains often are designed to not enter conventional wastewater treatment plants and directly enter open streams or the oceans, resulting in widespread outbreaks of disease, heavy metals contamination, and suspended solids, which adversely affect wildlife and human beings"}]</data>
