  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100767754-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "\u2465 there is a problem that there is no blocking function when harmful substances spill out of the upstream basin due to accidents such as overturning the amount of oil"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101067632-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "of the reservoir or river prevents turbid water diffusion that prevents contamination of the reservoir or stream so that it is economically appropriately blocked before it spreads inward, so that only clean water from which the soil and contaminants have been removed from the turbid water flows into the reservoir or stream to prevent contamination"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101147332-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, the existing dams and bore streams or rivers are blocked by concrete structures and used for water or power generation.however, there is an excessive amount of co 2 (0.9 ton per ton of cement) due to cement production and an ecosystem caused by heavy metals such as cr +8"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101238571-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the cleaning operation, by installing the upstream order wall 10 to block the inflow of river water and drain the water of the cleaning section, the water is exposed in the low area of the puddle while the riverbed is exposed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101239754-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "first, when the sewage flows from the upstream to the downstream to the sewer pipe 100, the sewage in the direction of the sewer pipe 100 by using the water gate 80 formed in the inlet pipe 10 and the discharge pipe 50 blocking the flow and the sewage stream upstream of the sewer pipe 100 is communicated with the sewer pipe 100 downstream through the discharge pipe 50 via the sedimentation facility 30 through the inlet pipe 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101282720-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in the reservoir collection block 10 provided in the present invention, the water in a small stream or wetland or ground water flowing through the water according to the structure of the terrain is often required to purify due to environmental pollution"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101384971-B1", "para_id": "para_54", "text": "the water-expert system using the expert system to determine whether to supply fresh air to the lower part of the stream or to temporarily block dams entering the coastal waters, and then notify the management center"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102028873-B1", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "a lower support pipe configured at a lower end of the front river water inlet control block on the one side and the other side, while adjusting the front stream water inlet control block up and down, the river water inlet control cylinder for opening and closing the lower portion of the river water inlet is configured in the lower front portion of the front sluice plate"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102187983-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "in addition, it has a significant effect of fundamentally blocking the red tide phenomenon that occurs when contaminated river water generated in the land stream flows into the sea"}, {"pat_id": "US-10329171-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "additionally, permeate streams from various treatment blocks 260 may be blended together, and may be blended with untreated filtered seawater from the blend/bypass line 225 to produce water having predefined water-characteristic tolerances"}, {"pat_id": "US-10329171-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "additionally, this process may continue for as many treatment blocks 260 as there are in the treatment system 200, until a final permeate stream, optionally having untreated filtered seawater water blended therein, is produced from a final membrane pressure vessel"}, {"pat_id": "US-10329171-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "4a-b, the filtered seawater may be provided to a treatment block 260 and either sent through blend/bypass line 225 or pumped by variable speed high-pressure pump 212, which pushes the filtered seawater through to one or more membrane pressure vessels (e.g., 214, 216, and 218), thereby creating a permeate stream and a concentrate stream"}, {"pat_id": "US-10329171-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "6a-b, a system and/or method of the present invention may be configured so that the variable speed high-pressure pump 212 pushes the filtered seawater 611 through one or more treatment blocks, thereby creating a concentrate stream 634 and a permeate stream (not shown)"}, {"pat_id": "US-10329171-B2", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "9, seawater treatment system 900 may include a treatment block 960 that may process and treat water from a water intake system 901 and produce a permeate stream and a concentrate stream, or multiple streams"}, {"pat_id": "US-10329171-B2", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "for example, in one or more embodiments, water taken in by the water intake system 901 may be treated in the treatment block 960 to produce a product water stream having a specific salinity and/or hardness"}, {"pat_id": "US-10343118-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "additionally, permeate streams from various treatment blocks 260 may be blended together, and may be blended with untreated filtered seawater from the blend/bypass line 225 to produce water having predefined water-characteristic tolerances"}, {"pat_id": "US-10343118-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "additionally, this process may continue for as many treatment blocks 260 as there are in the treatment system 200, until a final permeate stream, optionally having untreated filtered seawater water blended therein, is produced from a final membrane pressure vessel"}, {"pat_id": "US-10343118-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "4a-b, the filtered seawater may be provided to a treatment block 260 and either sent through blend/bypass line 225 or pumped by variable speed high-pressure pump 212, which pushes the filtered seawater through to one or more membrane pressure vessels (e.g., 214, 216, and 218), thereby creating a permeate stream and a concentrate stream"}, {"pat_id": "US-10343118-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "6a-b, a system and/or method of the present invention may be configured so that the variable speed high-pressure pump 212 pushes the filtered seawater 611 through one or more treatment blocks, thereby creating a concentrate stream 634 and a permeate stream (not shown)"}, {"pat_id": "US-10704740-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the closed state, the barrier may completely block the fluid passageway to prevent a fluid stream received by the valve input 40 from being output from the valve output 42 to the outlet 12"}, {"pat_id": "US-10704740-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in an embodiment, at block 306, the fluid stream received in block 304 is output through the outlet which was fixed to the pipeline in block 302"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "if, in block 8016, the system 6000 is not in a production start-up state, in block 8020 the target temperature for the blowdown process stream exiting the blowdown heat exchanger 6008b may be set to the desired temperature determined in block 8014"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "if, in block 8016, the system 6000 is not in a production start-up state, in block 8020 the target temperature for the blowdown process stream exiting the blowdown heat exchanger 6008b may be set to the desired temperature determined in block 8014"}, {"pat_id": "US-12492132-B2", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "blockages to prevent blockages, a mesh with smaller openings than the open area of a static nozzle or the smallest opening in an adjustable nozzle must be in place upstream of the the open area of a static nozzle or the smallest opening in an adjustable nozzle"}, {"pat_id": "US-5988188-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, the forwardly directed stream from the nozzle 19 is particularly useful in creating an initial opening through a blockage caused by most materials"}, {"pat_id": "US-5988188-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, if access to the sewer line is provided upstream of the obstruction, use of a nozzle such as nozzle 18 to clear a small opening through the blockage, and allow the flow through the obstruction and on down the sewer, enables use of the nozzle 20 without concern that the area between the nozzle and the obstruction will become flooded"}, {"pat_id": "US-5988188-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "for example, plugs may be positioned both upstream of the nozzle and downstream of the obstruction for blocking flow from upstream in the sewer line and creating a flow restriction downstream of the obstruction"}, {"pat_id": "US-6420185-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "on-line monitoring can then begin by shifting the four-way selector valve 182 to block the flow of the zero stream 184 and allow the flow of concentrate stream 116 to the analyzer 122, as shown in fig"}, {"pat_id": "US-6725717-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "detecting by the strain gauge the presence of any strain changes in the pipeline at the selected position caused by the pressure changes and determining therefrom whether the blockage is upstream or downstream of the selected position"}, {"pat_id": "US-6725717-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "by using very sensitive but readily available bonded resistance strain gauges , it can determine if there are pressure changes in the pipeline, thereby indicating whether there is blockage upstream or downstream of the test site"}, {"pat_id": "US-6725717-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "once the direction of the blockage has been ascertained, that is whether the strain gauge is upstream or downstream of the blockage, the gauge can be removed from the outside of the pipeline and the pipeline s external coating repaired (if necessary)"}, {"pat_id": "US-6725717-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "pressures in the pipeline on an upstream side 9 of the blockage can be increased or lowered but do not readily transmit or do not transmit at all to the down stream side 12 of the blockage"}]</data>
</edge>
