  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "EP-0576981-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the sensor 51 also gives the possibility that when the water level in the washing chamber 21 drops, for example due to leakage losses, the vacuum blower 36 can be switched on again in order to compensate for these leakage losses and to always have a fully filled washing chamber available for washing processes"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3309310-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as a result, contamination in the storage space can be effectively avoided by always takes place with sinking water level in the rain overflow basin, a backflow of water from the storage space to the pelvic chamber"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3309310-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "a certain water level difference in this case indicates a reduced flow of water between the pelvic chamber 5 and the storage space 10 via the retaining elements 11, wherein contamination of the retaining elements 11 can be concluded"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100673536-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "on the other hand, since the holes 22 of the storm duct 20 are formed to be below the normal water level of the second accommodation chamber 11b, relocation of the contaminants suspended through the holes 22 and their backflow is prevented"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101014995-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the amount of water increases, the water level sensor detects and opens the initial rainwater blocking door to remove the foreign matter from the primary strainer after collecting the rainwater from the primary strainer, filter it once more from the strainer, and then remove the foreign substance in the sedimentation chamber for final precipitation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101039196-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "this structure is to block the inflow of the initial excellent water when the internal water level of the first excellent soil chamber 21 and the second excellent soil chamber 31 is increased due to the continuous inflow of the initial excellent rain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101215187-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the high water level alarm sensor 46 is a water level of the sewage and rainwater in the chamber 12 of the collecting facility 10 above the limit point because the sewage pipe 16 is not blocked in the rain due to a malfunction of the first water level detection sensor 42"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101258565-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the rainwater introduced into the rainwater chamber 10 is increased in quantity and gradually increased in water level to reach the moving induction plate 300 installed in the sewage inlet 22 and the blocking plate 260"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102794732-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "if the electrolytic water generator continues to be used while the second feed water passage or the second outlet is blocked, the second outlet is immediately filled with the gas generated in the second electrode chamber, and the water level in the second outlet is lowered"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102794732-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as a result, electrolysis in the electrolytic chamber (40) is stopped, and further decrease in the water level in the second outlet (13) is suppressed, so that damage to the diaphragm (43) can be suppressed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200361427-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "on the other hand, since the holes 22 of the storm duct 20 are formed to be below the normal water level of the second accommodation chamber 11b, relocation of the contaminants suspended through the holes 22 and their backflow is prevented"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200420116-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in other words, the water level detector 12 is to operate the contaminant processing unit 40 only when the waste water reaches a constant level in the inflow chamber 10 to prevent unnecessary waste of power"}, {"pat_id": "US-10837164-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "this water level may reflect a level during a wastewater dosing cycle where wastewater or other water has been received via the distribution pipe and is temporarily held by the leaching module until it may infiltrate through any infiltrative surfaces of the receiving chamber and the outriggers"}, {"pat_id": "US-6423216-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, in case the water in the filter chamber rises over a water level of the overflow weir 37 placed at the filtrate outflow chamber 36, the injected oxidation air cannot rise over the water surface of the filter chamber but can be moved to the outflow side, due to the air pressure by the water head difference with the outflow side"}, {"pat_id": "US-7013909-B2", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "when the water level of sewage in the sewage pit 1 increases and the pressure in the pressure sensor pipe 2 increases, the pressure is transmitted via the pipe 33 to the first chamber 17 of the vacuum valve controller 100"}]</data>
</edge>
