  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "EP-0780524-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "the combination of both higher aspect ratio and lesser sidewall angle, compared to leaching chambers heretofore used in storm water systems, provides superior strength and increases the load which the bridge cover -- and thus the system -- can bear"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3464740-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "including 340 and 344 from easily passing through the joints or small gaps between the peripheral sides 188 of adjacent trays 1180 to the interstitial volume spaces 1174 thereby filling void space 1018 which could otherwise be useful for collection and retention of additional storm water outside of the interior chamber 1106 provided by the retention units 1040"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101250076-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the road surface storm water treatment tank 123a is provided with an inflow chamber 123a3, a processing chamber 123a4, and an outflow chamber 123a5, and the inflow chamber 123a3 has a contaminant receiver 123b and a processing chamber ( 123a4) is provided with pollutant filtration / adsorption means 123c, respectively"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101879690-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the stormwater inflow pipe 11 is arranged on the ceiling portion above the discharge chamber 14 of the collecting tank 10 and the discharge pipe 12 is arranged on the bottom portion of the discharge chamber 14 therefore, the stormwater flowing through the storm inflow pipe 11 is quickly discharged through the discharge pipe 12 when the initial storm water is excluded, and the initial stormwater with high contamination degree is discharged to the buoyancy chamber 15 )"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101926744-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the pollutant screening net 20 removes contaminants contained in the storm water flowing into the excellent stormwater chamber 11 from the outside and guides the contaminants to the contaminant discharge chamber 12 through the stormwater collecting chamber 11, a space is formed between the water collecting chamber 11 and the upper portion of the pollutant discharge chamber 12 and between the second partition 12a and the pollutant discharge chamber 12"}, {"pat_id": "US-11298635-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the storm water pretreatment chamber prevents premature rain garden bypass of the untreated storm water due to sediment and debris accumulation"}, {"pat_id": "US-7022243-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the event of a heavy storm where there is a high flow of storm water, the separation tank 10 of the present invention also functions to convey the additional flow of water into a separate high flow treatment chamber so as to circumvent the second treatment chamber 36 thereby preventing any scour or resuspension of previously captured material from the second chamber and filter/recharge chamber"}, {"pat_id": "US-8034236-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the storm water is thus forced under the bottom of the floatable skimmer panel while blocking floatable debris from entering the housing chamber outlet"}, {"pat_id": "US-8501016-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the storm water pretreatment chamber eliminates premature rain garden bypass of the untreated storm water due to sediment and debris accumulation"}, {"pat_id": "US-8501016-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the storm water pretreatment chamber eliminates premature rain garden bypass of the untreated storm water due to sediment and debris accumulation"}]</data>
