  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "EP-2914779-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "wherein the dirty water chamber has an inlet for the unfiltered water and the clean water chamber has a rain water outlet (12) for the filtered water, with a cistern overflow which runs via a siphon (17) into the dirty water outlet"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3309310-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as a result, contamination in the storage space can be effectively avoided by always takes place with sinking water level in the rain overflow basin, a backflow of water from the storage space to the pelvic chamber"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3466513-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in the event that the rain overflow basin 1 is busy or there is a blockage in the area of the retaining element 8, the water can thus flow from the basin chamber 5 to the basin overflow 7 via the emergency overflow 16 without being cleaned"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2663214-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the first rainwater retaining pipe 5 is parallel to the sewer pipe 1 up to the location corresponding to the underground water diversion chamber 2, the portion from the top of the drainage pit 14 at the lower end of the pit 13 for pumping water gradually descends downward from the sewer line 1 while tilting"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100447049-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and the wear 22 installed in the rainwater chamber 20 can be installed high enough because the flow rate can be adjusted by adjusting the water gate (70)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100447049-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, if the height of the wear 22 is excessively increased, this may affect the inundation of the upstream superior rain chamber 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100487067-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the rainwater flowing through the paving layer once received and delivered to the screening means, characterized in that the pit chamber formed by digging downward from the ground so that rainwater on the paving layer flows therein"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100487067-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the screening means, characterized in that the screening chamber having a screen that is located on the side of the pit chamber and receives the rain water passing through the pit chamber and filters"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100487067-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, when the rainwater collected in the pit chamber 16 reaches a level corresponding to the height of the connection hole 44, the rainwater moves from the pit chamber 16 toward the screening chamber 40"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100487067-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the rainwater flowing on the road 28 in the direction of the arrow b in case of rainfall moves toward each grill 14 and passes through the pit chamber 16, the screening chamber 40, and the grit chamber 48, and then the leakage pipe 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100487067-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "meanwhile, in the present embodiment, the chambers 16, 40, 48 and the leak pipe 20 are configured in one set, but when the rain pipe of the existing underground is directly connected to the leak pipe, the existing rain pipe may be utilized"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100774588-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "of the front wall of the rainwater chamber (3) to be rotatable through the operation from the outside and a tap hole for guiding the lifting and lowering of the horizontal bar 71 of the drop preventing jaw 7 in front of the vertical spiral shaft 81 through which the drop preventing jaw 7 is capable of lifting and lowering"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100784989-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in treating rainwater containing a large amount of turbidity, a blockage due to a large amount of turbidity may occur in the chamber portion 210 of the vortex valve, so that an outflow downstream from the rainwater discharge portion 130 of the manhole body may occur"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100841267-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as described above, in the conventional rainwater discharge chamber, the floating contaminants 5 flowing in do not flow into the collecting pipe 3 in rainy weather, but are discharged into the public water through the discharge pipe 4 so that water pollution of the public water is ) is the cause"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100990483-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the screen 12 is installed in multiple stages on the sewage pipe 10 to prevent the inflow of contaminants into the stormwater chamber 11 by separating various contaminants in advance before the initial rainwater reaches the first opening and closing plate 111"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101014995-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the amount of water increases, the water level sensor detects and opens the initial rainwater blocking door to remove the foreign matter from the primary strainer after collecting the rainwater from the primary strainer, filter it once more from the strainer, and then remove the foreign substance in the sedimentation chamber for final precipitation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101039196-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "this structure is to block the inflow of the initial excellent water when the internal water level of the first excellent soil chamber 21 and the second excellent soil chamber 31 is increased due to the continuous inflow of the initial excellent rain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101132847-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "1 is a block diagram showing a state in which rain and earth inflow prevention device having a buoyancy chamber according to the first embodiment of the present invention is installed, fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101202895-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "meanwhile, the septic tank 30 has a series of decaying tanks 31, filtration tanks 32, an oxidizing tank 33, and a disinfection tank 34 so that the initial rainwater introduced into the stormwater chamber 210 can be sequentially purified"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101215187-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the high water level alarm sensor 46 is a water level of the sewage and rainwater in the chamber 12 of the collecting facility 10 above the limit point because the sewage pipe 16 is not blocked in the rain due to a malfunction of the first water level detection sensor 42"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101250076-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "rainwater is introduced into the inflow chamber 123a3 and the contaminants are removed by the debris receiver 123b during the process of passing through the inflow chamber 123a3"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101250076-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "rainwater from the inflow chamber 123a3 flows into the treatment chamber 123a4 and is processed by the treatment action of the contaminant filtration / adsorption means 123c while passing through the treatment chamber 123a4 and then into the outflow chamber 123a5"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101258565-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the rainwater introduced into the rainwater chamber 10 is increased in quantity and gradually increased in water level to reach the moving induction plate 300 installed in the sewage inlet 22 and the blocking plate 260"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101545448-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "[ the end of the horizontal channel section 133 is clogged by the partition wall 111c while the guide channel 132b formed by the horizontal channel section 133 is formed by the opening 135 formed in the partition wall 111c so that the initial rain can be discharged through the opening 135 to the interior of the discharge chamber 116, which will be described later, and the opening 135 is blocked to be openable by the opening / closing door 136"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101926744-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "since the contaminants settled in the excellent water collecting chamber 11 lower the degree of purification of excellent purification, the water is guided to the contaminant discharge chamber 12 so as not to feed water to the purified water supply water chamber 14, which is conducted through the drain portion 16"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101989601-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the opening and closing member 55 coupled with the lifting rod 51 is coupled to the upper storage chamber 35 when the lifting rod 51 moves upward to block the discharge port 39 to prevent the discharge of the rainwater to the outside"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102008617-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "at the end of the sewer pipe (1), the sewage discharge port (2) is normally closed to guide the sewage to the sewage treatment plant through the rainwater discharge chamber (3) to block the discharge of odors and to increase the amount of sewage into rainwater that flows during rainy weather"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102055349-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, by simplifying the structure of the permeation ditches, the efficiency of rainwater discharge is increased, and at the same time, contaminants are removed from the pretreatment water, the irrigation chamber, and the ditches, etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102388770-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the upper inlet 111 may receive sewage from which contaminants have been removed by the contaminant screen 103 and introduce it into the rainwater chamber 110"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102388770-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the inlet opening/closing plate 120 is submerged in a closed state of the upper inlet 11 due to the rainwater condition that does not require a closure, a free space provided between surrounding parts for smooth operation of the inlet opening/closing plate 120 rainwater may leak into the rainwater chamber 110 through such a method"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102408952-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the upper inlet 111 may receive sewage from which contaminants have been removed by the contaminant screen 103 and introduce it into the rainwater chamber 110"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102408952-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the inlet opening/closing plate 120 is submerged in a closed state of the upper inlet 111 due to a rainwater condition that does not require a closure, a free space provided between surrounding components for smooth operation of the inlet opening/closing plate 120 rainwater may leak into the rainwater chamber 110 through such a method"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102773372-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "seals the rainwater receiving chamber (420) with the buoyancy of the rainwater (c), thereby blocking the fluid inflow into the casing (100)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200334419-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and the wear 22 installed in the rainwater chamber 20 can be installed high enough because the flow rate can be adjusted by adjusting the water gate (70)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200334419-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, if the height of the wear 22 is excessively increased, this may affect the inundation of the upstream superior rain chamber 20"}, {"pat_id": "US-11008747-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, as with conventional separate sewer manholes, it should be understood that in exceptional use, such as during heavy rain, flooding and/or blockage, the first chamber may be in liquid communication with the second chamber via the first access port and/or the second access port"}, {"pat_id": "US-11298635-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "alternative structures, for example, chambers filled with porous media and underdrains, can be cost prohibitive and may fail resulting in flooding the rain garden with debris, which requires extensive clean-up"}, {"pat_id": "US-11298635-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the storm water pretreatment chamber prevents premature rain garden bypass of the untreated storm water due to sediment and debris accumulation"}, {"pat_id": "US-8501016-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "alternative structures, for example, chambers filled with porous media and underdrains, can be cost prohibitive and may fail resulting in flooding the rain garden with debris, which requires extensive clean-up"}, {"pat_id": "US-8501016-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the storm water pretreatment chamber eliminates premature rain garden bypass of the untreated storm water due to sediment and debris accumulation"}, {"pat_id": "US-8501016-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the storm water pretreatment chamber eliminates premature rain garden bypass of the untreated storm water due to sediment and debris accumulation"}]</data>
