  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100383191-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "of course, the effective treatment to remove various heavy metals and salts is made safely, and the high temperature and high pressure steam generated in the hydrolysis process is transferred to the steam storage chamber (2) which is opened separately when the amount is reached to a certain level"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100385593-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "of course, the effective treatment to remove various heavy metals and salts is made safely and the high-temperature, high-pressure steam generated during the hydrolysis process reaches the predetermined level, and the electronic opening and closing valve 105 is opened in the steam storage chamber 2 separately installed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100628430-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "since industrial lubricating oil contains a carbon component with a low melting point, when the combustion chamber temperature rises excessively, molten carbon powder may adhere to the heat transfer surface or the like and cause an obstacle"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101044701-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in other words, if the heat deformation occurs due to the temperature rise of the coolant chamber 100, the lower surface of the coolant chamber 100 is fixed to the bottom surface of the core (99) so that the upper end of the coolant chamber 100 rises due to thermal deformation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101044701-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, when the upper end of the external pipe 200 rises due to heat deformation due to the temperature rise of the cooling water chamber 100 or the external pipe 200, the internal pipe 300 also rises together, and the internal pipe 300 of the the distance between the lower surface and the lower surface of the outer pipe 200 is farther away, thereby further securing an area (length) capable of absorbing heat deformation of the inner pipe 300"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101247110-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "pressure and temperature generated when the micro bubbles are destroyed can cause a corrosion state in the reaction chamber 41, so the reaction chamber 41 is connected to both ends by a flange 44, so that the structure can be replaced immediately in case of serious damage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101395863-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when there is a request for the alkaline ionized water at a normal room temperature, the flow control valve 150 is filtered by the water filter 110 to convert the general purified water bypassed through the bypass pipe 130 to the electrolytic water and is supplied to the alkaline ion electrolysis chamber 142 where the alkaline ionized water will be produced and the acidic ion electrolysis chamber 144 where the acidic ionized water will be produced"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101395863-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, as described above, in the alkaline ion electrolysis chamber 144 or the acidic ion electrolysis chamber 142 in which the alkaline ionized water of the electrolytic bath 140 is to be produced, a general constant of 60 to 70% by weight and an acidic electrolytic chamber 142 ) or a general constant of 30 to 40% by weight is supplied to the alkaline ion electrolytic chamber 144 and ionization is performed according to the electrolytic reaction, the production ratio of alkaline ionized water and acidic ionized water at room temperature is also 60"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101541469-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "further, the sandwich panel used in the buried flow meter chamber according to the present invention can prevent the condensation phenomenon caused by the temperature difference from the outside, thereby preventing the corrosion of the mechanical structure installed in the buried flowmeter chamber have"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101611632-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as water and water vapor pass through each of the sub-chambers of the vessel 12, additional water vapor is produced and the temperature of the water vapor is raised to leave salt, dissolved solids, and other contaminants in the remaining water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101804811-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in addition, since the sandwich panel 90 used in the temporary end water service valve chamber 1 according to the present invention can prevent condensation caused by a difference in temperature from the outside, corrosion of the mechanical structure can be prevented"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101804812-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in addition, since the sandwich panel 90 used in the temporary end water service valve chamber 1 according to the present invention can prevent condensation caused by a difference in temperature from the outside, corrosion of the mechanical structure can be prevented"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101828136-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as water and water vapor pass through each of the lower chambers of the vessel 12, the temperature of the water vapor is increased to produce additional water vapor, leaving salts, dissolved solids and other contaminants in the remaining water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102196538-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "it relates to a seismic valve chamber 100 for preventing water accumulation to collect condensation caused by a temperature difference between a chamber, a pipe, and the underground, and water storage due to water loss in a pipe when a facility is replaced"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102196538-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "meanwhile, when the chamber 10 is buried in the ground, condensation is generated in the wall plate 12 due to a temperature difference between the pipe and the underground, and such condensation occurs along the wall plate 12 of the chamber 10 and the bottom plate 13 it becomes a factor of failure due to corrosion of various valves and measuring instruments"}, {"pat_id": "US-10981818-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the higher wattage and overcapacity of the heating element is preferred to ensure that the chamber temperature is maintained because the air pump would bring in cold air in very cold or freezing weather"}, {"pat_id": "US-11559765-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "at block 720, the controller 180 may determine a dew point of the chamber 28 and an optimal post-evaporator air temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-11623178-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "at block 720, the controller 180 may determine a dew point of the chamber 28 and an optimal post-evaporator air temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-4236382-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in any of the vacuum freezing processes described, an aqueous solution is introduced into a chamber which is maintained at a pressure that is somewhat lower than the vapor pressure of the solution at the freezing temperature of the solution to thereby simultaneously flash vaporize water and form ice crystals"}, {"pat_id": "US-4236974-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the oxidation and hence the rise in temperature mostly take place in mixing chamber 64, because that is where most of the impurities are burned"}, {"pat_id": "US-5059228-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "referring to the processing of an aqueous solution by any vacuum freezing process, the aqueous solution is introduced into a chamber which is maintained at a pressure that is somewhat lower than the vapor pressure of the solution at the freezing temperature of the solution to thereby simultaneously flash vaporize water and form ice crystals"}, {"pat_id": "US-5080704-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "referring to the processing of an aqueous solution by any vacuum freezing process, the aqueous solution is introduced into a chamber which is maintained at a pressure that is somewhat lower than the vapor pressure of the solution at the freezing temperature of the solution to thereby simultaneously flash vaporize water and form ice crystals"}, {"pat_id": "US-5448892-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "vacuum freezing processes referring to the processing of an aqueous solution by any vacuum freezing process, the aqueous solution is introduced into a chamber which is maintained at a pressure that is somewhat lower than the vapor pressure of the solution at the freezing temperature of the solution to thereby simultaneously flash vaporize water and form ice crystals"}, {"pat_id": "US-5553637-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the second chamber 31 has a primary inlet 34 connected at 35 to the outlet 11 via the supply line section 13a subjected to freezing temperature, i.e., aboveground"}, {"pat_id": "US-5571424-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "for example, such calculations are first performed to determine the quantity and temperature of the hot water from central chamber 310 needed to heat the aqueous waste and oxidant in the inner annular chamber 335 to a temperature such that oxidation reaction can begin in the inner annular chamber"}, {"pat_id": "US-7678235-B2", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "effective removal of biological contaminants can require a variable amount of time being exposed to the high temperatures in the evaporation chamber"}, {"pat_id": "US-8273156-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "msf systems incur high capital and construction costs due to exotic material needed for the complex flash chambers and control of corrosion caused by high temperature scaling agents"}, {"pat_id": "US-9023184-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as a result, even in a case where the device has temperature variation that is caused when water is passed or stopped in the process of producing deionized water, a gap is not produced between the respective chambers and hence water leakage is not caused"}, {"pat_id": "US-9102545-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as the water and water vapor passes through each subchamber of the vessel 12, the temperature of the water vapor is increased such that additional water vapor is created and leaves the salts, dissolved solids, and other contaminants behind in the remaining water"}]</data>
