  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100447049-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, if the height of the wear 22 is excessively increased, this may affect the inundation of the upstream superior rain chamber 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200334419-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, if the height of the wear 22 is excessively increased, this may affect the inundation of the upstream superior rain chamber 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200432978-Y1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "therefore, the sewage for the excess capacity of the first accommodation chamber 110 of the sewage introduced into the inlet 112 of the first accommodation chamber 110 is connected to the stream through the second accommodation chamber 120 ( in addition to being discharged to 122, the sewage contained in the sewage is filtered by the contaminant treatment unit 200 and guided to be discharged through the discharge port 114 of the first accommodation chamber 110 connected to the sewage treatment plant"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200435493-Y1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "therefore, the sewage for the excess capacity of the first accommodation chamber 110 of the sewage introduced into the inlet 112 of the first accommodation chamber 110 is connected to the stream through the second accommodation chamber 120 ( in addition to being discharged to 122, the sewage contained in the sewage is filtered by the contaminant treatment unit 200 and guided to be discharged through the discharge port 114 of the first accommodation chamber 110 connected to the sewage treatment plant"}, {"pat_id": "US-10118835-B2", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "typically, input water is pretreated to prevent clogging and fouling of the evaporation chambers due to settling of the sediment inherent in the input water stream as well as to reduce the scaling of the chamber walls"}, {"pat_id": "US-10376807-B2", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "typically, input water is pretreated to prevent clogging and fouling of the evaporation chambers due to settling of the sediment inherent in the input water stream as well as to reduce the scaling of the chamber walls"}, {"pat_id": "US-10759677-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the introduction of air bubbles into the untreated water stream will increase the surface area of contact between the heated air in the evaporation chamber and the untreated water"}, {"pat_id": "US-11318395-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the introduction of air bubbles into the untreated water stream will increase the surface area of contact between the heated air in the evaporation chamber and the untreated water"}, {"pat_id": "US-12233354-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "barrier-free path to vapor flow can be achieved with a stream tube without physical obstacles and can be achieved with an expansion chamber in which the vapor flow section is increased so that the speed of the vapor flow decreases, and, inside this expansion chamber and while the vapor flow is moving at a lower speed, at least one liquid water jet is applied to it, the drops of which having a speed greater than that of the vapor flow"}, {"pat_id": "US-12325645-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "wherein the at least one fluid passage is adapted to isolated the continuous fluid stream inside of the at least one insert from the pressurized chamber and remote from the transducer to allow for cavitation inside of the at least one fluid passage via the traveling sonic wave"}, {"pat_id": "US-4244804-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "where significant amounts of organics are present in the water withdrawn from the chamber 17 , those components are subjected to oxidation at station 20, water of stream dischargeable quality being produced"}, {"pat_id": "US-5958240-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "waste streams can be treated with a de-chelation chamber that effectively removes high levels of organics and bacterial contamination"}, {"pat_id": "US-7699991-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in some exemplary embodiments of my invention, the amount of corrosion inhibitor added is such that the mixture of the precipitated solids, conditioner, buffer and sidestream water removed from the reaction chamber through the outlet, is softened"}]</data>
