ncy chamber 15 )"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101926744-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the pollutant screening net 20 removes contaminants contained in the storm water flowing into the excellent stormwater chamber 11 from the outside and guides the contaminants to the contaminant discharge chamber 12 through the stormwater collecting chamber 11, a space is formed between the water collecting chamber 11 and the upper portion of the pollutant discharge chamber 12 and between the second partition 12a and the pollutant discharge chamber 12"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102408952-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, it is possible to block the supply of river water or seawater backflowing to the stormwater chamber 110 to the sewage treatment plant"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200361427-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "on the other hand, since the holes 22 of the storm duct 20 are formed to be below the normal water level of the second accommodation chamber 11b, relocation of the contaminants suspended through the holes 22 and their backflow is prevented"}, {"pat_id": "US-7022243-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the event of a heavy storm where there is a high flow of storm water, the separation tank 10 of the present invention also functions to convey the additional flow of water into a separate high flow treatment chamber so as to circumvent the second treatment chamber 36 thereby preventing any scour or resuspension of previously captured material from the second chamber and filter/recharge chamber"}, {"pat_id": "US-8297880-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, because of their different use, storm chambers lack a multiplicity of small perforations in the sidewall, which necessarily characterize leaching chambers and weaken a sidewall"}, {"pat_id": "US-9580899-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, such end wall panels 82 act as a boundary block around the perimeter of the storm pod structure 10 and function to aid corresponding liquid retention chambers 76 in retaining the liquid or overflow water stored therein"}]</data>
