  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "EP-0576981-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the sensor 51 also gives the possibility that when the water level in the washing chamber 21 drops, for example due to leakage losses, the vacuum blower 36 can be switched on again in order to compensate for these leakage losses and to always have a fully filled washing chamber available for washing processes"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the wait period 695 ends when the leaking water has reached a predetermined water level in the drain pipe 394, and the leaking water is then able to exit through the drain line 398 past the first temperature sensor 414"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2780720-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, when the water level of the pair of water level sensors installed in the snow channel changes, the blockage of the two water level sensors is determined by judging which of the three types of the fluctuations is the above-described pattern"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2780720-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, since fluctuations in the water level are also observed in other water level monitoring panels in the system, the overall system determines the blockage position in units of sections where water level sensors are installed by comprehensively judging the detection results of each water level monitoring panel"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2780720-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "also, in consideration of the degree of water level difference between the two points, the absolute water level of each water level sensor, etc., the urgency of the water level rise due to blockage is divided into, for example, three stages, and only the alarm lamp is turned on in the first stage"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7183463-B1", "para_id": "para_40", "text": "for example, the monitoring device 200 uses the measurement data of the sensor devices 210 distributed in the a block to calculate the dynamic water level at each location in the a block"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7183463-B1", "