ensor 22b the operation of the inflow pump 70 is stopped"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100720388-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at this time, the primary electrolysis panel unit 100 is provided with a level sensor 111 for measuring the water level of the brine tank (110a), while opening and closing the solenoid valve 112 in accordance with the set water level to replenish the time a first water level detecting unit 110"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100841664-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the fifth water level sensor 45 detects an overflow phenomenon that occurs when the water level in the electrolytic cell 30 is increased due to a blockage of the outlet 27a or the like, which is not drained or an increase in inflow from the storage tank 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100932027-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in particular, the temporary storage tank of chemicals is formed by double walls of the outer wall and the inner wall so that even if the chemical exceeds the inner wall due to the malfunction of the water level control valve, it is protected by the outer wall as well as between the inner wall and the outer wall, that is, the leak detection sensor installed in the safety space"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100932027-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in particular, the temporary storage tank of chemicals is formed by double walls of the outer wall and the inner wall, so that even if the chemical exceeds the inner wall due to the malfunction of the automatic water level control valve, it is protected by the outer wall, and between the inner wall and the outer wall, that is, a leak detection sensor installed in the safety space"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100938251-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the first valve 500 and the second valve 600 are opened or closed at the same time, respectively, and received the displacement measured from the sludge detection unit 700 to determine whether there is deposition, and flows into the interior by the water level sensor 900"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100985209-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "as a result, the reliability of controlling the water level of the water tank can be improved, and there is an advantage that the control device does not malfunction by another even if an error occurs in any one of the pressure sensor and the angle sensor such as leakage into the water pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100985209-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "for example, when a leak occurs in the water supply pipe 120, even if the water level of the water tank 130 continues to increase, the pressure sensor 140 may sense a low pressure"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100985209-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "by estimating the wide water level range, it is possible to increase the reliability of controlling the water level in the water tank, and also, if an error occurs in either the pressure sensor or the angle sensor, such as leakage into the water pipe, the control device does not malfunction by the other"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100992828-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the water level of the wastewater introduced into the water treatment tank 110 rises above the water level detection sensor 200, the water level detection sensor 200 blocks the wastewater inlet 112a to prevent the inflow of wastewater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101014995-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the amount of water increases, the water level sensor detects and opens the initial rainwater blocking door to remove the foreign matter from the primary strainer after collecting the rainwater from the primary strainer, filter it once more from the strainer, and then remove the foreign substance in the sedimentation chamber for final precipitation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101045390-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the present invention as described above, the water level sensor detects the amount of manure contained in the manure tank to supply the electrolyte to the manure tank and the electrolysis device in accordance with the amount of manure contained in the manure tank to the manure of the appropriate concentration in the manure tank as it flows into the electrolysis device, there is an effect of uniformly treating the manure in the electrolysis device"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101054375-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the fifth water level sensor 45 detects an overflow phenomenon that occurs when the water level in the electrolytic cell 30 is increased due to a blockage of the outlet port 27a or the like, which is not drained or an increase in inflow from the storage tank 20 increases"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101114764-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, there are advantages in that various accidents such as fire and water leakage, which may be caused by malfunction of the water level sensor, may be prevented in advance"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101215187-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the high water level alarm sensor 46 is a water level of the sewage and rainwater in the chamber 12 of the collecting facility 10 above the limit point because the sewage pipe 16 is not blocked in the rain due to a malfunction of the first water level detection sensor 42"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101220540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, when the water level in the pressure tank 314 is increased because the pressurized water does not flow smoothly into the flotation tank 200 due to the blockage of the microbubble injection unit 320, the water level sensor 334 detects the pump 312"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101296571-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "the method of claim 3, the stopper is a water level sensor comprising a leak prevention packing to prevent leakage by contacting the water purification tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101306120-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "groundwater intake device characterized in that the anti-fouling cap for preventing the contamination coming from the ground while supporting the water level sensor is configured to be coupled to the upper side of the casing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101306120-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is characterized in that the a