  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "EP-3032245-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "accordingly, whether the impedance response of interest is due to the liquid property of the circulating liquid and the electrode surface coating or due to the change in temperature is required to be known, which would otherwise provide a concern of malfunction of the anticorrosion performance degradation detection sensor 10"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3032245-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "the impedance of the circulating liquid and the surface of the detection electrode 1 measured by the anticorrosion performance degradation detection sensor 10 increases by 2% when the temperature of the circulating liquid decreases by 1 c"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3706066-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "in another embodiment, not covered by the claimed invention, moreover the pressure sensor comprises another bragg grating, installed on a part of said sensor not deforming after pressure, such for example a cylindrical body, so that it is subject only to deformation due to temperature"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3706066-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "preferably, in addition the pressure sensor comprises another bragg grating, installed on a part of said sensor not deforming after liquid flow, so that it is subject only to deformation due to temperature"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3769176-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "temperature sensor 38 is used to collect real-time temperature data and monitor the temperature of the incoming water to determine if conditions are conducive to pipe freezing"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3769176-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "daily averages of temperature and pressure measurements are shared on a twelve-hour basis by leak sensor 20 and water control unit 30 via the gateway 40"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "claim_8", "text": "optionally wherein the drain blockage is determined by the controller (142) when the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor (414) is about the same as the temperature reading of the second temperature sensor (418)"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the controller 142 is further configured to compare the temperature readings of the first, second, and third temperature sensors 114, 118, 122 to determine whether an error has occurred in the water heater 10 (e.g., leakage, drain blockage), as further discussed below"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "for example, should the controller determine that the tolerance has changed from 0.5 c to 1.5 c (one f to three f) between the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 114 and the third temperature sensor 122 during the standby mode, the controller may determine there is a leakage and indicate to a user to check the water heater"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "a location of where the leakage is occurring may be determined by the controller when the temperature readings of these temperature sensors are compared while the water heater 10 is in the standby mode"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "for example, when determining a drain blockage, the controller 142 may be configured to query the first and second temperature sensors 114, 118 during morning hours when it is most likely the user will require use of hot water"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in another example, when determining a leakage, the controller 142 may be configured to query the first and third temperature sensors 114, 122 during evening hours (i.e., sleeping) when it is most likely the user will not require use of hot water"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "rather, only differences between the exhaust assembly 30 and the exhaust assembly 330 are specifically noted herein, such as differences in the positioning of the temperature sensors, and how the control system determines a leakage"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "10, the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 414 will increase (i.e., positive rate of change) again to a second peak or leakage temperature limit 690a after the water heater enters the standby mode from the heating mode"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in particular, the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 414 will increase to the leakage temperature limit 690a shortly after (e.g., about two minutes"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the wait period 695 ends when the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 414 detects a shift or change in state from the negative rate of change to the positive rate of change during the standby mode in which the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 414 begins to increase toward the leakage temperature limit 690a"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the difference in the detected rates of temperature change during the wait period 695 is explained by the position of the first temperature sensor 414 being located downstream of the condensate management portion 400 (i.e., the drain pipe 394) such that the leaking water is inhibited from entering the drain line 398 to be detected by the first temperature sensor 414"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "rather, the first temperature sensor 414 may be detecting a temperature of the residual condensate produced during the heating mode that has already begun to cool to a lower temperature (i.e., temperature lower than the leaking water) within the drain line 394"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the wait period 695 ends when the leaking water has reached a predetermined water level in the drain pipe 394, and the leaking water is then able to exit through the drain line 398 past the first temperature sensor 414"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "although the leaked water may lose some heat during the wait period 695 while accumulating in the drain pipe 394, this is not significant enough to prevent the change in state of the temperature reading from the negative rate of change to the positive rate or change, or to prevent the increase in the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 414 toward the leakage temperature limit 690a"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "9-11, only the first temperature sensor 414 is used to determine a leakage"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "further, since any slight increase in the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 414 at the end of the wait period 695 might indicate that there is a leak, the controller may be able to detect even smaller leaks"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "9 represents another way that the temperature sensors may be positioned in a condensing water heater and used to determine a leakage in the water heater"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "alternatively, the temperature readings of the first temperature sensor 414 during the heating mode may also be used to determine a drain blockage"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in particular, when the temperature readings of the first temperature sensor 414 decrease toward the minimum temperature limit 682 during the heating mode, the controller will determine that there is a drain blockage"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3983776-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "for example, the processor 206 can receive sensor data from the flow sensor 210, the temperature sensor 212, and the leak sensor 214"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100385568-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in this case, in the case of groundwater, after the operation of the temperature sensor 80 that detects the freezing temperature due to the characteristics of the groundwater, the water temperature (0) or more), it is preferable to have a timer to stop the continuous operation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100479757-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "the method of claim 1, the heat transfer unit 150 checks the temperature of the washing water at all times and the washing water temperature monitoring sensor 152 to block the operation of the heater when the temperature of the washing water is above a predetermined predetermined temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100479757-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "the heat transfer unit 150 checks the temperature of the washing water at all times and the washing water temperature monitoring sensor 152 to block the operation of the heater when the temperature of the washing water is above a predetermined predetermined temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100634761-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, when it is determined that the communication state is good, the temperature data of the water tank together with the ambient temperature data (which can determine the possibility of freezing of the water pipe, measured by the temperature sensor) and (if the pump abnormality can be determined) preferably, a current sensor is further provided to control the pump using the current data supplied to the pump"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100643176-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is configured to prevent the phenomenon from occurring, and to prevent freezing and condensation due to the temperature difference between the temperature inside the sensor unit 52 and the sample when measuring the sample in a low temperature state"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100728827-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "or less) detected by a temperature sensor (installed inside the pipe) to prevent freezing of the pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100728827-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the conventional pipe freeze protection device prevents the pipe pipe freezing only by the detected value by the temperature sensor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100874616-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "by filling the sensing unit, it is possible to prevent the malfunction of the leak detection sensor due to the small amount of condensate formed in the water supply pipe due to the difference between the water supply temperature and the room temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100901209-B1", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "a freeze protection driver for intermittently driving a pump to prevent freezing of the water supply pipe when the outside air temperature sensed by the temperature sensor is equal to or less than a reference value"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100901209-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "according to this aspect of the present invention, the water supply control device checks the outside air temperature sensed by the temperature sensor and intermittently drives the pump to prevent freezing of the water supply pipe supplying water to the water tank of the drain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100901209-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, when the outside air temperature falls below the reference value through the temperature sensor 270, the water supply control device 200 intermittently drives the pump 220 to prevent freezing of the water supply pipe 230"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100901209-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "on the other hand, the water supply control device 250 by checking the pressure in the water supply pipe 230 through the pressure sensor unit 260, it is possible to prevent the water from flowing into the water supply pipe 230 is frozen or blocked due to low temperature, the pipe is broken"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100991888-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the freeze protection system of the flush toilet of the present invention detects the temperature sensor 13 to prevent freezing of the connection pipe passing through the inside of the flush toilet 10, and when the temperature falls below the set temperature, the controller c controls a predetermined time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100991888-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, the controller c opens the first opening / closing valve v\u2081 and simultaneously shuts off the second opening / closing valve v2 when the temperature sensor 13 detects the expected temperature of the freezing wave"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101025538-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "the method of claim 1, the control unit drives the temperature sensor at regular intervals, the heat pipe leakage monitoring device, characterized in that to cut off the power at the remaining time except the driving time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101025538-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the mounting table is provided with a plurality of temperature sensors 120 for monitoring whether leakage occurs in the heat pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101066393-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "it includes a detection sensor 80 for detecting the operation of the fire fighting equipment connected to the fire water supply pipe (3), the control unit 60 receives the signals of the water temperature sensor 70 and the sensor 80 to prevent the water heater 10 from freezing only water around the heater 10 when the water temperature is lower than the set temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101090211-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the display unit 50 displays the temperature of the water received from the temperature sensor 14, the ph concentration of the electrolysis tank 40, the time, etc., the user at a glance using the electrolysis according to the present invention (1) outputs the status of)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101147332-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "water pollution monitoring system according to the prior art, by providing a temperature control device inside the water pollution monitoring system so that the sensitivity of the sensor is not affected by the external temperature, and also provides a sensor cleaning device inside the sensor to improve the sensitivity of the sensor it s about making sure you re not affected by contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101159544-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, as a simple method for preventing freezing, the configuration generates heat energy in the water pipe so that the outdoor water pipe does not freeze in winter, and is equipped with a temperature sensor in the water pipe to prevent freezing of the water pipe, and then detects the temperature in the water pipe all winter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101207999-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "belt conveyor cleaning system having a pre-applied temperature sensor configured as described above is to clean the transfer belt by the cleaner system when the temperature is lower than the set temperature, and by washing water when the temperature is higher than the set temperature in winter if the wash water cannot be used due to freezing, the cleaning belt can be easily cleaned by the cleaner system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101232378-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the controller 129 is a temperature measured by the water temperature sensor 128 is a temperature close to the freezing point and the internal space temperature measured by the temperature sensor 147 is the temperature measured by the water temperature sensor 128 if a lower freeze of water is expected, the heater 140 and the screw 125 may be activated immediately to prevent freezing of the water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101244452-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "by arranging a water temperature sensor and a heater for directly heating the fire water in the pipeline, it is possible to efficiently prevent freezing of the pipeline of the fire fighting apparatus"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101262046-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "various sensors such as temperature can be installed to detect the change of concentration of sterilization ion efficiently and actively.in order to efficiently generate concentration of sterilization ion through electrolysis when water passes, the electrode affects the flow rate of water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101289929-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the temperature detection sensor 12 may be installed in a water pipe adjacent to the meter 11, that is, in an area of the water pipe where the freezing may occur most easily due to exposure to the outside air, thereby detecting the temperature of water in the water pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101289929-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the controller 14 may be provided with information on the temperature of the water in the water pipe detected by the temperature detection sensor 12, and determine the freezing time of the water in the water pipe by grasping the temperature change of the water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101289929-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as another example, the controller 14 may receive the temperature of the water in the water pipe detected by the temperature detection sensor unit 11, and block the valve 13 when the temperature of the water in the water pipe rises above a predetermined temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101289929-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the process of detecting the temperature of the water in the water pipe (s11), in the case of the general water pipe, the water pipe adjacent to the meter 11, that is, a temperature detection sensor installed in one area of the water pipe where the freezing can occur most easily due to exposure to the outside ( 12)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101295851-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "on the other hand, the ultrasonic sensor 30 is not frozen even in winter as it is installed in the storage tank 20, but there is room for freezing when the temperature is drastically lowered, so as to prevent this ultrasonic sensor as shown in fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101295851-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "on the other hand, when the winter temperature is lowered below the set temperature, the heater 32 is operated to prevent the ultrasonic sensor from freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101327389-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, by checking the condensate and curing temperature throughout the construction by the moisture sensor and the temperature sensor, it is possible to contribute to the quality improvement by checking the uniform curing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101365041-B