es determined from each product temperature sensor 6082a-d are less than the threshold, the controller 6034 may proceed to block 7844"}, {"pat_id": "US-11549837-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "thus, a single set of localized sensors (flow rate sensor 105, optional pressure sensor 65, optional acoustic sensor, and/or optional temperature sensor 93) can be utilized and incorporated into the water meter and leak detection system 10 (126 shown in figs"}, {"pat_id": "US-11549837-B2", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "for measuring or monitoring the temperature of the water flowing through the water meter and leak detection system 10, 126, the use of various thermocouples or thermistor sensors 70 as depicted in fig"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in an alternative embodiment, the addition of an external environment sensor probe and temperature sensor package to a leak detection system creates a more comprehensive system able to prevent and detect leaks"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in an alternative embodiment of the invention, a temperature sensor and a heating element is utilized to detect fluid flow rate of a system, detect fluid leaks of a system, to detect fluid temperature, and to prevent fluid freeze conditions"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the primary temperature sensor package 702 and the secondary temperature sensor package 706 may be utilized to raise the temperature of the fluid to prevent the fluid within the fluid conduit system 720 from freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the primary temperature sensor package 806 and the secondary temperature sensor package 840 may be utilized to raise the temperature of the fluid to prevent the fluid within the fluid conduit system 810 from freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-11659812-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the sensor 72c may also sense a temperature of the plurality 