  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "EP-3309310-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "rain overflow tank (1) according to at least one of the preceding claims, characterized in that a sensor device is provided and the degree of contamination of the retaining element (11) can be derived from the measurement data of the sensor device"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3466513-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "rain overflow tank (1) according to at least one of the preceding claims, characterized in that at least one sensor device (18a, 18b) is provided, and the degree of contamination of the retaining elements (8, 22) is derived from the measurement data of the sensor device (18a, 18b), preferably from the measurement data of two sensor devices (18a, 18b)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101014995-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the amount of water increases, the water level sensor detects and opens the initial rainwater blocking door to remove the foreign matter from the primary strainer after collecting the rainwater from the primary strainer, filter it once more from the strainer, and then remove the foreign substance in the sedimentation chamber for final precipitation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101215187-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the high water level alarm sensor 46 is a water level of the sewage and rainwater in the chamber 12 of the collecting facility 10 above the limit point because the sewage pipe 16 is not blocked in the rain due to a malfunction of the first water level detection sensor 42"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101311288-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the drainage pump is provided with a water level sensor to drain the stagnant water while the position of the sediment detector descends to the settled contaminant surface"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101730962-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the discharge level sensor reservoir 1912 is independent of other reservoirs to prevent contaminants from mixing the generated water with the drain water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101743540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", 