"text": "however, since the temperature sensor is weak to moisture, if the inside gets wet due to snow or rain when exposed to the outside, the temperature sensor often malfunctions, and there is a tendency for the risk of electric leakage and breakdown"}, {"pat_id": "KR-960008516-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as a result, the present invention does not have any risk of moisture penetrating into the temperature sensing sensor effectively embedded in the cover even if it is hit by snow or rain as in the prior art, so there is no risk of leakage or risk of failure, especially the temperature sensing sensor is damp"}, {"pat_id": "US-11629721-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the algorithms can be trained to determine whether sensor data from a system is indicative of, for example, a normal activity (a normal flush), an abnormal activity (a minor, medium or major leak), a condition, and/or an activity in the fluid system"}, {"pat_id": "US-11629721-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "for example, the system can detect whether data is indicative of normal use conditions or a leak using machine learning algorithms that can be trained over time with data fed into the system(s) such that the system can accurately identify whether sensor data is indicative of normal and/or abnormal conditions"}, {"pat_id": "US-12252874-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "method 300 begins at block 302, where drain sensor data is received from the drainage sensors (e.g., the set of drainage sensors 146a-d of figs"}, {"pat_id": "US-12252874-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at block 322, tidal backflow and no tidal backflow zones of the drainage sensor depth data may be determined"}, {"pat_id": "US-9709431-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in this example, if the rain sensor indicates that there is no local precipitation, but that there are water levels above a threshold, the control system 100 may track property operations to determine if there is a problematic operation that may be causing water leakage within the property"}, {"pat_id": "US-9709431-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in this example, if the rain sensor indicates that there is excessive local precipitation, the calculated susceptibility of water damage may be increased based on determining that the likelihood of water leaking into the property is much higher"}]</data>
