  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102562303-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, due to the nature of sewage, sewage having a high degree of contamination has a problem in that durability of sophisticated digital sensors rapidly decreases, resulting in high costs"}, {"pat_id": "US-11333304-B2", "para_id": "claim_14", "text": "in which at least one sensor is integrated into the wireless information and communication stations to monitor the conditions within the annular gap in any given segment of the pipe apparatus, the at least one sensor helping to identify the nature of any leak from the inner or outer piper layer into the annular gap in that segment"}, {"pat_id": "US-11333304-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "this change in physical conditions is detected by the sensor, and its unique signature in the wireless information and communication station changes, thus identifying the gas leak and the pipe segment in which it started"}, {"pat_id": "US-11333304-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at least one sensor may be integrated into the wireless information and communication stations to monitor the conditions within the annular airgap in any given segment of the pipe apparatus, the at least one sensor helping to identify the nature of any leak from the inner or outer piper layer into the annular airgap in that segment"}, {"pat_id": "US-11333304-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "once a gas leaks from the inner pipe layer into the annular airgap, conditions within the annular airgap change and the signature of the sensor located in the portion of the annular airgap where such leakage occurred changes as well, thus identifying that leakage has occurred"}]</data>
</edge>
