nitial rainwater treatment device 100, the rainwater discharge reduction device 200 is a contaminant in the rainwater flowing through the rainwater inlet 250 and the rainwater inlet 250, the rainwater flows from the outside after filtering the filter may further include a filter net 260 to discharge the rainwater filtered to the vegetation filtration layer 210 side"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101564767-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and a fourth step of constructing a water receiving pavement layer on the non-point pollution source-reduced prefabricated storage block constructed through the third step, into the storage space of the non-point pollution source reduction type pre-stored storage block through the inlet, and then discharging the filtered rainwater through the outflow port"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101881491-B1", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "wherein the groundwater inlet pipe and the stormwater intake pipe are connected to an excellent connection portion formed on the upper side of the storage block to induce rainwater inflow"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101923707-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the rainwater flowing into the branch valve 150 through the upper inlet 154 flows into the side through hole 1572 as the blocking member 156 rotates by a predetermined angle in the lateral direction in accordance with the control signal of the controller"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101977695-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the rainwater on the road surface 1 flows through the inlet port 411 and falls to the upper side of the water permeable filter agent 493 to remove the contaminants adhering to the lower side of the screen net 492 and the water permeable filter agent 493 the drainage of the rainwater can be smoothly performed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102216793-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as described above, after removing the collecting plate 28 and the sensor 25, when the handle 29 of the top tank 12 is lifted and lifted, the inlet of the lower tank 12 from the drain 19 of the upper tank 