  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "EP-0797543-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "the sodium metabisulfite is added in an amount to reduce all of the ferric ion to ferrous ion which will prevent the co-precipitation of ferric hydroxide with aluminum hydroxide in reaction tanks 84 and 86"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3883596-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, in order to use the contact material 4 as a filter medium, the porosity of the contact material 4 must be 90% or more, like the contact material 3 provided in the precipitation tank 1"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5295753-B2", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "for this reason, the precipitation of salt in the connection pipe does not block the connection pipe and prevent the supply of the cleaning liquid from the cleaning agent tank to the cleaning liquid tank"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7083442-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "by connecting the discharge hole and the discharge tank via the pipe, the sedimentation of the organic salt generated in the annular movable partition plate is sent to the discharge tank, and in cooperation with the rotation of the annular movable partition plate, the pipe due to the organic salt precipitation the clogging can be effectively avoided, and the sediment in the discharge tank is quickly discharged by the rotation of the discharge screw rod, and the clogging of the discharge tank due to the sediment can be avoided"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100315874-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "1b, is a modification of the a 2 / o method to increase the removal efficiency of phosphorus and nitrogen, wastewater through the first settling tank 100 anaerobic reactor 200, the first anoxic reactor 300, the first aerobic oxidation tank 400, the second anoxic reactor 500, the second aerobic reactor 600 and the second precipitation tank 700, etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100341208-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and, the sludge produced by solidification and precipitation in step s2 is applied to the concentration tank to remove the water primarily to form a filter cake (step s6), the filter cake formed in step s6 is finally removed by the water discharged (step s7)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100379745-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "after passing through the slow flocculation tank 32, the aggregate aggregated while passing through the flow passage 4 can be uniformly introduced into the precipitation tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100387324-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "by desorption of the biofilm attached to the membrane, it prevents anaerobic conditions due to clogging of the filtration pores and provides a growth environment for microorganisms attached to the suspension contact media, and also provides direct filtration in the oxidation tank without the need for a separate precipitation tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100403183-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "a highly concentrated precipitation tank for filtration, oxidation, and decomposition to remove biochemical oxygen demand (bod) and suspended solids (ss)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100440250-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "after adjusting the ph, the oxidation reaction is carried out in the reactor, and then, the precipitate is adjusted by adjusting the appropriate ph in the precipitation tank for aggregation and precipitation, and then neutralized so as not to affect the microbial growth"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100442932-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the secondary treatment water in which the solid matter is removed by switching to the secondary precipitation tank 12b is sent to the oxidation tank 22, and the sludge precipitated in the secondary precipitation tank 12b is for the primary sludge treatment tank 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100442933-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "after the precipitation in the settling tank (l2a, b) to the decoloration treatment by the electrolytic oxidation treatment and untreated to remove the organic pollutants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100444099-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "wherein the overflow wear in the settling tank has a cylindrical shape or a separate type, and a wear plate control valve is configured to adjust the height so as to induce a uniform overflow load maintenance and normal precipitation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100449379-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "and converting the heavy metal into a corrosion precursor which is insoluble in water by a biological corrosion reaction, and sends it to the primary precipitation tank (5a) to precipitate and remove the solid material, and then to the primary treatment tank (13), and then to the primary precipitation tank (5a)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100449379-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "in the primary aeration tank (3a), when organic pollutants and heavy metals in the waste water are converted into corrosion precursors that are insoluble in water by biological corrosion reactions, they are sent to the primary precipitation tank (5a) to remove the corrosion precursors and microorganisms that exist in the solid state"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100449379-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "after the oxidation treatment, it is sent to the reaction tank 18 to supply the emulsion resin and the flocculant to solidify the unremoved heavy metal component, and then to stir slowly by the flocculation tank stirrer 21 to facilitate precipitation or pressure flotation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100472278-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the main feature of the conventional immersion-membrane separation method in the field of water quality, which is this field, is to circulate the water in the water tank up and down to prevent precipitation of suspended solids or decay of stored water, as shown in fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100518722-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the culture medium is supplied to the secondary aeration tank 16 while the culture medium circulates through the magnetic field of the magnet by the pump 32, and the blue water, which is fed to the upper portion of the secondary precipitation tank 17, is sent to the oxidation tank 20 to peroxide"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100605267-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at this time, the waste water passing through the bypass pipe 20 is treated water that does not pass only the filtration tank 17, and is discharged through precipitation in the apparatus, so that almost contaminants are removed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100624556-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a third purification step in which the inflow water, which has passed the precipitation step, is biologically purified while being introduced and passed through the contact oxidation tank in which the microbial contact material is installed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100631373-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the anaerobic tank and the anaerobic tank, sludge is deposited due to the sediment in the introduced wastewater and the returned wastewater, that is, denitrification or precipitation of phosphorus-overtake microorganisms"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100706536-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the agglomeration tank and the belt press may be further mounted between the ozone treatment tank and the ultraviolet treatment tank, thereby further improving the filtration efficiency by further performing the removal of agglomerates through oxidation and precipitation and aggregation by the oxidant"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100712175-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "organic matter in the microbial catalyst oxidation tank plays an important role for the formation of the floc, when the lack of organic matter in the floc weakens the floc strength may be poor sludge precipitation due to pin floc (clock) or floc release phenomenon"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100715020-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "an electrolysis device installed in the aerobic iron precipitation tank, the electrolysis module having an electrode mounted thereon, and an insoluble precipitate precipitated by reaction of an oxide produced by electrolysis of the electrolysis module and phosphate contained in the mixed solution"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100715020-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, the organic material and phosphorus are removed by the oxygen-free tank 40, the aerobic iron precipitation tank 50, and the electrolysis device 60, and nitrogen is removed in the nitrification and denitrification"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100715020-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the aerobic iron precipitation tank 50 removes organic substances by metabolic activity of microorganisms, oxidizes ammonia nitrogen and nitrite nitrogen to nitrate nitrogen by oxygen supplied through a blower, and causes electrolysis of iron or aluminum electrodes"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100784496-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the filtration tank 30 is provided with a filter 31 for filtering contaminants such as organic substances, oil components, and suspended solids in the rainfall that do not settle in the precipitation tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100969208-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "3, a sedimentation tank, a primary contact aeration tank, a precipitation tank, a secondary contact aeration tank, and a sludge-reduced soil-coated contact oxidation sewage treatment reactor, the upper part of each treatment tank, which was a contact filtration tank and a discharge tank, was covered with porous soil in which grass was planted"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101007564-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thereafter, after stopping the compressor 610 to induce precipitation of the oxidation catalyst particles 320, the concentrated water is transferred to the concentrated water treatment tank 430 via the concentrated water valve 420"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101019590-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "2, the aging reaction of the oxide of the aeration oxidation water oxidized in the aeration tank 100, and precipitates the precipitate produced it is preferable that a reaction precipitation tank 200 for performing the precipitation step is provided"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101050144-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in general, biological treatment apparatus for sewage and wastewater, which is widely used at present, is provided with an aeration tank, which is an organic oxidation tank, and a precipitation tank for precipitating microorganisms grown in the aeration tank, thereby oxidizing and removing organic matter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101080805-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at this time, when the overflowed water above the discharge standard is generated in the lower part of the storage tank due to precipitation of the solids, it may be transferred to the sewage treatment plant and discharged to the discharge water system after appropriate treatment"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101279418-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at this time, when the overflowed water above the discharge standard is generated in the lower part of the storage tank due to precipitation of the solids, it may be transferred to the sewage treatment plant and discharged to the discharge water system after appropriate treatment"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101365215-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the photocatalytic oxidation tank 190 sterilizes, disinfects and removes contaminants through the photocatalytic reaction of uv-tio 2 from the treated water separated and discharged from the precipitation tanks 142 and 160"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101382006-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in detail, the purification treatment tank 10 removes the fine turbidity contaminants or soluble contaminants contained in the rainwater passing through the precipitation tank 20 and the precipitation tank 20 removing the floating contaminants and the suspended solids from the rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101502675-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "since the precipitation tank is not used, the facility scale can be reduced to 1/10 or less and the coagulant- it is described that there is a useful effect of reducing the amount of sludge generated since it is not used"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101580859-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "[ therefore, the gravity type precipitation in the pretreatment tank and the primary treatment water in which the sediment and the contaminants are removed by the trapping net 110 are flowed to the filtration treatment tank 20 through the primary treatment water inflow pipe 19"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101779726-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in which after-precipitation process of a batch reaction tank is combined with an inverse filter module for discharging only the filtrate filtered out in treated water while separating fine contaminant particles"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101868534-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the electrolytic waste liquid and the precipitating accelerator are not mixed uniformly, and the undrawn salt from the supernatant of the precipitation tank can be removed from the electrodeposition / adsorption unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101904985-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the stirring device or the water stirrer 222 is formed so that a shaft having a plurality of blades is rotated by a driving motor so as to prevent precipitation of the nitrification solution introduced from the aerobic tank and thereby prevent decay"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102048511-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as described above, the sludge is removed through the modular inclined member 770 and the purified water is discharged through the overflow wear 711 formed on each edge of the sedimentation tank 710 of the precipitation facility 700, the the water discharged through the overflowware 711 is discharged through the discharge tank 750"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102052855-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is possible to control the discharge level of the treated wastewater, and to selectively block the supply of microbubbles inside the separation tank to use the separation tank as a sedimentation tank, but to induce precipitation in the vertical direction or inclined direction downward to maximize the precipitation efficiency"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102089278-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, the anaerobic tank 210 includes a stirrer or a water stirrer 211 for rotating a shaft having a plurality of blades by a driving motor to prevent precipitation of the conveyed sludge introduced from the secondary sedimentation tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102089278-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "an agitator or a water stirrer 222 for rotating a shaft having a plurality of blades by a driving motor to prevent precipitation caused by preventing precipitation of nitric acid liquid introduced from the aerobic tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102089278-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the aerobic tank is equipped with an aeration device or a stirring device to form aeration using air or agitation using an agitator to prevent decay due to precipitation of sludge in the anoxic tank and to supply external carbon sources such as methanol"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102268655-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a precipitation treatment unit 300 provided to receive the desorbed liquid separated from the screen dehydration unit 200 in a treatment tank 310 to separate sediment contaminants in a precipitation method"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102268655-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a precipitation treatment unit 300 provided to receive the desorbed liquid separated from the screen dehydration unit 200 in a treatment tank 310 to separate sediment contaminants in a precipitation method"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102422847-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in addition, it is possible to prevent iron precipitation through real-time ph measurement, and it is possible to provide a waste liquid decomposition monitoring device that can be used for maintenance of the uv reaction tank by checking the ph when washing the lamp in the uv reaction tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102568017-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "the electrolysis unit 50 receives the water filled in the precipitation tank 40 and electrolyzes it"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200431389-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the filtration tank 30 is provided with a filter 31 for filtering contaminants such as organic substances, oil components, and suspended solids in the rainfall that do not settle in the precipitation tank"}, {"pat_id": "US-10696574-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in step (1), after the oxidation reaction and the precipitation reaction, the precipitation can be removed by any suitable method in the art, such as filtering, and the employed filtering apparatus can be any filtering apparatus known in the art, preferably sedimentation tank, sand filter, multi-media filter, etc"}, {"pat_id": "US-4659463-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "another object of the present invention is to provide an aeration/precipitation tank assembly in the system for removing contaminants which sprays air laden water into an air column to further oxidize the contaminants contained in the water while maintaining the system water pressure"}, {"pat_id": "US-4659463-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "this system thus allows the sulphur to oxidize and precipitate in the aeration/precipitation tank and the iron to continue its oxidation and precipitation in such aeration/precipitation tank"}]</data>
</edge>
