tank using unit hollow plate material that blocks air flow to prevent condensation caused by temperature difference between indoor and outdoor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100875260-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the case of such a buried water tank, the water tank is not affected by the external temperature as compared to the water tank installed on the ground and is not affected by the external environment such as rain or dust, and in particular, the water in the winter water tank is prevented from freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100901209-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "according to this aspect of the present invention, the water supply control device checks the outside air temperature sensed by the temperature sensor and intermittently drives the pump to prevent freezing of the water supply pipe supplying water to the water tank of the drain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100942717-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "insulation material (10ac) is filled in the separation space formed between the first plate (10aa) and the second plate (10ab) can be used in the form of urethane, the winter of the water tank (10) by the temperature drop outside, such as it prevents freezing of rainwater stored inside to prevent the collection tank 10 from freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100953075-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, latent heat is scattered with water vapor during the dropping to evaporate the organic oxidation heat and the denitrification heat, and the temperature of the microorganism activity of the oxidizing tank is changed to the atmospheric temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100988365-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the concrete tank exhibits deformation due to temperature deterioration, the cracks may occur in the panel adhesive composition of the concrete tank, resulting in a decrease in waterproofness and separation of the panel and the adhesive composition"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101090211-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the display unit 50 displays the temperature of the water received from the temperature sensor 14, the ph concentration of the electrolysis tank 40, the time, etc., the user at a glance using the electrolysis according to the present invention (1) outputs the status of)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101151121-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in this way, by crushing and homogenizing the organic sludge, it is possible to reduce the temperature, pressure, reaction time and the like in the subsequent reaction tank 5"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101194148-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "if the temperature is lowered, the outdoor temperature may not directly affect the water tank, thus delaying the freezing time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101232378-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in such a state by maintaining a limited amount of air surrounding the water tank 120 only to a temperature higher than the freezing point it is possible to prevent the freezing of the stored water with a minimum of energy"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101232378-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, since the purpose is to prevent the water stored in the water tank 120 from being frozen, the air may be heated only to a temperature higher than the freezing point faithfully"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101232378-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as such, the water tank 120 is installed in the air in the inner space and heats only a limited amount of the internal air to a temperature higher than the freezing point in the state of good heat shielding with the outside, thereby maintaining a small amount to prevent freezing of the stored water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101240216-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an aerobic digestion tank 100 in which organic matter contained in waste water is oxidatively decomposed by activation of high temperature aerobic microorganisms, and an air nozzle provided at an inner lower portion of the aerobic digestion tank 100 to discharge air providing a lifting force for circulating the waste water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101255667-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, during the summer when the air temperature is high, the light blocking pad 51 is closed to prevent the internal temperature of the reaction tank 10 and the temperature of the sewage or waste water from being excessively high to block sunlight from penetrating into the internal space of the housing 30"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101265963-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "comprising an apparatus for maintaining a reaction temperature in an aerobic tank, and forming an optimum reaction condition in the aerobic tank even with an external temperature change, thereby improving the efficiency of organic matter oxidation and nitrification and thereby stable discharge"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101295851-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "on the other hand, the ultrasonic sensor 30 is not frozen even in winter as it is installed in the storage tank 20, but there is room for freezing when the temperature is drastically lowered, so as to prevent this ultrasonic sensor as shown in fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101326272-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "as can be seen from the experimental results as described above, according to the embodiment of the present invention, it is possible to significantly reduce the amount of chlorate generated by appropriately controlling the supply amount of dilution water, supply temperature, flame generation concentration, and current density of the electrolysis tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101368425-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at this time, the first cover 20 and the second cover 30 is provided to cover the opening of the water tank 10 to prevent the inflow of foreign matter and infiltration of bacteria in the air, the first cover 20 the space between the second cover 30 serves as a thermal insulation space to block the influence of the external temperature of the water tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101368425-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as such, the first cover 200 covers the opening of the water tank 100 to prevent the inflow of foreign substances and the penetration of bacteria in the air, and the space between the first cover 200 and the second cover 300 is it functions as an insulated space to block the influence of the outside temperature of the water tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101373842-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, by measuring the temperature change of the hot water inside the hot water tank through the temperature sensor, if the temperature change of the hot water over time is greater than the reference value by stopping the operation of the heating unit, heating in the absence of hot water in the hot water tank the negative operation can be blocked to prevent defective or malfunction of the heating unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101519389-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "when the dehydrated cake, the additive, and the moisture control agent (swelling agent) are mixed in the mixer 500 and supplied to the fermentation tank 503 of the fermentation process in the primary dehydration process and the secondary dehydration process, co 2 , h 2 o, and nh 3 , the temperature increases to 60-70 c due to the heat of reaction"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101532770-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, such an underwater aerator requires extra equipment (such as a crane) for lifting due to heavy weight due to attachment of a motor-equipped stirrer, and is installed in water, and the temperature of the aeration tank is raised due to the heat of the stirrer motor, ) may be lowered"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101642081-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, even when only the oxidizing agent is supplied to the regeneration wastewater purification tank 140 during purification of regeneration wastewater, on the other hand, if the temperature of the regeneration wastewater is lower than the reference temperature, the oxidizing efficiency of the oxidizing agent is lowered, so that it is required to supply the reaction catalyst for promoting the oxidation reaction in addition to the oxidizing agent"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101693100-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in the above-described embodiment, although the water treatment system has determined to perform the chemical cleaning when the contamination index of the membrane filtration tank is equal to or greater than the second value, in another embodiment, the chemical washing is performed according to at least one of the temperature, as shown in fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101861072-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the thermal hydrolysis apparatus 65 is operated to remove the concentrated sludge from the sludge concentration tank 60 under conditions of high temperature (about 150 c) and high pressure (about 20 bar) to methane fermentation of the post-"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102036529-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "that is, such a water tank is contaminated with water quality because the temperature of the stored water is increased due to the high external temperature of the summer, and the water quality is contaminated, and the contaminated water is not suitable for extinguishing, corrosion (mic"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102036529-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "or more, the water in the water tank 1 is heated and sterilized at low temperature, thereby suppressing the growth of microorganisms, in winter, when the temperature is 4 c or less, it is characterized in that the water in the water tank 1 is heated to prevent freezing due to the phenomenon of heat treatment"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102036529-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "or lower, the water tank 1 the heater member 20 is operated to maintain the temperature of the water inside 4 6 to prevent freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102036529-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "after checking only the temperature of the water inside the water tank (1) to determine the operation of the heater member 20 as the temperature inside the water tank (1) or less than 4"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102065694-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "thus, when the temperature of the storage tank 100 is below a certain temperature, the freezing prevention function operates"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102085280-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "a temperature control device installed in the liquid corrosion tank to reduce an elevated liquid temperature of the liquid corrosion solution in the aerobic liquid corrosion tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102085280-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "on the contrary, in the case where the mlss concentration is increased, the wastewater temperature in the tank is maintained at about 30 to 40 c during the biological treatment in the liquid corrosion tank, which is caused by the difference between the external temperature and the air supplied into the tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102085280-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "figure 3 is a schematic diagram showing a scattering prevention device in the temperature control device applied to the liquid corrosion tank of the high concentration organic sewage treatment system according to an embodiment of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102344740-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "maintaining the temperature of the purified water flowing into and stored in the purified water tank unit 1100 by the anti-freezing heater unit 1600 at any one temperature selected from the range of 27 to 75 degrees celsius is to promote the activation of the advanced oxidation process (aop)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102346405-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as described above, in the system for preventing freezing and freezing of pipes for liquid transport according to another embodiment of the present invention, any one of the antifreeze mixture or water stored in the antifreeze tank 18 or the water tank 21 is selected according to the external ambient temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102545607-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "furthermore, the microorganisms filtered here are collected and stored in a low-temperature container (preferably below 15 c.) to prevent contamination, and then put into a dormant tank at a predetermined speed, for example,