llection tanks, causing discomfort to passers-by"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102041291-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "odor leak prevention deodorization system 100 of the rainwater collection tank of the present invention is installed in the rainwater collection tank (5)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102041291-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "operation control for a time to remove the odor by the chemical reaction by ozone, but there is a risk that some of the odor may leak around the rainwater collection tank in the early stage of operation because the time required to reduce the odor by the chemical reaction of ozone and odor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102046131-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "there is a difficulty, and also, it is not easy to remove the contaminants accumulated in the rainwater collection tank, and thus there is a problem that the rainwater collecting capacity of the rainwater collected in the rainwater collection tank is greatly reduced"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102046131-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, it is possible to easily clean the contaminants accumulated in the initial excellent water tank, rainwater tank and sedimentation tank, thereby ensuring the long-term security of the initial water and rainwater treatment capacity.1 is a block diagram showing an example of the initial excellent water quality treatment system according to the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102060940-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "to provide a rainwater storage and water treatment system using a multi-stage rainwater storage tank that is easy to clean the removed contaminants separately"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102060940-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, it is possible to easily clean the contaminants accumulated in the initial excellent water tank, rainwater tank and sedimentation tank, thereby ensuring the long-term security of the initial water and rainwater treatment capacity.1 is a block diagram showing an example of rainwater storage and water treatment system using a multi-stage rainwater storage tank according to the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102060940-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the present invention is to provide a rainwater storage and water treatment system using a multi-stage rainwater storage tank that can effectively remove contaminants contained in the rainwater in the process of collecting rainwater, and easy to clean the removed contaminants separately"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102060940-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the internal tank 32 is induced so that the contaminants contained in the initial rainwater and rainwater from the initial rainwater collection tank 10 and the rainwater collection tank 20 do not relatively accumulate in the deep side of the settling tank 30, and thus the inner when cleaning the contaminants accumulated in the upper surface of the inner tank 32, only the main cleaning can remove most of the large contaminant particles"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102060940-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, it is possible to easily clean the contaminants accumulated in the initial excellent water tank, rainwater collection tank and sedimentation tank, so that the initial water and rainwater treatment capacity is secured for a long time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102076296-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the rainwater is stored in the storage tank 20 by using the drainage line 40, the rainwater is recovered cleanly to prevent contamination, odors, pest breeding, etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102095891-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "another object of the present invention is to remove the non-point contaminants by passing the initial rainwater through a rainwater bypass (\u96e8\u6c34 \u96e8) and bypassing the rainwater filtered through the screen of the pretreatment tank equipped with a screen through a downward filtration in a filtering tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102110404-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "these plastic storage tanks have the advantage of being able to construct a sturdy rainwater storage tank at a low cost because the plastic material, which is a raw material, is cheap, but the space between the plastic blocks must be narrowed to sufficiently withstand the load, making it difficult to secure a worker s path"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102141002-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "in other words, in the above-described embodiment, the planter block while dividing the collection pipe 16 connected between the rainwater collection rig 10 and the storage tank 20 into the first collection pipe 17 and the second collection pipe 35 each end is connected to a different vegetation hole 31 buried in the ground at 30"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102141002-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "rainwater flowing through the collecting pipe 16 or the first collecting pipe 17 may be directly supplied to the storage tank 20 or may be supplied to the storage tank 20 via the planter block 30"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102141002-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "9, rainwater supplied to the storage tank 20 through the water collection pipe 16 or the second water collection pipe 35 directly from the rainwater collection well 10 or via the planter block 30 is stored in the storage tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102216793-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, it was configured to block rainwater flowing into the tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102216793-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as described above, after removing the collecting plate 28 and the sensor 25, when the handle 29 of the top tank 12 is lifted and lifted, the inlet of the lower tank 12 from the drain 19 of the upper tank 12 as (18) is separated, the open upper tank valve 12 is closed, so that rainwater in the upper tank 12 can be prevented from leaking"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102220579-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in addition, conventionally, when rainwater does not flow into the rainwater treatment tank, rainwater stays in the rainwater treatment tank for a long period of time, and there is difficulty in treating boiling point contaminants due to the occurrence of decay, such as rot of the stored water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102281312-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "due to the instantaneous pressure and discharge, it is finely pulverized and stabilized while exerting a strong cleaning power, thereby preventing contamination of the inside of the storage tank 10 and the rainwater stored inside the storage tank 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102290677-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it has the effect of preventing clogging of the contact media and infiltration tanks, and contamination of soil and rivers.1 is a front view showing a rainwater treatment facility capable of excluding pipe-type initial rainwater according to the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102371298-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "the flow rate of rainwater decreases while passing through the rectification box 120 primarily, but when rainwater that has not been partially decelerated splashes and flows into the inflow tank 210 , the overflow prevention bulkhead 130 blocks it"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102371298-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "in addition, there is an effect of preventing blockage of the inflow tank 210 by preventing rainwater passing through the rectification box 120 from directly overflowing into the inlet 200"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102441986-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "in addition, since the contaminant screen 210 of the present invention discharges large foreign substances contained in the rainwater into the lower part of the sedimentation tank 100 in advance, the vortex inducing part discharge pipe 221 or the vortex inducing part discharge pipe 221 is closed due to large foreign substances due to large foreign substances"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102505041-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, rainwater flowing into each water collection tank 41 of the road block 40 while moving along the road surface 100 does not directly flow into the filling pipe 52 disposed in the filling section 41a, but settles in the sedimentation section 41b"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102505041-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, the filling pipe 52 is prevented from being clogged by foreign substances remaining in the rainwater flowing into the water collecting channel 41 of the road block 40, so that the filling pipe 52 flows into the water collecting tank 41"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102645553-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "in claim 1, a leak-free sewage flow rate control device, characterized in that the bottom (12) of the rainwater tank (10) is inclined downward toward the sewage outlet (20) to prevent accumulation of sludge"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102671842-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the pipe 46 is arranged at a certain inclination when connecting the lower end of the drain hole 42c and the upper edge of the water tank 20, which prevents rainwater accumulated in the pair of water receiving blocks 42a and 42b from stagnating"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102747240-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, due to the overload problem of the above-described wastewater storage tank (30), it is inevitable to install the above-described frame (61) and rainwater blocking tent (60), which requires a lot of effort and cost"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102747240-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, even if a rainwater blocking tent (60) and frame (61) are not installed in the car wash section (10) of the car wash, there is an effect of resolving the problem of overload caused by rainwater flowing into the wastewater storage tank (30)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102747240-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "therefore, to block the inflow of rainwater into the wastewater storage tank (30), the above-described rainwater inflow prevention device (100) is installed in the middle of the wastewater inlet pipe (40)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102783510-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "in the first paragraph, in order to prevent the decay of water stored in the above-mentioned rainwater storage tank (200), a stirring unit (500) is installed in the center of the bottom surface of the above-mentioned rainwater storage tank (200) so that a flow is formed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102783510-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "is driven to form a flow to prevent decay of water stored in the rainwater storage tank (200)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102783510-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in order to form a flow for preventing the decay of water stored in the above-mentioned rainwater storage tank (200), it is preferable to further include a bypass pipe (620)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102783510-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "is driven to form a flow for preventing the decay of water stored in the rainwater storage tank (200)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102783510-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "of the pump (700), thereby forming a flow for preventing decay of the water stored in the rainwater storage tank (200)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102783510-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "when the water level of the rainwater storage tank (200) reaches the minimum water level (h2), the agitating unit (500) is driven to form a flow to prevent the decay of the water stored in the rainwater storage tank (200)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102783510-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "7) in addition, in order to form a flow to prevent the decay of water stored in the rainwater storage tank (200), a bypass pipe (620) may be installed on the opposite edge of the suction pipe (710) to supply water into the interior of the rainwater storage tank (200) by a pump (700)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102783510-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "the structure of the suction pipe (710) or bypass pipe (620) of the pump (700) forms a flow to prevent the decay of water stored in the rainwater storage tank (200) separately from the agitating unit (500)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102783510-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "is driven to form a flow to prevent the decay of the water stored in the rainwater storage tank (200)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102809593-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, it is a system that physically stores filtered rainwater in a rainwater storage tank without electronic devices by utilizing the gravity of falling rainwater, thereby reducing maintenance costs and providing a physical rainwater utilization system that does not require frequent maintenance due to corrosion or damage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102885605-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "is blocked to prevent rainwater from flowing into the pretreatment tank (100)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200177676-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when freezing and raining due to the rainy season or weather changes in summer, rainwater has been introduced into the water meter protection tank, which has been a cause of oxidation and corrosion of the water meter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200208312-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the sediment is separated by stages through the fine holes of the primary filtration network and the bottom plate to provide a rainwater catchment for the road equipped with a filtration tank to prevent the drainage blockage in advance"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200249069-Y1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "according to claim 1, geotextile 50 is applied to within a height of less than 1/2 of the filter 40 of the perforated pipe 100, if the rainwater is leaked from the hole 60, the ground is soft, so the geotextile 50 is applied water tank-type pc pipe pipe, characterized in that to prevent the unequal seismic or structural deformation of the hole pipe (100)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200324955-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when it rains, the sewage is treated in the same way as above, and the rainwater that is exceeding the sewage treatment amount (exactly diluted sewage mixed with rainwater) is pumped by the rainwater transfer pump (bar), and the rainwater distribution tank (3) next, the supernatant is precipitated in the storm sedimentation basin (5)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the rainwater receiver 20, the treatment tank 40, and the first partition wall 50 combine block pieces divided into two upper and lower stages, respectively, to form a partitioned water tank, and the upper and lower two block pieces are formed of a connection pin or a metal"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is well known that the rainwater receiver 20, the maintenance tank 30, and the treatment tank 40 formed by the combination structure of such block pieces may be rectangular or circular, and the entire block may be formed in one tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200357071-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "road drainage with first flush treatment ability the present invention is to insert a filter filling tank having a filtration treatment function in the conventional rainwater receiver to the road surface drainage treatment device having an initial excellent treatment function that can reliably remove and treat contaminants contained in the road surface drainage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200414927-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "dropping is placed on the concrete foundation and connected to the bolt nut in the transverse direction and the end wall plate is attached to the column along the rainwater tank block requiring the wall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200449657-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, such a conventional device is designed to directly inject rainwater containing sand, cigarette butts, vinyl and other contaminants into the storage tank and settle it so that no contaminants are removed or secondary pollution by sediment occurs"}]</data>
