1", "text": "in addition, when the rainfall and the level of rainwater and sewage in the sump tank 150 increases, the water level in the guide groove 141 is also increased to raise the lifting height of the buoyancy member 122"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100549466-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "cylindrical filter 40 is connected to the supply pipe 30 to clean the primary filtered rainwater from the water tank 21 to filter impurities or organic matter, so that the rainwater stored in the water tank 10 is decayed by eutrophication or it is possible to prevent the end of deterioration and the like"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100584236-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "however, even with this method, it is difficult to completely remove the harmful contaminants that are strongly attached to the catchment surface by hydrophobic interaction, and the accumulated contaminants are gradually introduced into the storage tank over a long period of time during rainfall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100584236-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in addition, the continuous disinfection of rainwater in the storage tank requires expenditure of chemical costs, power costs, etc., and because the process is difficult to control and cumbersome, a more fundamental solution for removing the contaminants is required"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100584236-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "thus, when rainwater is concentrated on the catchment surface 2 in which contamination by contaminants is prevented early by the titanium dioxide photocatalyst layer, the rainwater is transferred to the storage tank 1 through the catchment port 3 and stored"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100614766-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the treated water through which the contaminant is removed by passing through the filter medium filling tank 71 is accommodated in the discharge box 91 by overflowing through the discharge unit 90, and then introduced into the drain pipe or artificial wetland through the drainage path 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100614766-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "therefore, in the present invention, the removal of contaminants is actively performed on the road drainage during the initial rainfall stage in which the content of the pollutants is high, and the filter filling tank 71 considering the low amount of pollutants in the subsequent road drainage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100614766-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in addition, the removal process of pollutants deposited on the road surface is almost completed in the initial rainfall stage, and since the amount of pollutants in the road drainage due to the subsequent rainfall remains small, the road drainage does not come into contact with the media installed in the treatment tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100614766-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "(3) since the filter filling tank which removes contaminants contained in the drainage by filtration or adsorption is detachably installed in the treatment tank, while the drainage flowed from the inlet of the storm receiver flows through the treatment tank, contaminants contained in the waste water are removed by the filter medium"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100660052-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "because of this, the block body 30 is installed in a row arrangement of the role of the storage tank for storing rainwater and the waterway line is formed so that the concentrated phenomenon does not occur even in a large amount of rain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100681933-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the vertical void outflow facility to be installed in a tank or the like is provided with a strainer settled on a base made of steel or the like, attaching a sump bucket 90 at the lower part of the filter settled cylinder 31, and connecting the discharge pipe 91 to the sump bucket 90"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100702860-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, in the excellent storage tank of the present invention, by forming the outer wall block and the storage block in the hexahedral structure with the upper and lower sides open while the opening is formed as described above, compared to the storage block of the conventional hexahedral structure with the upper and lower plates closed, the raw material cost is reduced along with this, there is another purpose of making the outer wall block and the storage block and the construction of the rainwater storage tank through the block very easy"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100702860-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at this time, in the case of the outer wall block (10, 10a) the inner wall of the storage tank (1) to achieve the outer wall of the storage tank (1) while smoothly flowing with the prevention of leakage of rainwater moved from each storage block (20)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100750645-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is provided in the storage space of the treatment tank 6 includes a filtration device (9) for filtering and adsorption to remove contaminants contained in the road surface drainage rising from the lower portion of the treatment tank (6)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100750645-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the amount of contaminants in the road surface drainage due to the subsequent rainfall is small, and it can be said that there is little problem even if the excess water is discharged immediately without passing through the filtration tank 54"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100752792-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "subsequently, the amount of rainwater transferred to the flow regulating tank 3 is controlled to increase rapidly, and a certain amount of air is supplied through an diffuser installed at the bottom of the flow regulating tank 3 to prevent sedimentation and decay of the sludge"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100784496-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the filtration tank 30 is provided with a filter 31 for filtering contaminants such as organic substances, oil components, and suspended solids in the rainfall that do not settle in the precipitation tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100784496-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the contaminants having their own weight among the contaminants included in the initial rainfall introduced into the first settling tank 10 are primarily precipitated at the bottom of the first settling tank 10 and do not settle in the first settling tank 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100784496-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "meanwhile, contaminants having their own weight among the pollutants included in the rainfall flowing into the second settling tank 20 are second precipitated to the bottom of the second settling tank 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100784496-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, regardless of the heavy rain or heavy rain, the initial rainfall is necessarily passed through the purification tank, it is possible to prevent the contamination of the river by the initial rainfall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100786511-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "this phenomenon causes a vortex phenomenon while the rainwater including the pollutant moving in the contaminant treatment tank 13 passes through the rainwater port 16 eccentrically to one side, and despite this vortex phenomenon, 17) and the reverse flow prevention plate 18 once settles down as it is"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100786511-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "fine suspended matter having little specific gravity remaining after being precipitated in the contaminant treatment tank 13 is moved through the filter 20 installed in the upper part to the storm conduit 12 due to the continuous inflow of rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100792022-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "an index member 33 made of a general rubber material or a synthetic resin material is installed to prevent leakage of rainwater stored from the water storage tank 1 having a horizontally sealed structure"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100800335-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "substantially, the rainwater treatment tank 22 is not likely to have the same internal diameter of the rainwater treatment tank 22 that is mass produced due to the high probability of shrinkage or deformation during drying (cooling), and the index plate 14 is coupled"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100819522-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "an index member 33 made of a general rubber material or a synthetic resin material is installed to prevent leakage of rainwater stored from the water storage tank 1 having a horizontally sealed structure"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100823240-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, when the initial rainwater and sediment contaminants are completely excluded from the initial rainwater treatment facility 1 and the pressure or water level becomes zero, the drain pump 21 receiving the water is driven to operate the water tank 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100875260-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the case of such a buried water tank, the water tank is not affected by the external temperature as compared to the water tank installed on the ground and is not affected by the external environment such as rain or dust, and in particular, the water in the winter water tank is prevented from freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100877621-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the cover of the sump is characterized in that formed of a transparent body that can identify the inside of the tank.according to the ozone oxidation type wastewater treatment device which strengthens the pretreatment process of the present invention, the pretreatment can be treated irrespective of the amount of wastewater including rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100883436-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the case of storage tanks, heavy rains in summer require large-scale land or equipment, and if untreated water is kept, pests such as flies and mosquitoes are generated, which causes hygiene problems"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100927631-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at this time, when rainwater flows into the sedimentation tank 200, heavy foreign matter such as sand sinks to the bottom and light foreign matter such as leaves or vinyl fragments rises on the surface of the water to easily remove contaminants"}