xt": "thus, particulate contaminants contained in rainwater fall into the sediment holding tank 410 and is confined"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100985170-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, in order to solve the problem that the contaminants accumulated in the inflow tank decay and cause odor after the rainfall is over, the hole is drilled at the bottom of the inflow tank, and gravel or porous media is installed outside to filter the contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101056650-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "here, the drain valve 158 is frequently opened to remove foreign substances when the rainwater reservoir tank 150 is cleaned or when foreign substances are deposited at the bottom"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101113989-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, since the tip of the connecting pipe 50 is bent downward so as to be submerged in the rainwater in the sedimentation tank 10, contaminants having a small specific gravity such as oil floating on the water surface may not pass through the connecting pipe 50"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101113989-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the contaminant is finally filtered while passing through the side surface of the ball-type water pipe 43 and discharged into the drain hole 24 at the bottom of the filtration tank 23 connected with the water pipe 43"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101133441-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as described above, the blocking plate 120 is opened so that the rainwater is drained through the drain 10, and the water tank 131 of the blocking plate opening / closing member 130 is filled with rainwater while the rainwater is drained"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101133441-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the blocking plate opening and closing member 130 stops the inflow of rainwater into the rainwater tank 132 after the rain, rainwater is drained into the drain hole 132 formed in the rainwater tank 132 to reduce the amount of rainwater in the rainwater tank 132"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101133580-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": 