into consideration when installing the side plate block"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101197024-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the rainwater penetration system of the present invention stores rainwater underground and partially penetrates underground to effectively inhibit rainwater leakage during heavy rains, and includes a sedimentation tank for depositing sand and foreign substances in water, and rainwater discharged from the sedimentation tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101202677-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "this, the rainwater introduced into the water collection tank 40 along the raw water inlet pipe 46 may include a contaminant and mud not filtered by the screen filter 20 described above, the bottom of the collecting tank 40 there is an effect of sinking by spraying in the down direction of the sump (40)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101202895-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the water quality can be discharged only purified rainwater or clear rainwater has the effect of greatly improving the water quality of the river.1 is a block diagram of a rainwater storage device according to the present invention, 2 is a cross-sectional configuration diagram of a switch and a septic tank and a storage tank showing an initial excellent movement path according to the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101202895-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "meanwhile, the septic tank 30 has a series of decaying tanks 31, filtration tanks 32, an oxidizing tank 33, and a disinfection tank 34 so that the initial rainwater introduced into the stormwater chamber 210 can be sequentially purified"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101202895-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the initial rainwater introduced into the rainwater toil 210 is introduced into the septic tank 30, and the initial rainwater introduced into the septic tank 30 is a series of decay tanks 31, a filtration tank 32, an oxidation tank 33 and , and is stored in the storage tank 40 in a purified state via the disinfection tank 34"}, {"pat_id": "KR