49-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the rainwater flows along the pipeline during the supply or discharge of rainwater, thereby minimizing contamination due to the propagation of microorganisms in the rainwater by maintaining uniform time of stagnation in the rainwater storage tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101345769-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the conventional wear and wash tank is provided with a movable beam that is opened and closed by a hydraulic cylinder for the fresh water and discharge of the rainwater or the initial excellent water, such a movable beam requires a high cost of construction, due to the nature of being submerged in water there is a problem that is not easy to maintain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101345769-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "2 and 10 to 12, the wear 30 serves to send the initial rainwater flowing from the drain 10 to the storage tank 700 in a state in which the sewage inflow prevention device 300 in the rain is closed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101358438-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the filtration tank 50 is supplied with rainwater from which sand and oil have been removed from the sedimentation tank 40, and various foreign matters contained in the rainwater [such as foreign matters of fine particles, etc., which are not sorted in the contaminant separator 20 and the sedimentation tank 40"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101358438-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the whole process, the contaminants are selected by particle size, and oil is introduced into the sedimentation tank 40 together with the rainwater because the oil is mixed in the rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101366083-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "if a problem such as a void occlusion occurs due to a pollution source generated during long-term operation, the filter can be easily washed and reused, and a predetermined size among rainwater flowing into the water collecting tank 10 through the water collecting inlet pipe 31"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101367848-B1", "para_id"