ls in the middle of a mine, a marsh planted with aquatic plants, and a shophouse tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102430974-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "in other words, when the torrential rain starts, an overflow phenomenon may occur due to insufficient space accommodated in the first storage tank 140, the second storage tank 220, and the permeable block 300"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102505041-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, rainwater flowing into each water collection tank 41 of the road block 40 while moving along the road surface 100 does not directly flow into the filling pipe 52 disposed in the filling section 41a, but settles in the sedimentation section 41b"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102505041-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, the filling pipe 52 is prevented from being clogged by foreign substances remaining in the rainwater flowing into the water collecting channel 41 of the road block 40, so that the filling pipe 52 flows into the water collecting tank 41"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102671842-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the pipe 46 is arranged at a certain inclination when connecting the lower end of the drain hole 42c and the upper edge of the water tank 20, which prevents rainwater accumulated in the pair of water receiving blocks 42a and 42b from stagnating"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102747240-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, due to the overload problem of the above-described wastewater storage tank (30), it is inevitable to install the above-described frame (61) and rainwater blocking tent (60), which requires a lot of effort and cost"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102747240-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, even if a rainwater blocking tent (60) and frame (61) are not installed in the car wash section (10) of the car wash, there is an effect of resolving the problem of overload caused by rainwater flowing into the wastewater storage tank (30)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102747240-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "therefore, to block the inflow of rainwater int