  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "EP-2895662-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "when there is heavy rainfall, a reservoir or tank may become overwhelmed by a sudden rush of water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100299334-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, in the reverse contact oxidation method, a water barrier is formed in the middle of the river to introduce the river water into the primary storage tank, and when the rainfall increases, the river is discharged to discharge the river water to protect the river water purification device"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100350735-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, during rainfall, the amount of sewage inflow is high and the flow rate is fast, so that the soil is not deposited in the sedimentation tank and flows into the dwelling house as it is, so that the cross section of the dwelling house 3 is reduced and the sewage terminal treatment plant is caused"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100531027-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, when the rainfall and the level of rainwater and sewage in the sump tank 150 increases, the water level in the guide groove 141 is also increased to raise the lifting height of the buoyancy member 122"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100531031-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, when the rainfall and the level of rainwater and sewage in the sump tank 150 increases, the water level in the guide groove 141 is also increased to raise the lifting height of the buoyancy member 122"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100584236-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "however, even with this method, it is difficult to completely remove the harmful contaminants that are strongly attached to the catchment surface by hydrophobic interaction, and the accumulated contaminants are gradually introduced into the storage tank over a long period of time during rainfall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100614766-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "therefore, in the present invention, the removal of contaminants is actively performed on the road drainage during the initial rainfall stage in which the content of the pollutants is high, and the filter filling tank 71 considering the low amount of pollutants in the subsequent road drainage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100614766-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in addition, the removal process of pollutants deposited on the road surface is almost completed in the initial rainfall stage, and since the amount of pollutants in the road drainage due to the subsequent rainfall remains small, the road drainage does not come into contact with the media installed in the treatment tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100750645-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the amount of contaminants in the road surface drainage due to the subsequent rainfall is small, and it can be said that there is little problem even if the excess water is discharged immediately without passing through the filtration tank 54"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100784496-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the filtration tank 30 is provided with a filter 31 for filtering contaminants such as organic substances, oil components, and suspended solids in the rainfall that do not settle in the precipitation tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100784496-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the contaminants having their own weight among the contaminants included in the initial rainfall introduced into the first settling tank 10 are primarily precipitated at the bottom of the first settling tank 10 and do not settle in the first settling tank 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100784496-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "meanwhile, contaminants having their own weight among the pollutants included in the rainfall flowing into the second settling tank 20 are second precipitated to the bottom of the second settling tank 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100784496-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, regardless of the heavy rain or heavy rain, the initial rainfall is necessarily passed through the purification tank, it is possible to prevent the contamination of the river by the initial rainfall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100930723-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the manhole structure in the present invention discharges the inflow water into the ground or drainage layers while collecting and storing the inflow water through the porous block of the infiltration tank, and rainfall or a lot of water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100955909-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, in order to solve the problem that the contaminants accumulated in the inflow tank decay and cause odor after the rainfall is over, the hole is drilled at the bottom of the inflow tank, and gravel or porous media is installed outside to filter the contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100985170-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, in order to solve the problem that the contaminants accumulated in the inflow tank decay and cause odor after the rainfall is over, the hole is drilled at the bottom of the inflow tank, and gravel or porous media is installed outside to filter the contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101052857-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "the method of claim 6, rainfall storage tank, characterized in that the outer peripheral surface of the rainwater storage tank block (b) is provided with a reinforcement finish panel 60 is fixed via the fastening means so as to block the stored rainwater is discharged to the outside"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101170311-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the initial rainfall storage tank 21 may be made of any one material selected from iron, stainless steel, polyethylene (pe) or concrete so as to prevent corrosion and damage caused by contaminants contained in the initial rainfall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200171293-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, during rainfall, the amount of sewage inflow is high and the flow rate is fast, so that the soil is not deposited in the sedimentation tank and flows into the dwelling house as it is, so that the cross section of the dwelling house 3 is reduced and the sewage terminal treatment plant is caused"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, the above structure can increase the treatment efficiency of high concentration pollutants drained through the road during the initial rainfall stage, but if it exceeds the treatment capacity of the maintenance tank due to the sudden rainfall, various pollutants deposited on the road are maintained"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "then, after the rainfall flows into the storm receiver 20, it is re-introduced into the maintenance tank 30, the treatment tank 40 is to properly remove the contaminants in the treatment tank 40"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as described above, the removal process of the pollutants deposited on the road surface is almost completed in the initial rainfall stage, and since the amount of the pollutants in the road drainage due to the subsequent rainfall remains small, the road drainage is applied to the media installed in the treatment tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200357071-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the removal process of pollutants deposited on the road surface is almost completed in the initial rainfall stage, and since the amount of pollutants in the road drainage due to the subsequent rainfall remains small, the road drainage does not come into contact with the media installed in the treatment tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200358330-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the present invention actively removes contaminants from road surface drainage during the initial rainfall stage with high content of contaminants, and the contaminant content is less for road drainage than the treatment capacity in the subsequent treatment tank 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200371407-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, such a continuous deflective separation (cds) device has to be sedimented at the bottom of the collection tank and sewage of the collected contaminants to artificially after the rainfall, which will reduce the efficiency due to the overload of the device due to overdeposition of contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200431389-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the filtration tank 30 is provided with a filter 31 for filtering contaminants such as organic substances, oil components, and suspended solids in the rainfall that do not settle in the precipitation tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200431389-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the contaminants having their own weight among the contaminants included in the initial rainfall introduced into the first settling tank 10 are primarily precipitated at the bottom of the first settling tank 10 and do not settle in the first settling tank 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200431389-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "meanwhile, contaminants having their own weight among the pollutants included in the rainfall flowing into the second settling tank 20 are second precipitated to the bottom of the second settling tank 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200431389-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, regardless of the heavy rain or heavy rain, the initial rainfall is necessarily passed through the purification tank, it is possible to prevent the contamination of the river by the initial rainfall"}, {"pat_id": "US-12209051-B2", "para_id": "para_84", "text": "when there is heavy rainfall, a reservoir or tank may become overwhelmed by a sudden rush of water"}]</data>
