  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "EP-3468925-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "the overflow stream of the wastewater may be directed to the contact tank responsive to a concentration of contaminants in the wastewater exceeding a threshold concentration of contaminants, as described above"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3468925-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "selectively directing the first fraction of ras to the contact tank may comprise directing the ras responsive to a flow rate of the first stream of the wastewater exceeding a threshold flow rate or responsive to a concentration of contaminants in the wastewater exceeding a threshold concentration of contaminants, as described above"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100441620-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "air generating means installed at the lowermost lower portion of the contact layer to increase the dissolved oxygen concentration of the stream water flowing into the reaction tank and to generate air bubbles so that contaminants between the contact layers fall off"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101382006-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, the present invention separates the overflow water and contaminants contained in the rainwater using the purification treatment tank 10, and the remaining water in the purification treatment tank 10 through the residual water discharge device 50, the remaining water treatment tank 60 ), and is configured to separate the contaminants contained in the residual water through the residual water treatment tank 60 to discharge to the stream"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101802534-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "by maintaining the adsorbent material in the biological reactor 202 or other upstream of the membrane operating system 204, the suspended-media membrane biological reactor system minimizes the possibility of contamination and / or wear of the membrane operating system tank membrane by the adsorbent material, remove"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101904985-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the measured values of the oxidation-reduction potential and the no 3 -n concentration in the upstream-stream aerobic tank are smaller than the target value, the amount of air in the blower is increased so as to correspond to an appropriate value for the influent load, and nitrification is induced"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101946554-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "according to the early stormwater treatment system according to the prior art, the initial stormwater having a high pollution level is discharged to the secondary tank through the gypsum, and when the amount of stormwater is increased, it is possible to prevent contamination of streams by flowing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200365446-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "(raynolds numbers 500-800 or so is preferred) and the first treatment, then the downstream filtration tank (4) is introduced into the secondary treatment, the downstream filtration tank (4) while allowing the bottom-up flow to the filter bed (10) the higher the porosity, the lower the porosity"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200365446-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the flow path length in the filtration tank 1 and the porosity of the filter are made larger in the downstream filtration tank 4 while communicating with the upstream and downstream filtration tanks 1 and 4, and the water barrier wall between the upstream and downstream filtration tanks 1 and 4"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200365446-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "by using the control equipment, the water level difference between the upper and the downstream filtration tanks is maintained at 1.0-1.5m, so that the sediment deposited in the upper and the downstream filtration tanks can be gradually discharged during the initial flooding with less floating dust, thereby preventing the ultimate closure of the filter media"}, {"pat_id": "KR-960002267-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "still another object of the present invention is to circulate and purify the water in the water tank through the lifting tank while ozone is dropped into the air stream and the air flow flows upward from the bottom of the tank for lifting the water in the water tank"}, {"pat_id": "US-10308538-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "materials that settle in grit box 500 and clarification tank 30 may be removed as part of periodic scouring of grit box 500 and clarification tank 30 or as part of the ongoing operation of clarification system 1 to selectively classify and separate grits, solids, particulates, and solvated materials from an influent stream"}, {"pat_id": "US-10308539-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "materials that settle in grit box 500 and clarification tank 30 may be removed as part of periodic scouring of grit box 500 and clarification tank 30 or as part of the ongoing operation of clarification system 1 to selectively classify and separate grits, solids, particulates, and solvated materials from an influent stream"}, {"pat_id": "US-10927539-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "3, the dirty water and included sediment may be removed from the point of collection at the downstream end 28 through one or more suction hoses 36 and conducted to a vacuum tank 38 that may be carried on a truck 40"}, {"pat_id": "US-11401171-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "3a and 3b, before, during, or after flowing into the portion 325 of the holding tank 280 via the inlet 285, the treated slop feed stream undergoes dissolved air flotation ( daf ), which is a process by which suspended solids, oil, and/or other contaminants are removed from the treated slop feed stream via air bubble flotation"}, {"pat_id": "US-11629721-B2", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "a continuous small leak (or a major leak), for example, can prevent the tank from refill and continue water stream until it is fixed"}, {"pat_id": "US-11999641-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the organisms downstream thus deselect themselves in the bypass (the term bypass denotes the flow of wastewater bypassing the tank and ahead of the batch of wastewater that goes into the front of the reactor) ahead of the earlier cascade"}, {"pat_id": "US-6627073-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "if the water level in the area on the uppermost stream side in the electrolytic tank is controlled in a predetermined range, as in the claim 16, therefore, it is possible to more reliably prevent the water from leaking from the electrolytic tank"}, {"pat_id": "US-6655402-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, liquid in the flush reservoir is quickly released through the ingress and egress port to the downstream storage tank or sewer resuspending the settled sewer solids and transporting them to a sediment pit for final disposal"}, {"pat_id": "US-7531096-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "such pre-treatment can cost effectively reduce the amount of organic contaminants prior to downstream reduction of organic contaminants (discussed below) cooling tower blowdown 30 exits feed tank 50 and is input into an evaporator system 52"}, {"pat_id": "US-8211296-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the oxidizing chemical is preferably introduced into a zone of turbulent flow of the frac fluid through an eductor disposed upstream of the frac tanks, thereby achieving better mixing and better contact with the particular contaminant(s) then being treated"}, {"pat_id": "US-8226832-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the oxidizing chemical is preferably introduced into a zone of turbulent flow of the frac fluid through an eductor disposed upstream of the frac tanks, thereby achieving better mixing and better contact with the particular contaminant(s) then being treated"}, {"pat_id": "US-8376254-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "certain embodiments of the present invention provide a spray assembly 15 for use in an automatic well washer that can reduce and/or eliminate the occurrence of blockage from accumulation of solid matter in a fluid stream used to wash the well, vault or tank"}, {"pat_id": "US-8425768-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "mechanical filter 412 may be configured to remove suspended solids and other particles to prevent clogging or fouling of ion exchange (i.e., resin) tanks 402 downstream in system 400"}, {"pat_id": "US-9586845-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "materials that settle in grit box 500 and clarification tank 30 may be removed as part of periodic scouring of grit box 500 and clarification tank 30 or as part of the ongoing operation of clarification system 1 to selectively classify and separate grits, solids, particulates, and solvated materials from an influent stream"}, {"pat_id": "US-9611160-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "1d, a recirculation stream 38 returns part of the third treated stream 34, intermittently or continuously, to the anodic oxidation section 4 by tanks, valves and pumps (not shown) as required"}, {"pat_id": "US-9656894-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "following the scaling prevention treatment 64 the stream of water is transferred into water and condensation recovery tank 66 for discharge to the atmosphere"}, {"pat_id": "US-9676642-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "materials that settle in grit box 500 and clarification, tank 30 may be removed as part of periodic scouring of grit box 500 and clarification tank 30 or as part of the ongoing operation of clarification system 1 to selectively classify and separate grits, solids, particulates, and solvated materials from an influent stream"}]</data>
