  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "JP-2885063-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the regeneration method in which the amount of salt water up to a predetermined water level in the salt water tank is applied irrespective of the concentration, poor regeneration of the resin capacity is caused, and the process shifts to the water softening treatment without completely regenerating the capacity"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3347959-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "[0003] in a vacuum valve unit of this type of vacuum type sewer system, when a sewage water level abnormality of a sewage tank occurs due to a vacuum valve failure or the like, it is necessary to quickly detect this and notify a manager"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5042805-B2", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "specifically, when the water level gauge 111 detects that the water level in the contaminant removal tank 110 is higher than the specified water level, control is performed to relatively increase the amount of water transferred by the advection pump 122, and the contamination level is also increased"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5042805-B2", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "for example, in the case of the water level gauge 111 having a configuration in which an on signal is output when the water level of the contaminant removal tank 110 exceeds a prescribed water level defined in advance and an off signal is outputted when the water level falls below the prescribed water level, the amount of effluent water can be derived from the time when the off signal switches"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6492150-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "that is, the circuit for detecting the conduction between the electrodes due to the water leakage is designed using the circuit for detecting the water level of the water receiving tank conventionally used"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6492150-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "the circuit for detecting the water level in the water receiving tank is a low voltage ac circuit in order to avoid electric shock and prevent electrolysis because the electrodes are always submerged"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0137696-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "moreover, the method of checking the low water level in the water tank by using the air tank is very conventional, and it only functions to block the flow of water only when the water is almost full in the water tank, thereby making it difficult to identify the low water amount in the water tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0161641-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "another object of the present invention is a water level sensor failure detection method of the cold and hot water purifier that can prevent the occurrence of freezing of the cold water tank caused by the failure of the water level sensor of the cold and hot water purifier, a failure due to the overheat of the heater, or excessive waste of purified water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0167322-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the cold air supplied to the upper side moves along the surface of the cold water storage tank 12, and since more cold air is supplied to the interface of the water level b than the normal state, the surface of the purified water freezes and the freezing grows gradually over time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100314663-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and water level (36) (37) is provided, the electronic safety valve (e) automatically discharged to the outside when abnormal pressure to maintain the set pressure and to prevent damage and deformation of the tank ( 39) and automatic air discharge valves 34 and 35 are provided"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100331066-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "by equaling the water level in groups, the concrete capacity of decaying tanks is reduced and the simultaneous treatment efficiency is maximized"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100472567-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "accordingly, when the water level of the sewage pit 5 reaches a predetermined height while the collection tank 21 and the vacuum line 9 are maintained in a vacuum state by operating the vacuum pump 23, the vacuum valve controller 17 ) opens the vacuum valve 13 so that the sewage in the sewage pit 5 is sucked into the collection tank 21 of the vacuum pumping station 7 along the vacuum line 9"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100499785-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the controller 64 is difficult to supply water to the water tank 10 due to a failure of the pump 3a or a blockage of the reverse osmosis filter 7 when the lower limit water level detection signal is input for a predetermined time or more among the water level detection signals sh"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100510269-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "into the flow rate adjustment tank 30 in a state in which the coarse contaminant is filtered and removed while passing through), and when the water level detection sensor 33 of the flow adjustment tank 30 detects the water level, the raw water pump 31 according to the detected signal"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100523314-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, in order to prevent the variable storage tank 110 from being ruptured, it is preferable to install a level gauge (not shown) capable of detecting a water level in the variable storage tank 110"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100523314-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, it is possible to detect whether or not the limit level is reached through the water level meter installed in the variable storage tank 110, and to prepare for the rupture of the variable storage tank 110 by alerting the alarm sound, etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100531027-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, when the rainfall and the level of rainwater and sewage in the sump tank 150 increases, the water level in the guide groove 141 is also increased to raise the lifting height of the buoyancy member 122"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100531031-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, when the rainfall and the level of rainwater and sewage in the sump tank 150 increases, the water level in the guide groove 141 is also increased to raise the lifting height of the buoyancy member 122"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100540762-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the controller 64 is difficult to supply water to the water tank 10 due to a failure of the pump 3a or a blockage of the reverse osmosis filter 7 when the lower limit water level detection signal is input for a predetermined time or more among the water level detection signals sh"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100546851-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the control unit 90, when the second filter material 22a of the second filter tank 20 is blocked and the water level is increased, the water flows back through the overflow pipe 45, and this is applied to the detection signal of the second water level sensor 22b"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100546851-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the control unit 90 is blocked by the second filter material 22a of the second filter tank 20 when the water level is increased, the water flows back through the overflow pipe 45, by the detection signal of the second water level sensor 22b the operation of the inflow pump 70 is stopped"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100624556-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "on the other hand, if the inflow water is directly transmitted to the sedimentation tank 400 through the water level control pipe 340 installed in the modular wetland infrastructure (300) due to the inflow of excess flow screen 430 of the sedimentation tank 400 physical filtration occurs thereby preventing the inflow of untreated water directly into the contact oxidation tank 500"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100644949-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "water purifier automatic drainage method of another embodiment of the present invention, the water level check step of detecting the water level of the water tank to determine the number of water, the step of determining the number of water to be confirmed for a certain time, and if a predetermined number or more is confirmed, drainage of the water tank and opening the valve and draining the water, determining whether the water level is confirmed within a predetermined time, checking the water level when the water level is confirmed, and draining the water by opening the water drain valve of the water tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100644949-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "second, after checking the water level, including the drainage step of opening and draining the drain valve of the water tank, it is possible to automatically adjust the water level to prevent the overflow of the refrigerant tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100644949-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "third, when the water level is confirmed for a predetermined number of times or more, a drainage step of opening and draining the drain valve of the refrigerant tank, determining whether the water level is confirmed within a predetermined time, and a water level checking step of checking the water level when the water level is confirmed as a result, errors due to internal factors can be recognized"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100674176-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "since the second filtration system 40 is relatively small and runs for a long time, it filters out contaminants as much as possible, enters the filtered water into the water level control tank 10 and consequently returns it to the swimming pool"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100720388-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at this time, the primary electrolysis panel unit 100 is provided with a level sensor 111 for measuring the water level of the brine tank (110a), while opening and closing the solenoid valve 112 in accordance with the set water level to replenish the time a first water level detecting unit 110"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100727599-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the overflow prevention process by the water level adjusting apparatus of the present invention is largely, the first blocking step of first blocking the inflow of raw water into the purified water tank 500 by a mechanical opening and closing structure when the water level of the purified water tank 500 is full"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100823240-B1", "para_id": "para_1",