 be improved, and there is an advantage that the control device does not malfunction by another even if an error occurs in any one of the pressure sensor and the angle sensor such as leakage into the water pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100985209-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "for example, when a leak occurs in the water supply pipe 120, even if the water level of the water tank 130 continues to increase, the pressure sensor 140 may sense a low pressure"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100985209-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "by estimating the wide water level range, it is possible to increase the reliability of controlling the water level in the water tank, and also, if an error occurs in either the pressure sensor or the angle sensor, such as leakage into the water pipe, the control device does not malfunction by the other"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100992828-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the water level of the wastewater introduced into the water treatment tank 110 rises above the water level detection sensor 200, the water level detection sensor 200 blocks the wastewater inlet 112a to prevent the inflow of wastewater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101000865-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, when the pressurized water tank reaches the minimum water level, the disk interlocked with the buckle automatically descends to close the flow path of the water cylinder connected to the water supply and drain pipe, thereby blocking the air pressure from leaking to the outside through the water supply and drain pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101007019-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "at this time, the third non-power flow control device 15 also operates in the shielding direction due to the water pressure applied as the water level rises in the filtration tank 8"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101033272-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, when the water level of the fish tank 300 is increased and the flow rate supplied to the cleaner through the drain port 301 increases, the flow rate may be reduced 