": "when the water level of the sewage stored in the tank 30 rises and the height of the buckle member 54 increases, the wire 56b is pulled up by the load of the sensing block 56c and the sensing block 56c is lowered"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101388033-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, in the present embodiment, since the sensing unit 58 that detects the water level of the sewage is installed outside the tank 30, the sensing unit 58 may be prevented from malfunctioning due to severe contamination of the sensing unit 58"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101500632-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "(f2 f3) accordingly, in the present invention, the amount of water stored in the water tank is automatically adjusted to a level higher than the water level capable of detecting a wind speed (wind load) this is to prevent defects due to wind loads such as overturning and partial crushing of the water tank due to insufficient amount of water stored in the water tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101660087-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as the amount of the treated water w introduced into the treated water storage tank 50 gradually increases during the electrolysis step s30, the water level of the treated water w gradually increases"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101676999-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "therefore, according to the present invention, it is possible to monitor the state of water leakage or foreign matter introduced into the water tank 1 by monitoring the rapid change of the water level and the water quality, thereby enabling cleaner and safer water quality management"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101729735-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "field of the invention [0001] the present invention relates to a water level elevating device for a water-the present invention relates to a water level elevating device, and more particularly, to a water level elevating device for a water pipe turning method applied to a water turning method bypassing a work section of a sub tank for maintenance or monitoring of a sub tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101741449-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "that is, if the operating time of the filtration tank is increased, the flow rate of the flow of the rainwater or the flow rate of the treated water is lowered due to the increase of the amount of contaminants collected in the lcd artificial floating filter media, or the water level of the tank before the rainwater is increased do"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101875497-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in order to prevent the polluted water from leaching to the sea side, the water level of the collecting tank is formed lower than the water level of the ocean, so as not to leach out to sea"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101875497-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and a control unit for controlling driving of the pressurization pressurizing pump to transport the contaminated water to the land storage tank when the internal water level of the shielding facility is higher than a predetermined reference value, and the inside water level of the shielding facility can be adjusted by being transported in both directions between the storage tank and the polluted water storage tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101875497-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "according to the present invention, a pipeline is installed between the shielding facility of the marine waste treatment plant and the land storage tank, and the polluted water of the shielding facility is transported to the land storage tank by the pipeline, thereby reducing the water level in the shielding facility of the marine waste treatment plant"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101875497-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "according to the present invention, by sensing in real time the water level inside the shielding facility of the marine waste treatment plant and the water level outside the sea surface, the polluted water in the shielding facility is transferred to the landfill tank, it can be surely prevented"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101875497-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, when the 