tion tank 400 through the water level control pipe 340 installed in the modular wetland infrastructure (300) due to the inflow of excess flow screen 430 of the sedimentation tank 400 physical filtration occurs thereby preventing the inflow of untreated water directly into the contact oxidation tank 500"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200365284-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the controller 64 is difficult to supply water to the water tank 10 due to a failure of the pump 3a or a blockage of the reverse osmosis filter 7 when the lower limit water level detection signal is input for a predetermined time or more among the water level detection signals sh"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200365446-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "by using the control equipment, the water level difference between the upper and the downstream filtration tanks is maintained at 1.0-1.5m, so that the sediment deposited in the upper and the downstream filtration tanks can be gradually discharged during the initial flooding with less floating dust, thereby preventing the ultimate closure of the filter media"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200371175-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "accordingly, when the water level of the sewage pit 5 reaches a predetermined height while the collection tank 21 and the vacuum line 9 are maintained in a vacuum state by operating the vacuum pump 23, the vacuum valve controller 17 ) opens the vacuum valve 13 so that the sewage in the sewage pit 5 is sucked into the collection tank 21 of the vacuum pumping station 7 along the vacuum line 9"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200425676-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the water level in the water tank 40 reaches a predetermined height, the float 56 serves to block the water inlet pipe 50 while rising upward according to the water level"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200442330-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "more specifically, when the purified water is filled to the water level set in the purified water storage tank (pressure tank), the automatic shut off valve for the wate