  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100516951-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in addition, between the second compartment member 400 and the storm water receiving tank 100 is further provided with a contaminant filtration adsorption means 700 filled with a filter medium to remove the contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101224380-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, in the field, problems such as securing convenience of pc block assembly construction, securing structural stability of storm water storage tanks constructed by pc block assembly, problems of leaking through gaps between blocks and removing sludge accumulated inside storm water storage tanks are pointed out"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101250076-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the road surface storm water treatment tank 123a is provided with an inflow chamber 123a3, a processing chamber 123a4, and an outflow chamber 123a5, and the inflow chamber 123a3 has a contaminant receiver 123b and a processing chamber ( 123a4) is provided with pollutant filtration / adsorption means 123c, respectively"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101741449-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the inlet tank 100 is formed with a screen box 120 to remove contaminants from the storm water discharged from the inlet pipe 110 and is formed at a lower side of the screen box 120, the desulphurization tool 130 is formed to have a flow regulating function"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101879690-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the stormwater inflow pipe 11 is arranged on the ceiling portion above the discharge chamber 14 of the collecting tank 10 and the discharge pipe 12 is arranged on the bottom portion of the discharge chamber 14 therefore, the stormwater flowing through the storm inflow pipe 11 is quickly discharged through the discharge pipe 12 when the initial storm water is excluded, and the initial stormwater with high contamination degree is discharged to the buoyancy chamber 15 )"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102041291-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "however, only the mechanical devices installed in rainwater pipes or storm water collection tanks do not completely prevent leakage of odors flowing back from the sewage pipes, and as a result, odor leaks around sewage pipes or storm water collection tanks, causing discomfort to passers-by"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "(7) the maintenance and treatment tanks can be installed in a block block made of concrete, or forcedly installed together with the storm water receiver"}, {"pat_id": "US-10865547-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the event of a truly significant rain (storm) event, these storage tanks can be overwhelmed, thus resulting in flooding or discharge of excess storm water to the sewage treatment system, a body of water, or a river"}, {"pat_id": "US-11603651-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the event of a truly significant rain (storm) event, these storage tanks can be overwhelmed, thus resulting in flooding or discharge of excess storm water to the sewage treatment system, a body of water, or a river"}, {"pat_id": "US-7022243-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the event of a heavy storm where there is a high flow of storm water, the separation tank 10 of the present invention also functions to convey the additional flow of water into a separate high flow treatment chamber so as to circumvent the second treatment chamber 36 thereby preventing any scour or resuspension of previously captured material from the second chamber and filter/recharge chamber"}]</data>
