  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100516951-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in addition, between the second compartment member 400 and the storm water receiving tank 100 is further provided with a contaminant filtration adsorption means 700 filled with a filter medium to remove the contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100614766-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "(3) since the filter filling tank which removes contaminants contained in the drainage by filtration or adsorption is detachably installed in the treatment tank, while the drainage flowed from the inlet of the storm receiver flows through the treatment tank, contaminants contained in the waste water are removed by the filter medium"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100786511-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "fine suspended matter having little specific gravity remaining after being precipitated in the contaminant treatment tank 13 is moved through the filter 20 installed in the upper part to the storm conduit 12 due to the continuous inflow of rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101013596-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the block-type stormwater storage tank according to the present invention, an assembling groove is formed on the bottom edge of the four sides of the corner block, the side block and the inner block, which are bounded with the open bottom surface, while the assembling groove is formed on the top surface of the corner block, the side block and the inner block"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101052857-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, another object of the present invention, because each storm storage block is connected via a fastener and a fastening means, not a wire, it is possible to connect and construct each storm storage block very quickly to significantly shorten the installation time it is to provide an excellent storage tank construction method using the excellent storage tank block and the excellent storage tank and the excellent storage tank block"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101052857-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the storm storage tank of the present invention, characterized in that the outer periphery surface of the storm storage block is provided with a reinforcement of the closing panel fixed through the fastening means so as to prevent the stored rainwater is discharged to the outside"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101202895-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "meanwhile, the septic tank 30 has a series of decaying tanks 31, filtration tanks 32, an oxidizing tank 33, and a disinfection tank 34 so that the initial rainwater introduced into the stormwater chamber 210 can be sequentially purified"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101224380-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, in the field, problems such as securing convenience of pc block assembly construction, securing structural stability of storm water storage tanks constructed by pc block assembly, problems of leaking through gaps between blocks and removing sludge accumulated inside storm water storage tanks are pointed out"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101224380-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the organic integrity of the floor block, corner wall block, side wall block, column block, ceiling border block, and ceiling block strengthens the overall integrity of the storm storage tank, thereby ensuring structural stability of the storm storage tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101250076-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the road surface storm water treatment tank 123a is provided with an inflow chamber 123a3, a processing chamber 123a4, and an outflow chamber 123a5, and the inflow chamber 123a3 has a contaminant receiver 123b and a processing chamber ( 123a4) is provided with pollutant filtration / adsorption means 123c, respectively"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101382006-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "accordingly, the initial stormwater treatment apparatus 1 of the present invention quickly discharges rainwater, that is, residual water remaining in the purification treatment tank 10, to prevent the residual water from decaying"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101391172-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and a filtration tank for removing fine contaminants in the initial storm that have passed through the swirl screen and discharging the initial storm in the state where fine contaminants have been removed through the discharge pipe to the outside"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101485001-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, the rainwater infiltrated through the permeable press block flows directly into the reservoir 500 through the induction pipe installed under the permeable press block, and the road effluent flowing through the rainwater receiver on the road passes through the filtration tank and then flows into the storage tank 500 after the initial storm has been processed through the storage tank 300"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101653780-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the sludge hopper 230 allows the sludge contained in the storm to flow into the backwash drainage storage tank 310 so that the contaminants separated from the backwashing means 220 due to the backwashing process, to the backwash drainage storage tank 310 side by a predetermined angle"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101653780-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the filtration tank 210 is also provided with a filter means 220 for purifying the effluent from which solids contained in the storm and fine contaminants are removed from the stormwater inflow pipe 140 of the storage tank 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101741449-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the inlet tank 100 is formed with a screen box 120 to remove contaminants from the storm water discharged from the inlet pipe 110 and is formed at a lower side of the screen box 120, the desulphurization tool 130 is formed to have a flow regulating function"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101778786-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, it is possible to prevent the initial storm having a high contamination degree from being supplied to the sedimentation tank guide pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101859056-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "therefore, the storage tank structure for stormwater infiltration and storage according to the present invention can ensure sufficient durability against repetitive vehicle shafts since the storage unit blocks have sufficient strength"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101865757-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, the conventional water treatment apparatuses such as storage tanks have a problem of non-environmental problems because the filtration efficiency of contaminants contained in rainwater such as early storms is low"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101879690-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the stormwater inflow pipe 11 is arranged on the ceiling portion above the discharge chamber 14 of the collecting tank 10 and the discharge pipe 12 is arranged on the bottom portion of the discharge chamber 14 therefore, the stormwater flowing through the storm inflow pipe 11 is quickly discharged through the discharge pipe 12 when the initial storm water is excluded, and the initial stormwater with high contamination degree is discharged to the buoyancy chamber 15 )"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101946554-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "according to the early stormwater treatment system according to the prior art, the initial stormwater having a high pollution level is discharged to the secondary tank through the gypsum, and when the amount of stormwater is increased, it is possible to prevent contamination of streams by flowing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200148426-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "due to this, various flies and mosquitoes inhabited in the sewer pipe are blocked by the blocking plates 6 installed on the outer wall surfaces of the waste collection container 4 of the storm drainage tank 1 for roads, thereby preventing passage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200324955-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when it rains, the sewage is treated in the same way as above, and the rainwater that is exceeding the sewage treatment amount (exactly diluted sewage mixed with rainwater) is pumped by the rainwater transfer pump (bar), and the rainwater distribution tank (3) next, the supernatant is precipitated in the storm sedimentation basin (5)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as a result, deposits absorbing contaminants are deposited in the mud at the bottom of the storm receiver 20, the maintenance tank 30, and the treatment tank 40"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "then, after the rainfall flows into the storm receiver 20, it is re-introduced into the maintenance tank 30, the treatment tank 40 is to properly remove the contaminants in the treatment tank 40"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "on the other hand, if the removal process of the contaminants continues, the bottom of the storm receiver 20, the maintenance tank 30 and the treatment tank 40, deposits containing contaminants are deposited, and the filter medium filling tank ( 70) contaminants will also collect inside, and regular removal will be required"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "(2) since the filter which removes contaminants contained in the drainage by filtration or adsorption is installed in the treatment tank, the drainage flowed into the inlet of the storm drain flows through the flow path including the maintenance tank and the treatment tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "(6) the bottom of the storm receiver, maintenance tank and treatment tank is laminated with synthetic resin sheet, treatment media and porous sheet made of permeable material so that the road drainage remaining in the drainage system is allowed to penetrate into the soil with contaminants removed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "(7) the maintenance and treatment tanks can be installed in a block block made of concrete, or forcedly installed together with the storm water receiver"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200357071-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "(3) since the filter filling tank which removes contaminants contained in the drainage by filtration or adsorption is detachably installed in the treatment tank, while the drainage flowed from the inlet of the storm receiver flows through the treatment tank, contaminants contained in the waste water are removed by the filter medium"}, {"pat_id": "US-10865547-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the event of a truly significant rain (storm) event, these storage tanks can be overwhelmed, thus resulting in flooding or discharge of excess storm water to the sewage treatment system, a body of water, or a river"}, {"pat_id": "US-10865547-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in extraordinary storm events, these surge tanks can easily become overwhelmed, thus requiring the release of untreated water (sewage and stromwater) to a river, bay, etc., or even bypassing the stormwater collection tank(s) altogether"}, {"pat_id": "US-11603651-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the event of a truly significant rain (storm) event, these storage tanks can be overwhelmed, thus resulting in flooding or discharge of excess storm water to the sewage treatment system, a body of water, or a river"}, {"pat_id": "US-11603651-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in extraordinary storm events, these surge tanks can easily become overwhelmed, thus requiring the release of untreated water (sewage and stormwater) to a river, bay, etc., or even bypassing the stormwater collection tank(s) altogether"}, {"pat_id": "US-7022243-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the event of a heavy storm where there is a high flow of storm water, the separation tank 10 of the present invention also functions to convey the additional flow of water into a separate high flow treatment chamber so as to circumvent the second treatment chamber 36 thereby preventing any scour or resuspension of previously captured material from the second chamber and filter/recharge chamber"}]</data>
</edge>
