  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "EP-3655743-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "for instance, recent precipitation or flooding events may be responsible for the changes, which do not indicate the presence of a water network leak"}, {"pat_id": "US-9709431-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in this example, if the rain sensor indicates that there is no local precipitation, but that there are water levels above a threshold, the control system 100 may track property operations to determine if there is a problematic operation that may be causing water leakage within the property"}, {"pat_id": "US-9709431-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in this example, if the rain sensor indicates that there is excessive local precipitation, the calculated susceptibility of water damage may be increased based on determining that the likelihood of water leaking into the property is much higher"}]</data>
