  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "JP-6593422-B2", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "in the present invention, corrosion in a heat exchanger of a high heat load device can be suppressed while preventing problems such as precipitation of calcium carbonate due to slaked lime input and cost increase due to chemical input"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100449379-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "and converting the heavy metal into a corrosion precursor which is insoluble in water by a biological corrosion reaction, and sends it to the primary precipitation tank (5a) to precipitate and remove the solid material, and then to the primary treatment tank (13), and then to the primary precipitation tank (5a)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100449379-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "in the primary aeration tank (3a), when organic pollutants and heavy metals in the waste water are converted into corrosion precursors that are insoluble in water by biological corrosion reactions, they are sent to the primary precipitation tank (5a) to remove the corrosion precursors and microorganisms that exist in the solid state"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100625882-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "supercritical heat exchanger to recover in the supercritical water with little corrosion, and to install the quenching mixture to prevent corrosion and precipitation of inorganic substances in the cooling process of the treated water to secure the stability and continuous operation of the supercritical water oxidation process it was"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100625882-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in particular, it is difficult to prevent corrosion in some subcritical sections under aerobic formation formed near the reactor inlet of the waste liquid preheated to subcritical temperature in order to prevent the precipitation of inorganic materials, and to prevent the precipitation of inorganic materials during the discharge of treated water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100625882-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in addition, by improving the supercritical water oxidation process, which consumes a large amount of energy to prevent the precipitation of inorganic substances, supercritical heat exchanger and quenching mixer are installed to prevent corrosion of the treated water and precipitation of inorganic substances and to save energy"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100625882-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "2, the preheater 33 is a structure for preventing corrosion and precipitation of inorganic materials, and is closed to the preheater outer wall 118 and the outlet 116, and a portion adjacent to the inlet is in communication with the preheater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100625882-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "there is no formation of critical temperature zones, which can suppress corrosion, and the linear velocity several times faster than subcritical conditions greatly reduces the likelihood of precipitation of inorganic materials, and maintains the supercritical temperature from the inlet of the reactor to increase organic decomposition effects"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100625882-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "it is effective in preventing clogging caused by corrosion, and supercritical water oxidation process, which consumes a large amount of energy, is installed to prevent the precipitation of inorganic materials, and supercritical heat exchangers and quenching mixers are installed to prevent corrosion of the treated water and precipitation of inorganic materials"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101791441-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the aqueous solution of ascorbic acid is remarkably lower in corrosion occurrence than the sodium thiosulfate, and precipitation of aqueous ascorbic acid is in the form of powder, so that there is little phenomenon such as a pipe wall"}]</data>
