  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100605267-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at this time, the waste water passing through the bypass pipe 20 is treated water that does not pass only the filtration tank 17, and is discharged through precipitation in the apparatus, so that almost contaminants are removed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100784496-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the filtration tank 30 is provided with a filter 31 for filtering contaminants such as organic substances, oil components, and suspended solids in the rainfall that do not settle in the precipitation tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100967057-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "optionally, certain flocculants may be administered to increase the precipitation of contaminants in the settling basin"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101365215-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the photocatalytic oxidation tank 190 sterilizes, disinfects and removes contaminants through the photocatalytic reaction of uv-tio 2 from the treated water separated and discharged from the precipitation tanks 142 and 160"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101382006-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in detail, the purification treatment tank 10 removes the fine turbidity contaminants or soluble contaminants contained in the rainwater passing through the precipitation tank 20 and the precipitation tank 20 removing the floating contaminants and the suspended solids from the rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101580859-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "[ therefore, the gravity type precipitation in the pretreatment tank and the primary treatment water in which the sediment and the contaminants are removed by the trapping net 110 are flowed to the filtration treatment tank 20 through the primary treatment water inflow pipe 19"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101779726-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in which after-precipitation process of a batch reaction tank is combined with an inverse filter module for discharging only the filtrate filtered out in treated water while separating fine contaminant particles"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102268655-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a precipitation treatment unit 300 provided to receive the desorbed liquid separated from the screen dehydration unit 200 in a treatment tank 310 to separate sediment contaminants in a precipitation method"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102268655-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a precipitation treatment unit 300 provided to receive the desorbed liquid separated from the screen dehydration unit 200 in a treatment tank 310 to separate sediment contaminants in a precipitation method"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200431389-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the filtration tank 30 is provided with a filter 31 for filtering contaminants such as organic substances, oil components, and suspended solids in the rainfall that do not settle in the precipitation tank"}, {"pat_id": "US-4659463-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "another object of the present invention is to provide an aeration/precipitation tank assembly in the system for removing contaminants which sprays air laden water into an air column to further oxidize the contaminants contained in the water while maintaining the system water pressure"}]</data>
