  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100631373-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the anaerobic tank and the anaerobic tank, sludge is deposited due to the sediment in the introduced wastewater and the returned wastewater, that is, denitrification or precipitation of phosphorus-overtake microorganisms"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100659176-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "foreign matter functions to suppress clogging that may occur due to precipitation or deposition on the bottom of the stepped manhole 10 or the drain sewer 15"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101868534-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the electrolytic waste liquid and the precipitating accelerator are not mixed uniformly, and the undrawn salt from the supernatant of the precipitation tank can be removed from the electrodeposition / adsorption unit"}, {"pat_id": "US-10654738-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in processes for the precipitation of solids in a fluidized bed reaction chamber, despite the presence of the fluidized bed with its abrasive effect to reduce deposits forming on the reaction chamber in a wall, certain portions in the reaction chamber may not be optimally circulated, thus allowing the deposit of salts on the walls, for instance at the inlet of the reaction chamber"}]</data>
</edge>
