  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "JP-4357141-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "[0002] [prior art] when a pipeline damage occurs due to an earthquake, it is difficult to identify the damaged part"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4554634-B2", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "a control device that enables it, and in addition, when there is a crack or breakage in a gas supply pipeline due to an earthquake or disaster, a pipeline abnormality detection device that automatically shuts off the pipeline, etc"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5529803-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in particular, if water is drained when there is a lot of tap water consumption or when there is a water leak in the water pipeline due to an earthquake, etc., the water pressure in the water pipeline is likely to drop excessively"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7222143-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "2 is for guiding breakage when a load is applied to the pipeline 1 due to an earthquake or the like"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7222143-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "the earthquake-resistant structure 10 configured in this manner can prevent water leakage from the pipeline 1 when the pipeline 1 is damaged by an earthquake or the like"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7222143-B1", "para_id": "para_48", "text": "that is, when a large load is applied to the pipeline 1 due to an earthquake or the like, by guiding the guide groove 20 covered with the water stop body 31 to be damaged, leakage of water or groundwater into the pipeline 1 can be prevented"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100687800-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the case of water supply pipeline, it is manufactured to minimize the destruction of the water supply pipeline caused by sag or collapse of the ground due to external impact force such as earthquake by utilizing the elasticity to the maximum"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200367651-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the case of water supply pipeline, it is manufactured to minimize the destruction of the water supply pipeline caused by sag or collapse of the ground due to external impact force such as earthquake by utilizing the elasticity to the maximum"}, {"pat_id": "US-5708195-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in other words, the first conventional technique is premised on the existence of water leak and lacks the viewpoint that pipeline breakage should be sensed rapidly at the time of a disaster such as an earthquake"}, {"pat_id": "US-5708195-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "besides the time of occurrence of an earthquake, however, the determination of priority order of restoration locations may be also carried out when water leak (pipeline breakage) has been sensed in a plurality of locations"}]</data>
