  <data key="d5">["behavior", "content", "shape", "leakage", "apparatus", "property", "ablation", "point", "pipeline", "branch", "engine", "depth", "distance", "way", "masonry", "signal", "wall", "speed", "signature", "damage", "detection", "biofilm", "pipe", "formation", "construction", "work", "extent", "order", "limit", "variation", "loss", "measurement", "water", "art", "corrosion", "period", "treatment", "structure", "nature", "edge", "mass", "segment", "decay", "gas", "pressure", "operating", "event", "geometry", "supply", "user", "energy", "condition", "pit", "stationarity", "leak"]</data>
  <data key="d6">["learn", "determine", "be", "result", "advance", "carry", "consist", "perform", "affect", "remain", "mistake", "sample", "lead", "work", "examine", "change", "allow", "assess", "propagate", "connect", "perform up", "bury", "know", "generate", "assume"]</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100935006-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "due to the nature of the pipeline construction that the engine should be advanced at a high speed, the first work is performed up to the limit depth (about 2m) to allow the pit work to work without the masonry structure, and then the construction of the masonry structure and the second pit work are performed simultaneously"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102069616-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the leakage measurement of underground buried water supply pipelines is buried over a very long distance due to the nature of the pipeline, and also consists of small water supply pipelines connected to many branch points"}, {"pat_id": "US-10350653-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in order to learn more about the extent and nature of the damage, and therefore to determine an appropriate treatment, a user may sample the environmental conditions at various points along the pipeline by assessing properties that would be indicative of conditions suitable for biofilm formation"}, {"pat_id": "US-10352505-B2", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "15, small pipeline leaks often result in a subtle leading edge decay signatures (non-abrupt), therefore, ima examines nodal potential energy behavior over a brief period to determine loss of mass from the pipe segment"}, {"pat_id": "US-11033648-B2", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "in order to learn more about the extent and nature of the damage, and therefore to determine an appropriate treatment, a user may sample the environmental conditions at various points along the pipeline by assessing properties that would be indicative of conditions suitable for biofilm formation"}, {"pat_id": "US-11359989-B2", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "these transient pressure events propagate along the pipeline in the same way as a pressure event generated by a leak (e.g., potential leak signal) and may be mistaken by the pipeline leak detection apparatus as a leak events due to their transient nature"}, {"pat_id": "US-5416724-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "because the gas carrying pipeline, pressure and leak shape remain relatively constant, the nature of the leak signal does not change, and statistical stationarity can be assumed"}, {"pat_id": "US-7941282-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as known in the art, these variations among pipeline construction, geometry, contents, and nominal operating condition affect the extent and nature of corrosion and ablation of the pipeline walls"}]</data>
</edge>
