  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "JP-3459918-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the first conduit e1 or the second conduit e it is possible to guide rainwater and the like that have entered into the gutter block 1 through the drainage grooves 1d and 1d into the gutter block 1 without being blocked by the covering material w placed on the lid-hanging stepped portion 1b"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3459918-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "further, according to the gutter block provided with the drainage device described in claim 13 , in addition to the effect of claim 11 or 12 , rainwater and the like that have entered the first water conduit can be along the lower surface that is the inclined surface"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100696883-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, when the external force is applied to the sewage pipe or drainage pipe is to support the sewage pipe by the upper and lower fixed frame 20 will be able to prevent the deformation of the conduit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100786511-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "fine suspended matter having little specific gravity remaining after being precipitated in the contaminant treatment tank 13 is moved through the filter 20 installed in the upper part to the storm conduit 12 due to the continuous inflow of rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100959161-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at this time, the storm conduit 10 may be provided with a plurality of overflow wear (11, 12, 13), if necessary, the front side of each overflow wear (11) (12) (13) as a settlement 20 a gate is installed to allow initial rainwater to flow in"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101008372-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the blocking plate 120 is rotated upward by a hinge (not shown) by the water pressure of the mixed water which is mixed with the sewage and rainwater to the sewage pipe 11 while opening the discharge conduit 110 and opened at the same time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101133277-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "the height of the purification device 1 of the present invention is lower than the height of the inclined drain conduit 2, so that the contaminants are smoothly conveyed to the contaminant collecting part 40, and also due to the heavy rain, the flow rate of rainwater may be high"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101173254-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "by preventing the rainwater from flowing into the sewer conduit 20 by the rotation of the wear 40, it is possible to maintain a constant treatment capacity of the sewage treatment plant by adjusting the inflow amount into the sewage treatment plant, thereby maintaining excellent sewage treatment quality"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101196227-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a water purification filtration layer formed on the upper and lower trench conduits to remove contaminants in rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101196227-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a filtration step for purifying water to remove contaminants in rainwater formed on the upper and lower trench conduits"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101196227-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a water purification filtration layer (70) formed on the upper and lower trench conduits (50, 60) to remove contaminants in rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101196227-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a water purification filtration step formed on the inner surface of the upper and lower trench conduits 50 and 60 to remove contaminants in rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101196227-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at this time, the inner wall of the upper, lower trench conduits (50, 60) to form a water purification filtration layer 70 to prevent contamination of the rainwater is stored"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101305591-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, due to the wide diameter, it is easy for sediment to settle in conduits, and there is a high possibility that sewage from rainwater tosoil may leak into the body of water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101946554-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, at the time of rainfall, the stormwater flows through the stormwater conduit (40), and the initial stormwater is transferred to the climatic site (50) side, and the continuous stormwater flows into the river while overflowing the swimwear (41)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102053107-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a bad smell blocking member that prevents the coming offensive odor from dissipating to the outside of the grating, and discharges the rainwater that flows back to the outside of the grating when the rainwater rises in the conduit and the rainwater flows back from the conduit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102053107-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the rainwater flowing from the outside of the grating 10 flows along the inclined upper surface of each malodor blocking blade 122 and accumulates on the inclined lower upper surface of each malodor blocking blade 122, and each of the malodors when the rainwater accumulated on the inclined lower upper surface of the blocking blade 122 is accumulated by a predetermined amount or more, the respective odor blocking blades are formed such that the lower portion of each odor blocking blade 122 faces the conduit due to the weight of the rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102053107-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "if the rainwater rises in the conduit due to excessive rain, etc., and the rainwater flows back from the conduit, the rainwater flowing back from the conduit pushes up the inclined upper bottom surface of each odor blocking blade 122"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102399564-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the gate 20 not only collects an appropriate amount of sewage or rainwater by opening and closing the inlet, but also blocks the pressure from being transmitted into the collecting pipe due to the rise of the water level in the conduit during flooding to prevent damage to the collecting pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102399564-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when it rains, the shutter 30 blocks the exit of the conduit 10 to prevent the odor from spreading to the outside"}, {"pat_id": "US-11560697-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "such scenarios can occur when the sewer conduit has been blocked by detritus, and/or accumulation or buildup around the interior of the drainage pipes which can occur without regular maintenance and monitoring of the sewer drainage lines"}, {"pat_id": "US-6167916-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the rest of the large central sub-conduit 34 is typically provided for storm water drainage as may become necessary in the event of a flood or water overflow during a fire fighting event or burst water main"}]</data>
</edge>
