  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100786511-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "fine suspended matter having little specific gravity remaining after being precipitated in the contaminant treatment tank 13 is moved through the filter 20 installed in the upper part to the storm conduit 12 due to the continuous inflow of rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100959161-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at this time, the storm conduit 10 may be provided with a plurality of overflow wear (11, 12, 13), if necessary, the front side of each overflow wear (11) (12) (13) as a settlement 20 a gate is installed to allow initial rainwater to flow in"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101946554-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, at the time of rainfall, the stormwater flows through the stormwater conduit (40), and the initial stormwater is transferred to the climatic site (50) side, and the continuous stormwater flows into the river while overflowing the swimwear (41)"}, {"pat_id": "US-10927539-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "such sediments accumulate over time, often to the point of greatly impeding flow through such storm drain conduits so that subsequent storm runoff may be blocked to the point of backing up, leaving the storm drain conduits ineffective"}, {"pat_id": "US-10927539-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the costs for hauling clean water to storm drain conduit cleaning sites and for hauling away dirty water and the materials removed from the storm drain conduits are significant"}, {"pat_id": "US-10927539-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "such trucks can also present problems for traffic in the vicinity and can cause undesirable wear and tear on streets and highways where storm drain conduits are being cleaned"}, {"pat_id": "US-10927539-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "6 is a schematic illustration of the apparatus for use in cleaning accumulated sediments from a storm drain conduit and preparing the dirty water for further use"}]</data>
</edge>
<edge source="conduit" target="subsidence">
  <data key="d1">2</data>
  <data key="d2">due to</data>
  <data key="d3">["KR-100810555-B1", "KR-102014763-B1"]</data>
  <data key="d4">["due to"]</data>
  <data key="d5">["defect", "pipeline", "sewage", "fluctuation", "breakage", "separation", "pipe", "variation", "cracking", "earth", "connection", "ageing", "conduit", "pressure", "subsidence", "ground", "pvc", "aging", "disconnection"]</data>
  <data key="d6">["have", "mean"]</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100810555-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in general, underground pipelines, such as concrete pipes, pvc pipes, and conduits, have defects such as cracking, breakage, or separation of connections due to ageing of the pipe itself, subsidence of the underground ground, or variations in earth pressure from the ground"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102014763-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "here, structural defects in sewage conduits mean defects such as cracking, breakage, or disconnection due to aging of the pipe itself, subsidence of underground ground or fluctuations in earth pressure from the ground"}]</data>
</edge>
