nd urban flooding prevention according to the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101468324-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "10 (a), the third open / close board 40 of the present invention can be shut off passively, so that even when the rain is over in the event of an emergency, the river floods or exceeds the sewage treatment capacity of the sewage end treatment plant , it is possible to block a multiple of the initial storm stored in the reservoir"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101518865-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "by providing the guide block 66 on the upper side of the drainage passage 52, rainwater that suddenly overflows due to heavy rainfall or the like is prevented, so that flooding of the earths due to heavy rainfall can be stably prevented"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101841645-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the diameter of the water hole 311 formed in the block housing 30 is smaller than the diameter of the inlet hole 21 formed in the press plate 20, the number of the holes 311 is formed in the block housing 30 in a smaller number than the number of the inlet holes 21 formed in the press plate 20 so that the gap between the inlet holes 21 of the block housing 30 is discharged to the permeable hole (311) in a state of being filled with water, thereby preventing flooding or flooding due to abrupt discharge"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102306868-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "7 is a perspective view showing the configuration of a drainage module and a blocking module in the flood prevention system of the building structure of fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102306868-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "1 , the flooding diffusion prevention system may include a drain module 100 , a flood control module 200 , and a blocking module 300 so that water can be flushed and drained"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102569525-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "4 is a block diagram showing a control system of a drainage system for preventing road flooding according to the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102660526-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "therefore, when a flood is expected, the operation of the filtration device 300 is stopped in advance by the automatic control system 500, and the water supply pipe valve 312 of the water supply pipe 310 connected to the filtration device 300 is blocked"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "15, the drain trap structure of the underground flood prevention and water damage control equipment collects water in a part of the drainage device and allows water to pass freely, but blocks the circulation of air or gas"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "this relates to an underground passage flood prevention and control device configured to prevent and control flood damage by controlling flood damage inside the main body of the flood control device, thereby eliminating and eliminating the disaster by blocking off the source from the disaster area where the flood control process is configured"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102814353-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "meanwhile, if waste such as leaves flows into the drain, the drain with the above function loses its flood prevention function by blocking the flow and discharge of rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102822205-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "an experiment conducted by the national disaster and safety research institute found that when a rainwater drain is blocked by trash or covered with rubber sheets, the flooded area increases three times and the flood depth increases by more than 2.3 times"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200495876-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a sewer stink blocking device the present invention relates to a sewage odor blocking device, and more particularly, it is located under the manhole cover to block the bad smell of sewage, and a backflow permitting hole is provided on one side to selectively allow backflow in the event of a flood"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200495876-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "according to the present invention, it is located on the lower side of the manhole cover to block odors and at the same time provide a backflow permitting hole on one side to selectively allow backflow in case of a flood, thereby preventing damage to the manhole due to water pressure in advance"}, {"pat_id": "US-10640941-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "further, due to the opening of the flood discharge holes on the dam, floating objects in the flood may block the flood discharge holes, which in turn causes the flood to flow over the dam, causing greater environmental damage"}, {"pat_id": "US-11560697-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the drainage line becomes clogged or blocked with debris, ice, or as a result of build-up inside the pipe, a flooding event can occur in the building if adequate precautions are not taken"}, {"pat_id": "US-11560697-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "without proper maintenance, backwater valves can become blocked or stuck, giving building managers and homeowners a false sense of security that they will be protected during a flooding event"}, {"pat_id": "US-11560697-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however many homeowners and residents are not aware of the presence or operation of a backwater valve, and if the valve is closed due to a flooding event or blockage many residents will not be aware of it until sanitary sewage begins flowing back into their building"}, {"pat_id": "US-11560697-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "this causes a flood condition, where blockage of the drainage from the building causes pressure buildup between the municipal sewer and the building, putting the building at risk of a backwater flood"}, {"pat_id": "US-4797028-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "various methods have been used in an attempt to prevent beavers from blocking the inlet of flood control risers in water reservoirs and the like"}]</data>
