  <data key="d6">["include", "instal", "transfer", "reduce", "call", "attach", "pass", "have", "be", "result", "remove", "suspend", "flow out", "consider", "contain", "precipitate", "flow", "filter", "perform", "sediment", "provide", "treat", "discharge", "combine", "say", "collect", "sink", "store", "float", "cause", "operate", "deposit", "introduce", "accumulate", "settle", "re", "confirm", "adsorb", "leak"]</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100516951-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "therefore, in the present invention, the removal of contaminants is actively performed for the building drainage during the initial rainfall stage with a high content of contaminants, and some of the contaminants are considered in consideration of the low content of contaminants for the subsequent building drainage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100546061-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "also, in sewage or polluted small streams, contaminants are deposited on the bottom in sinking areas, lowlands, and bore areas, and when the flow rate increases during rainfall, the sewage power increases, causing the sediment to float and outflow"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100584236-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "however, even with this method, it is difficult to completely remove the harmful contaminants that are strongly attached to the catchment surface by hydrophobic interaction, and the accumulated contaminants are gradually introduced into the storage tank over a long period of time during rainfall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100614766-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "therefore, in the present invention, the removal of contaminants is actively performed on the road drainage during the initial rainfall stage in which the content of the pollutants is high, and the filter filling tank 71 considering the low amount of pollutants in the subsequent road drainage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100750645-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "these storm receivers store the road drainage during rainfall and transfer it to the filtration apparatus to adsorb and remove contaminants contained in the road drainage, and then discharge only the treated water to the sewer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100750645-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the amount of contaminants in the road surface drainage due to the subsequent rainfall is small, and it can be said that there is little problem even if the excess water is discharged immediately without passing through the filtration tank 54"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100784496-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the filtration tank 30 is provided with a filter 31 for filtering contaminants such as organic substances, oil components, and suspended solids in the rainfall that do not settle in the precipitation tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100784496-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the contaminants having their own weight among the contaminants included in the initial rainfall introduced into the first settling tank 10 are primarily precipitated at the bottom of the first settling tank 10 and do not settle in the first settling tank 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100784496-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "meanwhile, contaminants having their own weight among the pollutants included in the rainfall flowing into the second settling tank 20 are second precipitated to the bottom of the second settling tank 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101024670-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "this is called cso (combined sewer overflow), and due to the initial rainfall, the pollutants on the surface and the contaminants settled in the combined sewage pipe are simultaneously leaked, resulting in a high concentration and load of the pollutants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101067633-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "this is called cso (combined sewer overflow), and due to the initial rainfall, the pollutants on the surface and the contaminants settled in the consolidation sewers flow out at the same time, resulting in a very high concentration and load of the pollutants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101095323-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "this is called cso (combined sewer overflow), and due to the initial rainfall, the pollutants on the surface and the contaminants settled in the consolidation sewers flow out at the same time, resulting in a very high concentration and load of the pollutants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101959509-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, the non-contact sensor 146 is installed in the waterproof and dustproof spring cylinder 142 to operate as a switch, and the increase in weight of the filtration part 120 of the rainfall effluent contaminant filtering device 100 can be confirmed at the lowest standby power state have"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "then, after the rainfall flows into the storm receiver 20, it is re-introduced into the maintenance tank 30, the treatment tank 40 is to properly remove the contaminants in the treatment tank 40"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the present invention actively removes contaminants from the road drainage during the initial rainfall stage with a large amount of pollutants, and considers that the content of the pollutants in the subsequent road drainage is low"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200357071-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the present invention actively removes contaminants from the road drainage during the initial rainfall stage with a high content of contaminants, and considers that the content of the contaminants is low in the subsequent road drainage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200358330-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the present invention actively removes contaminants from road surface drainage during the initial rainfall stage with high content of contaminants, and the contaminant content is less for road drainage than the treatment capacity in the subsequent treatment tank 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200371407-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, such a continuous deflective separation (cds) device has to be sedimented at the bottom of the collection tank and sewage of the collected contaminants to artificially after the rainfall, which will reduce the efficiency due to the overload of the device due to overdeposition of contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200431389-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the filtration tank 30 is provided with a filter 31 for filtering contaminants such as organic substances, oil components, and suspended solids in the rainfall that do not settle in the precipitation tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200431389-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the contaminants having their own weight among the contaminants included in the initial rainfall introduced into the first settling tank 10 are primarily precipitated at the bottom of the first settling tank 10 and do not settle in the first settling tank 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200431389-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "meanwhile, contaminants having their own weight among the pollutants included in the rainfall flowing into the second settling tank 20 are second precipitated to the bottom of the second settling tank 20"}]</data>
