  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100598365-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "this is because large water tanks, which are largely divided from large ones, are more likely to leak due to hydraulic pressure in the case of minor gaps and ground subsidence"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102664616-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, as the ground subsides or sags occur at the joints of the concrete hume pipes due to their own weight, the filled concrete mortar breaks, and sewage leaks between them, causing soil contamination, ground subsidence, and sinkholes, as well as various other problems"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200362691-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "or due to ground subsidence of any one culvert unit when the (100) falls outwards, a gap is formed in the connection part, and the sealing force by the sealing ring (4) is dropped, so that the waste water from the outside is soaked into the culvert through the gap, or the waste water from the culvert is leaked to the outside"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200436180-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the present invention was devised to solve the above problems, and even if the water well or the pipe is distorted due to ground subsidence and external impact, the watertight coupling state is maintained to completely prevent the occurrence of leakage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200436228-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in particular, if the ground subsidence occurs due to some soft ground in the lower part of the channel, the pipeline leakage phenomenon becomes more serious"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200436228-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in particular, even in soft ground where ground subsidence occurs, the connection part of the front and rear body parts is stably maintained, thereby effectively preventing the pipeline leakage phenomenon"}]</data>
