oir"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101485001-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a stormwater receiver (100) a permeable sidewalk block (200) constituting the sidewalk and configured to allow the storm to penetrate into the bedrock"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101485001-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, the rainwater infiltrated through the permeable press block flows directly into the reservoir 500 through the induction pipe installed under the permeable press block, and the road effluent flowing through the rainwater receiver on the road passes through the filtration tank and then flows into the storage tank 500 after the initial storm has been processed through the storage tank 300"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101859056-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "therefore, the storage tank structure for stormwater infiltration and storage according to the present invention can ensure sufficient durability against repetitive vehicle shafts since the storage unit blocks have sufficient strength"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102408952-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, it is possible to block the supply of river water or seawater backflowing to the stormwater chamber 110 to the sewage treatment plant"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200148426-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "due to this, various flies and mosquitoes inhabited in the sewer pipe are blocked by the blocking plates 6 installed on the outer wall surfaces of the waste collection container 4 of the storm drainage tank 1 for roads, thereby preventing passage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "(7) the maintenance and treatment tanks can be installed in a block block made of concrete, or forcedly installed together with the storm water receiver"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200414927-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "1-a is a top plan view of several storm reservoir block slabs and is stacked (1) where the multiple storm reservoir block slabs meet to become one"}, {"pat_id": "US-10927539-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "such sediments ac