  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100499612-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "third, the contaminants or solids in the treatment facility in the overflow water treatment facility of the combined sewer pipe or storm pipe by not capturing and storing, it is easy to maintain the maintenance of the overflow water treatment facility and reduce the maintenance cost"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100516951-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in addition, between the second compartment member 400 and the storm water receiving tank 100 is further provided with a contaminant filtration adsorption means 700 filled with a filter medium to remove the contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100614766-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the contaminants are adsorbed in the precipitated sand or mud, and as a result, the precipitates absorbing the contaminants are formed in the mud state at the bottom and the vicinity of the storm receiver 10 and the discharge box 91"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100614766-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "(3) since the filter filling tank which removes contaminants contained in the drainage by filtration or adsorption is detachably installed in the treatment tank, while the drainage flowed from the inlet of the storm receiver flows through the treatment tank, contaminants contained in the waste water are removed by the filter medium"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100673536-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "on the other hand, since the holes 22 of the storm duct 20 are formed to be below the normal water level of the second accommodation chamber 11b, relocation of the contaminants suspended through the holes 22 and their backflow is prevented"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100750645-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the present invention relates to a multifunctional storm receiver that can reliably filter oily contaminants and prevent odors in the confluence area"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100750645-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "these storm receivers store the road drainage during rainfall and transfer it to the filtration apparatus to adsorb and remove contaminants contained in the road drainage, and then discharge only the treated water to the sewer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100786511-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "fine suspended matter having little specific gravity remaining after being precipitated in the contaminant treatment tank 13 is moved through the filter 20 installed in the upper part to the storm conduit 12 due to the continuous inflow of rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100795399-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the stormwater manager regularly checks the slope screen bar (4) and sand sedimentation chamber (5) of the stormwater chamber and periodically removes contaminants and sand by manpower"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101154026-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "to prevent or prevent flooding and flooding of roads and houses, and to treat sewage by storm control facilities after rain, and to utilize the sidewalls of the stormwater to collect contaminants contained in rainwater and to vent rainwater reservoirs"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101250076-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the road surface storm water treatment tank 123a is provided with an inflow chamber 123a3, a processing chamber 123a4, and an outflow chamber 123a5, and the inflow chamber 123a3 has a contaminant receiver 123b and a processing chamber ( 123a4) is provided with pollutant filtration / adsorption means 123c, respectively"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101280771-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the storm flows into the inlet chamber 123a3 and the contaminants are removed by the obstacle receiver 123b during the passage through the inlet chamber 123a3"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101323288-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "is not only to filter out pollutants introduced with rainwater to the storm pipe (5) side as well , removes low-density floating contaminants and sends them down to the reservoir penetrating portion (10c) side of the lower portion, the reservoir penetrating portion (10c) to send rainwater introduced from the infiltration vegetation portion (10b)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101391172-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and a filtration tank for removing fine contaminants in the initial storm that have passed through the swirl screen and discharging the initial storm in the state where fine contaminants have been removed through the discharge pipe to the outside"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101653780-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the sludge hopper 230 allows the sludge contained in the storm to flow into the backwash drainage storage tank 310 so that the contaminants separated from the backwashing means 220 due to the backwashing process, to the backwash drainage storage tank 310 side by a predetermined angle"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101653780-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the filtration tank 210 is also provided with a filter means 220 for purifying the effluent from which solids contained in the storm and fine contaminants are removed from the stormwater inflow pipe 140 of the storage tank 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101741449-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the inlet tank 100 is formed with a screen box 120 to remove contaminants from the storm water discharged from the inlet pipe 110 and is formed at a lower side of the screen box 120, the desulphurization tool 130 is formed to have a flow regulating function"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101822469-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in such a configuration, since the impurities deposited at the time of detaching the initial stormwater treatment apparatus from the drainage port 100 are separated from the drainage port 100 together with the initial stormwater treatment apparatus while being stored in the impregnation sedimentation section 900, it is possible to prevent the contaminants from flowing into the drain port 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101865757-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, the conventional water treatment apparatuses such as storage tanks have a problem of non-environmental problems because the filtration efficiency of contaminants contained in rainwater such as early storms is low"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101926744-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the pollutant screening net 20 removes contaminants contained in the storm water flowing into the excellent stormwater chamber 11 from the outside and guides the contaminants to the contaminant discharge chamber 12 through the stormwater collecting chamber 11, a space is formed between the water collecting chamber 11 and the upper portion of the pollutant discharge chamber 12 and between the second partition 12a and the pollutant discharge chamber 12"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as a result, deposits absorbing contaminants are deposited in the mud at the bottom of the storm receiver 20, the maintenance tank 30, and the treatment tank 40"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "then, after the rainfall flows into the storm receiver 20, it is re-introduced into the maintenance tank 30, the treatment tank 40 is to properly remove the contaminants in the treatment tank 40"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "on the other hand, if the removal process of the contaminants continues, the bottom of the storm receiver 20, the maintenance tank 30 and the treatment tank 40, deposits containing contaminants are deposited, and the filter medium filling tank ( 70) contaminants will also collect inside, and regular removal will be required"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "(2) since the filter which removes contaminants contained in the drainage by filtration or adsorption is installed in the treatment tank, the drainage flowed into the inlet of the storm drain flows through the flow path including the maintenance tank and the treatment tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "(6) the bottom of the storm receiver, maintenance tank and treatment tank is laminated with synthetic resin sheet, treatment media and porous sheet made of permeable material so that the road drainage remaining in the drainage system is allowed to penetrate into the soil with contaminants removed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200357071-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the contaminants are adsorbed in the precipitated sand or mud, and as a result, the precipitates absorbing the contaminants are formed in the mud state at the bottom and the vicinity of the storm receiver 10 and the discharge box 91"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200357071-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "(3) since the filter filling tank which removes contaminants contained in the drainage by filtration or adsorption is detachably installed in the treatment tank, while the drainage flowed from the inlet of the storm receiver flows through the treatment tank, contaminants contained in the waste water are removed by the filter medium"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200361427-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "on the other hand, since the holes 22 of the storm duct 20 are formed to be below the normal water level of the second accommodation chamber 11b, relocation of the contaminants suspended through the holes 22 and their backflow is prevented"}, {"pat_id": "US-7208082-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "for example, a number of rock bags may be positioned around a storm drain in order to filter drainage water from the construction site, and prevent other construction contaminants from entering the storm drain, thereby reducing water pollution and protecting water quality"}]</data>
