  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101484891-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "preferably, in the present invention, the capacity of the reservoir 200 is reduced to 8 to 24 hours until the initial boiling point contamination reaches the height of the stormwater supply line 120, which is the maximum level of the reservoir 200"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101778786-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, it is possible to prevent the initial storm having a high contamination degree from being supplied to the sedimentation tank guide pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101879690-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the stormwater inflow pipe 11 is arranged on the ceiling portion above the discharge chamber 14 of the collecting tank 10 and the discharge pipe 12 is arranged on the bottom portion of the discharge chamber 14 therefore, the stormwater flowing through the storm inflow pipe 11 is quickly discharged through the discharge pipe 12 when the initial storm water is excluded, and the initial stormwater with high contamination degree is discharged to the buoyancy chamber 15 )"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101946554-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, in the case of the initial stormwater treatment system according to the present invention, the initial stormwater is introduced into the secondary granulator 60 through the gypsum basin 50 and purified at the sewage treatment plant, thereby preventing the contamination of the river as much as possible, do"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101946554-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "according to the early stormwater treatment system according to the prior art, the initial stormwater having a high pollution level is discharged to the secondary tank through the gypsum, and when the amount of stormwater is increased, it is possible to prevent contamination of streams by flowing"}, {"pat_id": "US-5322629-A", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "this removal efficiency was reduced in part by relatively poor removals in some of the earlier storms due to drain rock and construction contamination"}, {"pat_id": "US-8961793-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "further, storm drains often are designed to not enter conventional wastewater treatment plants and directly enter open streams or the oceans, resulting in widespread outbreaks of disease, heavy metals contamination, and suspended solids, which adversely affect wildlife and human beings"}]</data>
