  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100531027-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, when the rainfall and the level of rainwater and sewage in the sump tank 150 increases, the water level in the guide groove 141 is also increased to raise the lifting height of the buoyancy member 122"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100531031-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, when the rainfall and the level of rainwater and sewage in the sump tank 150 increases, the water level in the guide groove 141 is also increased to raise the lifting height of the buoyancy member 122"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100841664-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and controlling the water level of the sump by identifying the state of the wastewater, controlling the ph, electrical conductivity and flow rate of the reservoir, and controlling the electrolysis by being connected to the level of the electrolytic cell and the positive and negative plates"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101054375-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "and it is characterized by including a control unit to determine the state of the wastewater to control the water level of the sump, the ph and electrical conductivity and the flow rate of the reservoir, and connected to the level of the electrolytic cell and the positive and negative plates to control the electrolysis"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101171869-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, when the pumping of the stream water 2 collected in the sump 120 continues while the collection efficiency of the screen 110 is lowered due to the blockage of the lower bed 4, the water level in the sump 120 is increased"}, {"pat_id": "US-7802587-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "thus, if float valve 10 were not in place, basement 61 could easily flood as the water level in sump pit 50 rises above sump pit lid 52"}, {"pat_id": "US-7802587-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "float 11 lifts due to a rising water level in sump pit 50, thus causing float arm 14 to disengage rollers 16, 16 as it rotates"}, {"pat_id": "US-9709431-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "for example, the application server 170 may receive information from neighboring properties that indicate that both sump pumps are turned on but the water level is high, which may indicate that major water leak may be impacting both properties"}, {"pat_id": "US-9709431-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the monitoring system control unit 110 may receive a transmission identifying the pipe burst from the application server 170 and in response, may increase the susceptibility of water damage calculated from the water level and the operation of the sump pump 140"}]</data>
</edge>
